{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188958": {
      "title": "Research Associate CDB/AFCRI (CS)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine Centers and Institutes: Abramson Family Cancer Research Institute Location: Philadelphia, PA The Abramson Family Cancer Research Institute in collaboration with the Department of Cell and Developmental Biology at the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of mouse models of disease, metabolism, cancer biology, biochemistry, and computational approaches. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include investigation of Urea Cycle Disorders, obesity, and liver cancer. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to contribute to the development of potential new treatments for obesity and dietary interventions of Urea Cycle Disorders while further developing critical thinking skills, gaining expertise in relevant literature and experimental techniques, preparing manuscripts and extramural funding proposals, presenting research at international meetings, mentoring junior scientists, and participating in University-sponsored career development workshops. Candidate should have a minimum of 3-5 years postdoctoral experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187117": {
      "title": "Director of the Center of Excellence in Environmental Toxicology, Standing Faculty",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine Centers and Institutes: Center for Excellence in Environmental Toxicology Location: Philadelphia The Perelman School of Medicine (PSOM) at the University of Pennsylvania invites applications and nominations for the position of Director of the Center of Excellence in Environmental Toxicology (CEET). This is a national search for an accomplished and visionary leader to guide CEET into its next phase of scientific innovation, impact, and growth. The Center of Excellence in Environmental Toxicology is a nationally recognized, NIEHS-funded Environmental Health Sciences Core Center dedicated to elucidating how environmental exposures affect human health and disease and translating discoveries into improved health outcomes. CEET brings together a diverse group of basic, clinical, and population scientists across Penn and its partner institutions, with strong commitments to community engagement, team science, and workforce development. The Director will provide scientific, strategic, and administrative leadership for CEET, shaping the Center’s vision and ensuring continued excellence in research, training, and community engagement. The Director will serve as the primary representative of CEET within the Perelman School of Medicine and the larger University of Pennsylvania community as well as regional and national communities. The Director will be expected to: ·         Articulate and advance a compelling scientific and strategic vision for CEET ·         Lead and integrate multidisciplinary research programs in environmental health sciences ·         Oversee CEET cores, programs, and governance structures ·         Maintain and strengthen NIEHS Environmental Health Sciences Core Center funding ·         Foster mentoring, training, and career development for early-stage investigators and trainees ·         Promote meaningful community engagement and translation of environmental health research ·         Serve as an advocate for environmental health sciences across the University and beyond Candidates for the position must hold a PhD and/or MD degree and qualify for an appointment at the Associate or Full Professor level in the Standing Faculty of the PSOM at the University of Pennsylvani a. The faculty appointment will be in a department within the School of Medicine that aligns with the successful candidate’s scientific expertise. Candidates should have a strong record of leadership as well as an established, externally funded research program in environmental health sciences or a closely related field. The impact of the research program will be carefully reviewed. Preferred qualifications include: ·         Experience leading large, multidisciplinary or center-level initiatives ·         Prior involvement with NIEHS-funded programs or environmental health core centers ·         Demonstrated commitment to health equity and community-engaged research Applications are due July 23, 2026.  Interested candidates should submit a cover letter describing leadership experience and vision for CEET, a curriculum vitae and a brief statement of research to the attention of Garret A. FitzGerald, MD via this posting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185447": {
      "title": "Endowed Associate/Full Professor of Special Education",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Graduate School of Education Location: Philadelphia, PA Located in urban Philadelphia, Penn GSE is dedicated to preparing equity-oriented educators, leaders, and scholar-practitioners who advance opportunity for all students. We are seeking a colleague to strengthen this mission through rigorous research in special education, with a focus on teacher preparation and development. In particular, Penn GSE seeks a scholar whose research advances knowledge in the field while also informing the preparation and development of educators and leaders. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: teacher preparation for special and inclusive education; neurodivergent learners and learning differences, including autism, ADHD, and executive functioning; literacy and language development for students with reading disabilities and language-based learning differences; high-incidence disabilities such as learning disabilities, emotional and behavioral challenges, and speech-language impairments; and interventions such as multi-tiered systems of support and Universal Design for Learning. We are looking for a colleague who considers intersections between learning and mental health and wellbeing, as well as the ways that systems and structures are implicated in both how disabilities are identified and potential interventions. We welcome candidates representing diverse disciplinary perspectives and methodological approaches. Depending on the candidate's expertise and interest, opportunities exist to collaborate across Penn GSE's divisions and centers, including with faculty working in educational policy, school leadership, literacy, and instructional design. This endowed position, made possible through the generous support of the Usdan Family, represents a significant institutional investment in special education research and practice. The successful candidate will have an earned doctorate and an outstanding record of research, funding productivity, and teaching expertise, commensurate with experience level, with a focus on special education and its intersections with equity and inclusive practice. The ideal candidate will have demonstrated success working in partnership with K-12 schools and districts to improve outcomes for students with disabilities, their educators, and their communities. The successful candidate will provide intellectual leadership within GSE's educator preparation programs and contribute to building sustained partnerships with the School District of Philadelphia and other high-need urban districts. Please submit a CV, cover letter, research statement, a statement of teaching philosophy, the names of three references, and at least three writing samples or publications through Interfolio . Please submit your application by September 15, 2026. The search committee will continue reviewing applications until the position is filled. You can contact the Office of Research and Faculty Affairs with questions at facultyaffairs@gse.upenn.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174790": {
      "title": "Research Associate-ITMAT",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine Centers and Institutes: Institute for Translational Medicine and Therapeutics (ITMAT) Location: Philadelphia, PA The Institute for Translational Medicine and Therapeutics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of circadian biology, and cardiovascular physiology and pathology. The research associate should have skills in laboratory techniques relating to cell culture, molecular biology, mouse models, and rodent cardiac surgery. For the clinical portion of the work, strong experience in clinical translational research, advanced statistical analytics, omics analyses, wearable device application and data analysis, and statistical programming languages is required. Applicants must have an Ph.D. and/or M.D. degree. Responsibilities may include the design and execution of wet lab and animal model experiments in addition to clinical studies and database or biobank research, studying the role molecular clocks play in cardiovascular disease and the effects circadian disruption has on health and patient outcomes. The research associate is also expected to support the lab’s work on prostanoid biology. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to support translational studies relating to circadian biology, human circadian and diurnal rhythms, and cardiovascular physiology and disease. PhD and/or MD required. The research associate should have skills in laboratory techniques relating to cell culture, molecular biology, mouse models, and rodent cardiac surgery. For the clinical portion of the work, strong experience in clinical translational research, advanced statistical analytics, omics analyses, wearable device application and data analysis, and statistical programming languages is required. A degree in medicine or a strong understanding of human physiology and disease is desired."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177884": {
      "title": "Moon Family Postdoctoral Fellowship, 2026-27",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: School of Arts and Sciences: School of Arts and Sciences Centers and Institutes: Kim Center for Korean Studies Location: Philadelphia, PA The James Joo-Jin Kim Center for Korean Studies at the University of Pennsylvania announces a Moon Family Postdoctoral Fellowship for the 2026–27 academic year. The postdoctoral fellowship is open to scholars from any discipline with a research and teaching focus on Korea. The fellowship is the 12-month period between August 1, 2026 and July 31, 2027 and carries a minimum stipend of $67,000 as well as conference travel funds up to $2,000. The postdoctoral fellow will also receive a shared office space and access to libraries and other resources at Penn. The fellowship may be renewed for a second year, based on satisfactory performance, the existence of funding, and programmatic need. The fellow will be required to: 1) reside in the Philadelphia area; 2) teach one Korea-related course per year; 3) give a public presentation for the Korean Studies Colloquium; 4) mentor the Kim Center graduate and undergraduate fellows; 5) participate in the Kim Center events and related activities at Penn; and 6) organize a Korean Studies Conference (either in Fall 2026 or in Spring 2027). Eligibility The applicant who is awarded the fellowship must complete all requirements for the Ph.D. degree (dissertation deposited) by July 31, 2026. Application Requirements ● Cover Letter (including a description of research projects to be carried out during the fellowship, and teaching interests/experiences) ● CV ● Writing Sample (a published/publishable article or a dissertation chapter) ● One Korea-related course syllabus ● Two Letters of Recommendation (uploaded to the Interfolio directly by the recommenders) Applications will be accepted only via Interfolio here : The application must be submitted by 5 p.m. EST on Feb. 17, 2026. Award decisions will be made by early April 2026. The School of Arts and Sciences at the University of Pennsylvania is committed to cultivating a vibrant community of students, scholars, researchers, and staff and to upholding the highest standards of academic excellence.   The School and the Center for Korean Studies strive to create working and learning environments that foster intellectual growth and encourage meaningful connections within our Penn academic community and beyond. Questions can be directed to: Seok Lee, Associate Director of Academics Email: seok2@sas.upenn.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194895": {
      "title": "Full-time Lecturer/Senior Lecturer and Faculty Director, International Studies",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: School of Arts and Sciences: School of Arts and Sciences Centers and Institutes: Lauder Institute-Management and International Studies Location: Philadelphia, PA The Lauder Institute and the School of Arts and Sciences (SAS) at the University of Pennsylvania invite applications for a full-time appointment as a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer and Faculty Director, International Studies. This position combines graduate-level teaching with year-round academic leadership and administrative responsibilities for the core curriculum of the Masters of Arts (MA) degree in international studies. The Lauder Institute offers a distinctive model of graduate education that combines the analytical rigor of the School of Arts and Sciences with advanced language training, deep cultural and regional expertise, and their application to complex global business challenges; students receive a joint MBA-MA in two years. Lauder students develop the ability to analyze international markets, political and economic developments, and cross-cultural environments through interdisciplinary coursework that bridges the social sciences, humanities, and international business alongside language training. A hallmark of the program is its regional immersion model, which provides students with opportunities for intensive international travel experiences that connect classroom learning with direct engagement with business leaders, policymakers, alumni, and local communities around the world. The Faculty Director will join the senior leadership team at the Institute and teach international studies (INTS) courses that bring the analytical rigor of the School of Arts and Sciences to contemporary global business questions through interdisciplinary perspectives such as comparative politics, political economy, economic history, and regional studies. The successful candidate will be an intellectually engaged scholar and educator whose research and teaching illuminate the intersection of global business, politics, economics, culture, and society. In addition to teaching, the Faculty Director will serve as the principal academic and administrative leader of the international studies core curriculum, overseeing its development, delivery, assessment, and continuous improvement. Working closely with Institute leadership and faculty, the Faculty Director will ensure coherence across coursework, regional programming, experiential learning opportunities, and the master's thesis, while helping to develop curricular innovations that reflect Lauder's distinctive integration of language training, cultural fluency, and business education. Appointment as a full-time Lecturer is for a period of one year with possibility of renewal for up to two additional years contingent on satisfactory performance review and Dean’s approval, and a fourth year, pending Provost’s approval.  Consideration for appointment as a Senior Lecturer requires four years of service as a full-time Lecturer at Penn or current status as a Penn Senior Lecturer, as well as the standard processes and approvals for appointment in a receptive home department within the School of Arts and Sciences.  Appointment as Senior Lecturer is for a four-year term, with renewal contingent upon satisfactory performance reviews and University approval. The position combines an MA teaching load based on the teaching needs of the Institute with year-round academic leadership and administrative responsibilities for the Institute's international studies curriculum and programming. The salary is competitive. Minimum qualifications include: (1) a doctorate in a relevant field such as international affairs, area studies, business, economics, political science, public policy, or a related discipline; (2) international, regional, and linguistic expertise that contributes to the Institute's mission of developing global business leaders; (3) demonstrated excellence in graduate-level teaching; (4) the ability to work collaboratively and effectively with a wide range of stakeholders; and (5) willingness and availability to travel internationally for Lauder immersive student experiences potentially during academic year and summer for periods of 2 to 6 weeks at a time. Additional desirable qualifications include: (1) experience organizing, administering, and leading international programs, including experiential and immersion-based learning opportunities; (2) interest and experience in managing complex academic initiatives and curricula; (3) an active research agenda that engages global business questions through the analytical frameworks of the social sciences and humanities, with quantitative research methodologies preferred; and (4) ability to engage effectively with students, faculty, alumni, corporate partners, government officials, and other external stakeholders. (5) Candidates whose scholarship, teaching, or professional experience focuses on the Middle East are particularly encouraged to apply. Candidates are to apply at apply.interfolio.com/194895 . Include (1) a cover letter, (2) CV, (3) two sample course syllabi and teaching evaluations from the previous three years, (4) a brief statement (maximum 2,000 words) describing your approach to interdisciplinary teaching and curricular leadership at the intersection of international studies and global business, and (5) names and contact information for three individuals who have agreed to provide a letter of recommendation. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/141297": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in East and Southeast Asia Regional History",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: School of Arts and Sciences: School of Arts and Sciences Centers and Institutes: Lauder Institute-Management and International Studies Location: Philadelphia, PA The Lauder Institute of Management and International Studies, in conjunction with the School of Arts and Sciences, at the University of Pennsylvania invites applications for a part-time lecturer for a Summer 2024 intensive course in East & Southeast Asia Regional History.  The course is fully in-person, running from June 3-June 18, with ten 3-hour sessions. The successful candidate will have a PhD in History or a related field.  Doctoral candidates with strong teaching records may also be considered.  Local candidates are encouraged to apply as transportation costs are not covered by the university. Applicants will need to submit the following materials to: apply.interfolio.com/141297 Cover letter Curriculum vitae Contact information for three references (Note: We will not consult them without interviewing first and requesting permission in advance.) The Lauder program is highly team-oriented, valuing interdisciplinary scholarship, collaboration, and collegiality. We are committed to promoting a culturally diverse intellectual community that strongly encourages applications from women, minorities, and under-represented communities. Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until the position is filled. We seek candidates who share our strong commitment to research, teaching and mentoring, and to a scholarly community shaped by values of inclusive excellence.  The School of Arts and Sciences at the University of Pennsylvania is committed to cultivating and sustaining a community of students, scholars, researchers, and staff that reflects the diversity of our world. We nurture working and learning environments that are affirming, equitable, and inclusive. As a community, we are committed to thoughtful discussions and dynamic interactions as we strive for an environment where everyone is supported and valued. Please see our School’s Inclusion and Antiracism Initiatives to learn more about our active priorities: https://www.sas.upenn.edu/2020-inclusion-and-anti-racism-initiatives ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190020": {
      "title": "2027 Assistant Professor of Law",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Penn Carey Law Location: University of Pennsylvania Carey Law School The University of Pennsylvania Carey Law School seeks to fill tenure-track positions in various fields with a start date of July 1, 2027. Applicants should have an excellent academic record, high-quality publications, and/or exceptional experience of a scholarly nature in nationally recognized law reform work, government service, or cutting-edge legal practice. To apply, please submit a C.V., cover letter, and research agenda via Interfolio. If you have any questions, please contact Karen Crater, Assistant Director of Faculty Affairs, at kcrater@law.upenn.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176836": {
      "title": "Abdominal Imaging - Academic Clinician - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. The ideal candidate should be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with sub-specialty training in an ACGME-approved abdominal imaging fellowship program. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision and teaching of residents and fellows during readouts and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties. Medical student education will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. In addition, the candidate will be responsible for preparing learning materials and lectures, teaching posters, and presentations for national review. Clinical responsibilities may include the interpretation of Computed Tomography, Magnetic Resonance Imaging, Ultrasound, and Fluoroscopy of the body. Prior experience in image-guided biopsy is highly desirable but not required. The successful candidate will also participate in the Abdominal Imaging off-hour on-call program, including evenings, nights, and weekend coverage. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center (PAVMC), as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176838": {
      "title": "Abdominal Imaging - Academic Clinician – Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. The ideal candidate should be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with sub-specialty training in an ACGME-approved abdominal imaging fellowship program. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision and teaching of residents and fellows during readouts and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical sub-specialties. Medical student education will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. In addition, the candidate will be responsible for preparing learning materials and lectures, teaching posters, and presentations for national review. The successful candidate will be an accomplished educator and will be expected to serve in an educational leadership role within the Abdominal Imaging Division. Clinical responsibilities may include the interpretation of Computed Tomography, Magnetic Resonance Imaging, Ultrasound, and Fluoroscopy of the body. Prior experience in image-guided biopsy is highly desirable but not required. The successful candidate will also participate in the Abdominal Imaging off-hour on-call program, including evenings, nights, and weekend coverage. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center (PAVMC), as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176850": {
      "title": "Abdominal Imaging - Instructor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. The ideal candidate should be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with sub-specialty training in an ACGME-approved abdominal imaging fellowship program. Responsibilities may include the interpretation of Computed Tomography, Magnetic Resonance Imaging, Ultrasound, and Fluoroscopy of the body. Prior experience in image-guided biopsy is highly desirable but not required. The successful candidate will also participate in the Abdominal Imaging off-hour on-call program, including evenings, nights, and weekend coverage. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop research credentials. Instructors are provided with research and educational support to prepare them for an academic and/or clinical career. A specialized research focus may be developed in consultation with the Division Chief. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center (PAVMC), as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175862": {
      "title": "AC Faculty Position in Non-Malignant Hematology - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of sickle cell disease and disorders of hemostasis and thrombosis. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certification or eligibility in Hematology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, and fellows as well as advanced practice providers, pharmacists and their trainees. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients with sickle cell disease, disorders of hemostasis and thrombosis, and/or general benign hematologic conditions."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/163729": {
      "title": "AC Track Faculty - GI Oncology at Penn Presbyterian Medical Center",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of gastrointestinal cancers. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Medical Oncology. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include hematology/oncology fellows, house staff and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients with gastrointestinal cancers in an outpatient setting and as an attending on the inpatient service. Enrolling patients into clinical trials is an important role in this position. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193357": {
      "title": "AC Track Faculty Position, Division of Infectious Diseases - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Infectious Diseases Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Infectious Diseases in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certified or board eligible in Infectious Diseases is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching Infectious Diseases fellows, residents and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient weeks at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC) as well as outpatient sessions at the Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine (PCAM)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193359": {
      "title": "AC Track Faculty Position, Division of Infectious Diseases - Associate or Full Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Infectious Diseases Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Infectious Diseases in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certified or board eligible in Infectious Diseases is required.  Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching Infectious Diseases fellows, residents, and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. There will be an expectation of the ability of selected candidates to provide management and/or leadership. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient weeks at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), HUP-Cedar, as well as outpatient sessions at the Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine (PCAM) or PPMC. Clinical areas of focus may include general Infectious Diseases, HIV, and infections in immunocompromised hosts."
    },
