    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164682": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician - GI Hospitalist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Gastroenterology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Gastroenterology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of diagnosis and management of hospitalized patients with gastrointestinal and liver disorders. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants should be board eligible or board certified in Internal Medicine and Gastroenterology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching Penn medical students, residents, and fellows. Candidates should be outstanding clinicians who excel at teaching. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per/year of active and high-quality teaching at the Perelman School of Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include care for patients as a GI Hospitalist in the inpatient setting at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and/or Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC). The clinical responsibilities will include seeing inpatient consults, performing endoscopic procedures, provide teaching to learners, including medical students, residents and fellows. Selected applicants will join a highly interactive and exciting multidisciplinary academic and clinical environment at the University of Pennsylvania as integral members of the Division of Gastroenterology and will have opportunities to teach the GI fellowship and internal medicine residency programs at the Perelman School of Medicine."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171407": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Emergency Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of emergency medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. ABEM certified or board eligible. Teaching responsibilities may include bedside teaching to medical students, residents, and fellows. Additional teaching responsibilities include lectures, journal clubs, case conferences, simulation teaching, small group discussions, and other formats. Dedication to teaching is highly valued in our department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing emergency medical care to patients presented to the emergency department at HUP Spruce, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, HUP Cedar, ED Observation Unit, and Pennsylvania Hospital."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/163206": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Faculty Position - Senior ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Gastroenterology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Gastroenterology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants should board certified or board eligible in Internal Medicine and Gastroenterology. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching Penn medical students, residents, and fellows.  Selected applicants will join a highly interactive and exciting multidisciplinary academic and clinical environment at the University of Pennsylvania as integral members of the Division of Gastroenterology and will have opportunities to teach the GI fellowship and internal medicine residency programs at the Perelman School of Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients in the outpatient and inpatient setting at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH) and/or Penn Medicine at Radnor (PMR) that specializes in inflammatory bowel disease, neurogastroenterology, esophagology, hepatology, advanced endoscopy, and/or general gastroenterology. Responsibilities include seeing patients in clinic as well as performing endoscopy. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to build on an enormously strong foundation of excellence, including over 44,000 outpatient clinic visits and over 34,000 endoscopic procedures, and develop innovative ways for the clinical practice. Candidates should have leadership experience, a record of strong clinical skills, a demonstrated commitment to all missions of the Division, and proven excellence in mentoring, and administrative abilities. Responsibilities include overseeing the clinical programs in gastroenterology, hepatology and endoscopy across the hospitals, each with ambulatory clinics and ambulatory endoscopy unit, and a large outpatient center, also with clinic space and endoscopy unit. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174433": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Faculty Position, Division of Rheumatology - Junior rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Rheumatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Rheumatology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be ABIM certified or eligible in Rheumatology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include caring for patients within the University of Pennsylvania Health System with a variety of rheumatic diseases, including through sub-specialty programs for lupus, myositis, rheumatoid arthritis, scleroderma, Sjögren's syndrome, spondyloarthritis, and vasculitis, and a multidisciplinary Musculoskeletal Center."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174431": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Faculty Position, Division of Rheumatology - Senior ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Rheumatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Rheumatology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be ABIM certified or eligible in Rheumatology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include caring for patients within the University of Pennsylvania Health System with a variety of rheumatic diseases, including through sub-specialty programs for lupus, myositis, rheumatoid arthritis, scleroderma, Sjögren's syndrome, spondyloarthritis, and vasculitis, and a multidisciplinary Musculoskeletal Center. There will be an expectation of the ability of selected candidates to provide management and/or leadership. Rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192115": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Faculty Position, Gastroenterology - Senior ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Gastroenterology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Gastroenterology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible in Internal Medicine and Gastroenterology. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching Penn medical students, residents, and fellows. Selected applicants will join a highly interactive and exciting multidisciplinary academic and clinical environment at the University of Pennsylvania as integral members of the Division of Gastroenterology and will have opportunities to teach the GI fellowship and internal medicine residency programs at the Perelman School of Medicine. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits and active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients in the outpatient and inpatient setting at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH) and/or Penn Medicine at Radnor (PMR) that specializes in inflammatory bowel disease, neurogastroenterology, esophagology, hepatology, advanced endoscopy, and/or general gastroenterology. Responsibilities include seeing patients in clinic as well as performing endoscopy. There will be an expectation of the ability of selected candidates to provide management and/or leadership."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189051": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Faculty Position, VA Medical Center - Junior rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Philadelphia VA Medical Center (PVAMC) and the Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Board certification or board eligibility in Medical Oncology and/or Hematology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients with classical or malignant hematologic conditions and/or solid tumors. Research is not a requirement of the Academic Clinician track; however selected candidates may engage in clinical investigation. Experience and/or advanced training in the conduct of clinical trials is not required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189049": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Faculty Position, VA Medical Center - Senior ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Philadelphia VA Medical Center (PVAMC) and the Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Board certification or board eligibility in Medical Oncology and/or Hematology is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients with classical or malignant hematologic conditions and/or solid tumors. There will be an expectation of the ability of selected candidates to provide management and/or leadership. Research is not a requirement of the academic clinician track; however selected candidates may engage in clinical investigation. Experience and/or advanced training in the conduct of clinical trials is not required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175954": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Position - Hospitalist Program - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hospital Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hospital Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of General Internal Medicine, ideally in Hospital Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified or board eligible in internal medicine is required. Teaching responsibilities may include working in the general medicine teaching services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and/or Penn Presbyterian Medical Center. Candidates will also be expected to mentor medical students and residents. There are also opportunities to teach advanced practice providers and engage in lectures and small groups in the medical school. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include work on non-resident, acute care hospital services and also may include specialized populations such as oncology, LTACH service, or consults/surgical co-management. Core practice sites are the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Good Shepherd Penn Partners/Penn Institute for Rehabilitation Medicine. Prior experience as faculty, including completion of a chief residency or time in hospital medicine, is strongly preferred. Candidates should demonstrate excellence in, teaching with institutional awards, completion of a graduate or professional certificate program or significant institutional, regional or national leadership roles. Successful candidates will benefit from Penn’s robust mentorship and faculty development programs and rich opportunities in quality/process improvement, informatics, medical education, and health care innovation."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175952": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Position - Hospitalist Program - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hospital Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hospital Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of General Internal Medicine, ideally Hospital Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified or board eligible in General Internal Medicine is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include working in the general medicine teaching services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and/or Penn Presbyterian Medical Center. Candidates will also be expected to mentor medical students and residents. There are also opportunities to teach advanced practice providers and engage in lectures and small groups in the medical school. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include work on non-resident, acute care hospital services and also may include specialized populations such as oncology, LTACH service, or consults/surgical co-management. Core practice sites are the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Good Shepherd Penn Partners/Penn Institute for Rehabilitation Medicine. Prior experience as faculty at other academic institutions in general medical practice, ideally in hospital medicine, at the Associate or Full Professor rank is strongly preferred, but strong candidates from ambulatory or specialty backgrounds who have practiced as senior academic faculty will be considered. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching with institutional awards, completion of a graduate or professional certificate programs, or significant institutional, regional or national leadership roles. Successful candidates will benefit from Penn’s robust mentorship and faculty development programs and rich opportunities in quality/process improvement, informatics, medical education, and health care innovation."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191780": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Position, Gastroenterology - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Gastroenterology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Gastroenterology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Internal Medicine and Gastroenterology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching Penn medical students, residents, and fellows. Candidates should be outstanding clinicians who excel at teaching. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per/year of active and high-quality teaching at the Perelman School of Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients in the outpatient and inpatient settings at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH) and/or Penn Medicine at Radnor (PMR) that specializes in inflammatory bowel disease, neurogastroenterology, esophagology, hepatology, advanced endoscopy, and/or general gastroenterology. The clinical responsibilities will include seeing patients in clinic as well as performing endoscopy at each of the sites mentioned."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192669": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Track - Assistant Professor - Dermatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board-certified or board eligible in Dermatology. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical teaching of residents and/or fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include providing health care services at University of Pennsylvania dermatology clinics. Clinicians may see patients at several locations, including Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine, Penn Medicine University City, Dermatology at Pennsylvania Hospital, Dermatology at Bucks County, and Dermatology at Radnor. Successful candidates will have demonstrated record of excellent clinical abilities in the teaching of residents and/or fellows."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169375": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Track - Assistant Professor – Mohs and Dermatological Surgeon",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree and be board-certified or board-eligible upon completion of both an ACGME-accredited residency in dermatology and a fellowship in Micrographic Surgery and Dermatologic Oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include didactics and bedside dermatologic surgery instruction to our world-class residents, fellows, and medical students. We seek enthusiastic candidates who are dedicated to teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include Mohs and reconstructive surgery in our ambulatory practices in Philadelphia or Penn Medicine Radnor. Candidates will benefit from a busy surgical practice and an extensive infrastructure with state-of-the-art facilities and a large support staff of nurses and histotechnicians. Our Mohs surgeons use immunostains for melanoma and other rare tumors, and we mentor candidates to develop these skills. We seek candidates who demonstrate excellent clinical judgement, professionalism, and commitment to our team. Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in Mohs surgery and reconstruction and to building a nationally or internationally recognized career in academic dermatologic surgery. Candidates will enjoy extensive mentorship from our experienced surgeons and faculty to develop advanced surgical skills and an academic niche. The Philadelphia region boasts a rich history with excellent restaurants, sports, art, and neighborhoods. Candidates can book easy plane travel to almost any destination worldwide, and train travel along the East Coast is fast and convenient."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169377": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Track - Associate or Full Professor – Mohs and Dermatological Surgeon",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure Academic Clinician track.  Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree and be board-certified or board-eligible upon completion of both an ACGME-accredited residency in dermatology and a fellowship in Micrographic Surgery and Dermatologic Oncology.  Mid-career individuals are encouraged to apply. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include didactics and bedside dermatologic surgery instruction to our world-class residents, fellows, and medical students. We seek enthusiastic candidates who are dedicated to teaching and mentoring. Clinical responsibilities may include Mohs and reconstructive surgery in our ambulatory practices in Philadelphia or Penn Medicine Radnor. Candidates will benefit from a busy surgical practice and an extensive infrastructure with state-of-the-art facilities and a large support staff of nurses and histotechnicians. Our Mohs surgeons use immunostains for melanoma and other rare tumors, and we mentor candidates to develop these skills. We seek candidates who demonstrate excellent clinical judgement, professionalism, and commitment to our team. Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in Mohs surgery and reconstruction and have a nationally or internationally recognized career in academic dermatologic surgery. The Philadelphia region boasts a rich history with excellent restaurants, sports, art, and neighborhoods. Candidates can book easy plane travel to almost any destination worldwide, and train travel along the East Coast is fast and convenient."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171665": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician Track – Associate or Full Professor - Dermatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA/Montgomeryville The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board-certified or board eligible in Dermatology. Teaching responsibilities may include didactics and clinical teaching of our world-class residents, fellows, and medical students. Clinical responsibilities may include general or sub-specialty dermatology services in our ambulatory practices at the University of Pennsylvania. We are recruiting physicians to practice in several locations in Philadelphia and the surrounding suburbs. Candidates will be able to quickly build a busy practice with high patient demand and an extensive infrastructure with state-of-the-art facilities and a large support staff of nurses. We seek enthusiastic candidates who are dedicated to teaching and who demonstrate excellent clinical judgement, professionalism, and commitment to our academic mission. Rank will be commensurate with experience. The Philadelphia region boasts a rich history with excellent restaurants, sports, art, and neighborhoods. Candidates can book easy plane travel to almost any destination worldwide, and train travel along the east coast is fast and convenient."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180666": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician, Assistant Professor Outpatient Psychiatry—CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include supervising behavioral health trainees (including psychiatry fellows and residents, psychology externs, fellows, and interns); giving lectures to trainees in psychology, psychiatry, and pediatrics; develop curricula. Clinical responsibilities may include providing evaluations, assessment and treatment services to children and families in The Division of Outpatient Behavioral Health (https://www.chop.edu/centers-and-programs/child-and-adolescent-psychiatry-and-behavioral-sciences/dcapbs-outpatient-division), including specialty programs focusing on autism, ADHD/disruptive behavior disorders, mood and anxiety disorders, and eating disorders."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169513": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician, Assistant Professor, Pediatric Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Emergency Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Pediatrics with a focus on Emergency Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include participating in the clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows as a member of the Division of Emergency Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include providing direct patient care in an Emergency Department that has an annual volume of 100,000 visits. Clinical employment opportunities in Pediatric Emergency Medicine are also being offered at both our clinical affiliate institutions, Virtua Voorhees, in Southern New Jersey and our new King of Prussia Center in King of Prussia, PA which is scheduled to open in the Fall of 2021. Positions at Virtua Voorhees and King of Prussia will include an academic appointment, as well as clinical shifts in the CHOP Emergency Department. The distribution of clinical activity at CHOP and the designated clinical affiliate is negotiable, and can be tailored to the interests of the applicant but significant time away from CHOP Main should be expected. Candidates are expected to be knowledgeable of current ED studies and participate in patient enrollment, as needed."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158014": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician, Associate Professor(s) or Full Professor(s), Pediatric Emergency Medicine, CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Emergency Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Certification in Pediatric Emergency Medicine or must be Board-Eligible. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include participating in the clinical education of medical students, residents, and fellows as a member of the Division of Emergency Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include providing direct patient care in an Emergency Department that has an annual volume of 100,000 visits. Clinical employment opportunities in Pediatric Emergency Medicine are also being offered at both our clinical affiliate institutions, Virtua Voorhees, in Southern New Jersey and our new King of Prussia Center in King of Prussia, PA. Positions at Virtua Voorhees and King of Prussia will include an academic appointment, as well as clinical shifts in the CHOP Emergency Department. The distribution of clinical activity at CHOP and the designated clinical affiliate is negotiable and can be tailored to the interests of the applicant but significant time away from CHOP Main should be expected. Candidates are expected to be knowledgeable of current ED studies and participate in patient enrollment, as needed. Experience working in a large, complex medical system is preferred. Ideal candidates should also have comfort and flexibility in caring for a wide range of pediatric diagnoses. Effective communication skills and the ability to work in multidisciplinary teams are essential. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/166163": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician, Associate Professor, Pediatric Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Emergency Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of working in a large, complex medical system. Ideal candidates should also have comfort and flexibility in caring for a wide range of pediatric diagnoses. Effective communication skills and the ability to work in multidisciplinary teams are essential. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Certification in Pediatric Emergency Medicine or must be Board-Eligible is required for all applicants. Teaching responsibilities may include participating in the clinical education of medical students, residents, and fellows as a member of the Division of Emergency Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include providing direct patient care in an Emergency Department that has an annual volume of 100,000 visits. Clinical employment opportunities in Pediatric Emergency Medicine are also being offered at both our clinical affiliate institutions, Virtua Voorhees, in Southern New Jersey and our new King of Prussia Center in King of Prussia, PA. Positions at Virtua Voorhees and King of Prussia will include an academic appointment, as well as clinical shifts in the CHOP Emergency Department. The distribution of clinical activity at CHOP and the designated clinical affiliate is negotiable and can be tailored to the interests of the applicant but significant time away from CHOP Main should be expected. Candidates are expected to be knowledgeable of current ED studies and participate in patient enrollment, as needed."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189528": {
      "title": "Academic Clinician, Division of Integrated Behavioral Health, Senior rank-CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Child & Adolescent Psychiatry, Applicant must have experience in healthcare systems administration, hospital operations & practice management in a large, academic medical center and/or similarly complex environment including leadership experience. Strong preference for active involvement in national organizations and relevant committees. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board certified or board eligible in General Psychiatry and Child and Adolescent Psychiatry. Applicants must be eligible for PA medical license. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include high quality teaching including didactic lectures to interns, fellows, residents, as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Excellence in teaching is required. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include providing inpatient/CL/ER consult and/or outpatient services in the Integrated Division. Candidates must show evidence of continued excellence in clinical care and supervision. Leadership responsibilities may include directing clinical activities in the section while promoting research and educational activities, recruitment of faculty and partnering with quality improvement teams. Required Skill: Developing and maintaining effective relationships with medical, and administrative staff, patients, and the public pertaining to the care of children with medically and psychiatrically complex needs."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/157006": {
      "title": "Academic Surgical Pathologist-Assistant Professor-Academic Clinician Track-Pathology and Laboratory Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Surgical Pathology with a focus on Gastrointestinal, Head and Neck, Gynecological or Breast Pathology. Applicants must have an M.D./Ph.D or equivalent degree. Anatomic Pathology (and/or AP/CP) from the American Board of Pathology or equivalent and an unrestricted PA medical license/eligibility are requisites. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in a broad spectrum of intra and inter departmental teaching activities including pathology house-staff and fellows, and medical student teaching is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include Anatomic Pathology/Clinical Pathology coverage at Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) with subspecialty interest in gynecologic pathology, breast pathology and cytopathology. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161827": {
      "title": "Allergy and Immunology Faculty Position, Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants should be board certified/eligible in Allergy and Immunology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching Allergy and Immunology fellows, other house staff and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include working in the outpatient clinics and as an attending on the inpatient service. Experience in the evaluation of the full range of allergic and immunologic diseases is required. The Section of Allergy and Immunology at Penn provides high quality care for a diverse patient population with a broad range of allergic and immunologic diseases in outpatient clinics and on inpatient consultation services. We seek candidates with proficiency in treating both common and complex allergic and immunologic disorders. This role primarily involves patient care and teaching of Allergy and Immunology fellows as well as other trainees and medical students. Preferred candidates will have an interest and experience in education and systems improvement initiatives. Selected candidates will join a dedicated team in a dynamic and collaborative academic practice. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168423": {
      "title": "Anesthesiologist - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Teaching responsibilities may include the instruction of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the operating rooms and wards of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and the Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC) as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of clinical anesthesia at HUP and PPMC. Opportunities are available with a focus in general and/or cardiovascular anesthesia. Applicants with critical care, neurocritical care, obstetrical, regional, or pain management expertise should apply to the relevant job listing. The academic clinician track emphasizes clinical and teaching excellence. Are you interested in this position but are unsure if it's the right fit? We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Office of Academic Affairs website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/faculty-career-development/"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168425": {
      "title": "Anesthesiologist - Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include the instruction of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the operating rooms and wards of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and the Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC) as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of clinical anesthesia at HUP and PPMC. Opportunities are available with a focus on general and/or cardiovascular anesthesia. Applicants with critical care, neurocritical care, obstetrical, regional, or pain management expertise should apply to the relevant job listing. The academic clinician track emphasizes clinical and teaching excellence. Are you interested in this position but are unsure if it's the right fit? We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Office of Academic Affairs website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/faculty-career-development/"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186779": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Academic Clinician - Surgical Retina",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents, students, and fellows at the Scheie Eye Institute, the Philadelphia VA and one of Scheie's satellite offices. Clinical responsibilities may include providing medical and surgical retina care for patients at the Scheie Eye Institute, Philadelphia VA, and one of Scheie's satellite offices."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182328": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Academic Clinician Track - Outpatient Clinic",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of adult psychiatry. Applicants must have an M.D., D.O., or equivalent degree from an international medical school. Candidates must be board certified/board eligible in psychiatry and eligible for medical licensure in Pennsylvania. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and supervising medical students and residents in an outpatient setting. Clinical responsibilities may include direction of patient care, establishment of diagnosis, development of treatment plans, documentation of treatment services and provision of direct ongoing care and services to psychiatric outpatients. The successful applicant will have demonstrated excellent qualifications in education and clinical care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183936": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Academic Clinician- Cutaneous Oncologist (Dermatology)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of non-invasive diagnosis and surveillance of pigmented lesions is required. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicant must be board certified or board eligible in the field of Dermatology with focus on cutaneous oncology and skin cancers at increased risk for recurrence or metastasis. Skin cancer expertise, proven by publications, invited lectures, or clinical experience, is strongly preferred. Demonstrated leadership experience or potential is preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include didactics to our world-class residents, fellows, medical students and trainees rotating from other institutions in dermatology and other specialties concerning skin cancer, Mohs micrographic surgery and dermatologic oncology. The faculty member(s) will play a key role in educating our residents on the cutaneous oncology track and research fellow in cutaneous oncology. Clinical responsibilities may include evaluation and treatment of patients with skin cancer, particularly those with a high risk of recurrence or metastasis. Clinical responsibilities will focus on patients in the Penn Dermatology Oncology Center's specialty clinics, including the Pigmented Lesion Clinic, the Rare and Inherited Skin Cancer Clinic, and the High-Risk Skin Cancer Clinic for Organ Transplant Recipients and Immunosuppressed patients. Candidates will benefit from a busy practice and an extensive infrastructure with state-of-the-art facilities and a large support staff of nurses, histotechnicians, research fellows, and coordinators. We seek candidates who demonstrate excellent clinical judgement, professionalism, and commitment to our team. Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in Cutaneous Oncology and building a nationally or internationally recognized career in dermatology. Candidates will enjoy extensive mentorship from our experienced dermatological oncologists and faculty to develop advanced preventive and treatment skills. The Philadelphia region boasts a rich history with excellent restaurants, sports, art, and neighborhoods. Candidates can book easy plane travel to almost any destination worldwide, and train travel along the East Coast is fast and convenient."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175128": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Academic Movement Disorders Physician - AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Parkinson’s disease, related disorders and other movement disorders. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. The successful candidate must be board certified or eligible in Neurology. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include out-patient consultations and ongoing care of patients with Movement Disorders. Expertise with botulinum toxin injection and management of neurostimulators is strongly encouraged. Supervision of residents clinic and a minor component of inpatient care of general neurology patients (approximately 1-2 weeks per year) may be required. Clinical care will be primarily at Pennsylvania Hospital, but some coverage of satellite clinics in suburban locations may be available. Participation as a site investigator in clinical trials is encouraged. Collaboration on research publications is encouraged but not required. Completion of fellowship in Movement Disorders preferred."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193531": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Clinical Neuropsychologist - AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of comprehensive neuropsychological assessment and assessment of neurologic populations, including those with epilepsy, stroke, movement disorders, multiple sclerosis, dementia and neuro-oncology. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. The candidate should be licensed (or license eligible) in Pennsylvania, have completed a predoctoral internship and postdoctoral fellowship in neuropsychology according to the Houston Conference Guidelines and be eligible for board certification in Clinical Neuropsychology.  Applicants will have a minimum of two years of experience (including post-doctoral training) conducting assessments of individuals with a variety of neurological problems, excellent written and oral communication skills, integrative report writing skills, and interpersonal and time management skills, and experience working in an interdisciplinary setting. Teaching responsibilities may include providing clinical supervision for trainees at the pre-doctoral (practicum and internship) and post-doctoral level, supervising staff psychometricians, participating in neuropsychology seminar series, and participating in intern and postdoctoral trainee application review and interviews. Clinical responsibilities may include providing neuropsychological evaluations in a high-volume assessment service, providing comprehensive, patient-centered care tailored to the neurologic populations served, providing consultation to multidisciplinary teams, including pre-surgical evaluations, and providing expertise in evaluation of cognition on collaborative clinical research. Clinical practice will be at multiple out-patient Penn Medicine clinic locations, with the potential for occasional in-patient consultation."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194827": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Clinical/Teaching Faculty in Neurocritical Care - AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board-certified in Neurology, must have completed an ACGME- approved or UCNS-approved fellowship in Neurocritical Care, and must be board-certified or eligible in Neurocritical Care. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching of fellows, residents, advanced practice providers and medical students will be expected through bedside rounds and through a formal didactic curriculum, including the Division’s neurocritical care didactic conference. Teaching in the Perelman School of Medicine through formal courses, such as the Brain and Behavior Course, will be strongly encouraged. Opportunities for educational leadership within the Penn Neurocritical Care Fellowship Program may be available to the right candidate. Clinical responsibilities may include for this primarily clinical position, responsibilities will include attending on all services of the Neurocritical Care Division, which presently include the primary inpatient NeuroICU services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), inpatient neurocritical care consultation, including consultation for the RECOVER (Recovery Following Acute Brain Injury) Program at HUP and/or PPMC. Outpatient responsibilities, most likely in the RECOVER Program clinic or the TBI clinic, are anticipated; the specific balance of inpatient consultative and outpatient work will be tailored to the applicant’s interests. The position might, at a later date, include a Neurocritical Care Consult Service and/or a Tele-neurocritical care consult service. The applicant must have demonstrated excellent qualifications in education and clinical care. The successful applicant will have experience in the field of Neurology with completion of a fellowship in Neurocritical care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177037": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Clinician Educator Track - Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Neonatology and Newborn Services Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Neonatology & Newborn Services in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine by the American Board of Pediatrics. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows as well as formal lecture opportunities within the Division and Department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical care and productivity in program development. Clinical care will be provided in the 100 bed Level IV NICU at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and the 40 bed Level III NICU at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Duties also include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or basic studies and will be dependent on the candidate’s interests and independent support. Evidence of scholarship is required for the Clinician-Educator track."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175477": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Department of Neurology/ Division of Cognitive Neurology - AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of clinical experience in the diagnosis and management of adult cognitive conditions with emphasis on Alzheimer's Disease. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be Board eligible in Neurology. Board certified in Neurology is a preference. The succesful candidate will be Fellowship trained in Cognitive and Behavioral Neurology. Teaching responsibilities may include staffing patients in neurology resident clinic every other week, working with Cognitive Neurology Fellows, lectures for medical students, neurology residents and cognitive neurology fellows, and mentoring residents and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include seeing patients in the Penn Memory Center, Frontotemporal Disorders Center, and general cognitive neurology with a focus on Alzheimer's Disease and participating in clinical research trials and studies in Alzheimer's Disease and Related Dementias."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172588": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Neuromuscular Medicine Neurologist – AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Neuromuscular Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applications must be board-certified or board-eligible in Neurology and Neuromuscular Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, neuromuscular fellows, as well as EMG technologists. Clinical responsibilities may include the clinical care of patients with neuromuscular diseases. This may include the performance of nerve conduction studies and EMG, as well as inpatient neurology service time in line with the standard clinical department requirements. Research is not a requirement of faculty on the AC track. Candidates may have opportunities to have active involvement in neuromuscular clinical trials."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179686": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Research Track - Epigenetics Research Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of advanced genomics and super-resolution imaging techniques appropriate for the understanding of the interplay of epigenetics and tumor initiation and progression. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative and independent research programs related to cancer epigenetics, co-supervision of postdoctoral fellows, students, and research staff, coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators or independently, and active leadership in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts. The selected candidate will participate in cancer biology and epigenetic programs at Penn Medicine."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177039": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Research Track - Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Neonatology and Newborn Services Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Neonatology & Newborn Services in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure research track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine by the American Board of Pediatrics or Internal Medicine. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include having a national reputation for collaborative or independent research of high quality with distinctive, original, and expert intellectual contributions. For Full Professor rank, candidates must show evidence of an international reputation for their scientific accomplishments. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in basic laboratory research with a publication record in neonatology, developmental or molecular medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include education of postdocs and fellows as well as formal lecture opportunities within the Division and Department."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193339": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Tenure Track, Division of Experimental Pathology - Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the tenure track. Applicants must have an Ph.D. and/or M.D. degree. Applicants must show evidence of strong postdoctoral or fellowship experience, demonstrating excellent research accomplishments, intellectual independence, and leadership promise. They must have a clear record of productivity and ingenuity, a high likelihood of securing extramural funding, and a desire to take advantage of our unique collaborative environment. Teaching responsibilities may include providing an outstanding training environment for undergraduate, graduate and medical students, as well as clinical and postdoctoral fellows. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing and maintaining an independent, extramurally funded research program. We aim to recruit an outstanding faculty colleague who is using molecular tools and innovative technologies to probe the mechanistic basis of pediatric diseases. We are particularly interested in candidates developing or leveraging platform technologies in areas such as functional genomics, (epi)transcriptomics, proteomics, metabolomics, genome and RNA engineering, chemical biology, protein design, human organoids, and advanced molecular and cellular imaging, although we welcome applications from exceptional candidates pursuing other innovative and impactful research directions. We expect the successful candidate to engage broadly across diverse research communities and build upon existing Departmental and institutional strengths in areas including immunology, infectious disease, cancer biology, neuroscience, RNA biology, epigenetics, and cellular architecture, with the strongest candidates demonstrating potential to bridge between these research areas. The position is within the Experimental Pathology Division at the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP). Faculty within the Division are active members of many of the centers and institutes that span research across the University of Pennsylvania system. As a CHOP-based Penn faculty member, the candidate will have access to the rich research resources, core facilities, and collaborative opportunities offered across the entire University of Pennsylvania/CHOP campus. In addition to resources available to all Penn investigators, the CHOP Research Institute offers unique advantages such as close ties to clinicians and access to patient materials. A generous recruitment package and lab space will be provided, together with outstanding institutional resources."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177043": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Tenure Track, Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Neonatology and Newborn Services Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Neonatology & Newborn Services in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine by the American Board of Pediatrics or Internal Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include consultations for high risk neonatology and maternal and fetal conditions, as well as prenatal genetic diagnosis. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include a body of work that demonstrates intellectual independence, co-supervision of postdoctoral fellows, students, and research staff, coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators, participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts, and a publication record in neonatology, developmental or molecular medicine."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180141": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor AC Track – Assistant Director of Clinical Chemistry Laboratory - Children's Hospital of Philadelphia",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Clinical Chemistry. Applicants must have an M.D. and/or Ph.D degree. Ph.D. applicants must have appropriate postgraduate board certification or active candidate status (ABCC in Clinical Chemistry). M.D. applicants must have board eligibility/certification in clinical pathology. Physicians must be eligible/licensed in the state of Pennsylvania. Teaching responsibilities may include fellows, residents, medical and graduate students or Medical Laboratory Scientist students. Clinical responsibilities may include assisting in oversight of clinical chemistry laboratory operations, clinical test interpretation, quality control, innovation and test development. The successful candidate will serve as Assistant Director of the Clinical Chemistry Laboratory. Demonstrated ability in test development, experience with total lab automation, and expertise with mass spectrometry is required. Post-graduate training experience in pediatric clinical chemistry is strongly preferred."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172930": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Academic Clinician Cardiac Anesthesiologist – CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Pediatric Anesthesiology with a focus on Pediatric Cardiothoracic Anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspeciality certification or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology, the equivalent, or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching in our formal didactic lecture program as well as the informal teaching of medical students, residents, fellows, and other health care professionals working in the cardiothoracic operating rooms and procedural areas. Clinical responsibilities may include direct patient care and medical direction in the cardiothoracic operating rooms and procedural areas. Primary practice is located at the Philadelphia campus of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Experience in pediatric cardiothoracic anesthesiology and evidence of academic productivity and leadership in projects related to an area of focus is required. The Academic Clinician track is intended for faculty members who demonstrate impactful contributions to clinical care and education and who develop an Area of Concentration (AoC) in which they become recognized. We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/flpd/career-development/ ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172222": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Academic Clinician Cardiac Critical Care Medicine - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Cardiac Critical Care Medicine with a focus on Pediatric Cardiac Critical Care Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Completion of fellowship training in pediatric critical care medicine or pediatric cardiology is required.  Candidates must be ABP certification in pediatric critical care medicine or pediatric cardiology, the equivalent, or status as a candidate in the examination system. The ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license is mandatory. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching in our formal didactic lecture program as well as the informal teaching of medical students, residents, fellows, and other health care professionals working in the Cardiac Intensive Care Unit. Attendance and participation in lectures, presentations, and conferences within the division as well as multidisciplinary conferences is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include direct patient care and medical direction in the Cardiac Intensive Care Unit. Primary practice is located at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. The major emphasis of the Academic Clinician track is teaching and clinical excellence in pediatric cardiac critical care medicine, and a sustained record of professionalism. The expectation is that there will be a chosen area of concentration that include, but are not limited to, education, clinical operations, community service, quality and safety, health equity, diversity and inclusion, health policy, and global health. Evidence of academic productivity and leadership in projects related to an area of focus will be required. We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: Faculty Career Development | Faculty Career Development | Office of Academic Affairs | Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/170485": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Academic Clinician Critical Care Medicine - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Critical Care Medicine with a focus on Pediatric Critical Care Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABP certification or board eligibility and Pennsylvania licensure and completion of fellowship training in pediatric critical care medicine is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching in our formal didactic lecture program as well as the informal teaching of medical students, residents, fellows, and other health care professionals working in the Pediatric Intensive Care Unit. Attendance and participation in lectures, presentations, and conferences within the division as well as multidisciplinary conferences is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical practice in the Pediatric Intensive Care Unit at our Philadelphia and/or King of Prussia campuses and may include practice in the Progressive Care Unit at our Philadelphia campus."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/170481": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Academic Clinician General Anesthesiology - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Anesthesiology with a focus on Pediatric Anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspecialty certification, the equivalent, or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology or status as a candidate in the examination system, along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license, is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching both in our formal didactic lecture program as well as in the informal teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows in the Operating Rooms. Clinical responsibilities may include direct patient care and medical direction in the Operating Rooms. Primary practice is located at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and King of Prussia campuses. Experience in pediatric anesthesiology and teaching of residents and fellows required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/160951": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor at HUP Cedar - Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of acute psychiatric treatment and management. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Must be board certified or board eligible by the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical supervision of rotating medical students, residents, and advanced practice learners. Participation in psychiatry residency and medical student classroom teaching. May also include serving as an educational site director for residents, medical students, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include evaluation, treatment, and management of patients on acute psychiatry services, including inpatient units, inpatient detox, crisis response center, and consultation/liaison. Participation in HUP Cedar quality improvement efforts and potential clinical leadership responsibilities for appropriate candidates. This position will have no mandatory call responsibilities but will have the option of compensated, voluntary call. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180159": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor at Pennsylvania Hospital - AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of emergency psychiatry, especially the evaluation and management of suicidality, homicidality, behavioral agitation, and acute presentations of mood, anxiety, psychosis, and substance use disorders. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology certified or eligible. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical supervision of medical students, psychiatry residents, and emergency medicine residents in emergency psychiatry; didactic teaching of psychiatry residents in emergency psychiatry. Clinical responsibilities may include delivery of care in the Crisis Response Center at Pennsylvania Hospital, including serving as physician leader of the interdisciplinary treatment team; assessment of patients in crisis; medication management of psychiatric emergencies; ensuring of safe disposition; and collaboration with advanced practice practitioners. Additional responsibilities will include collaboration with emergency department providers and engagement in quality and safety initiatives. Candidates with relevant qualifications and interest may also be considered for clinical leadership responsibilities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169747": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor CE, Retina Specialist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of retina. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents, students, and fellows at Scheie. Clinical responsibilities may include providing medical and surgical retina care for patients at Scheie and one of Scheie's satellite offices. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include collaborative or independent research within a specific area. Applicants in early careers with a demonstrated record of scholarship are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172928": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Clinician-Educator Cardiac Anesthesiologist – CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Pediatric Anesthesiology with a focus on cardiothoracic anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspeciality certification or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology, the equivalent, or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching both formal didactic lecture program as well as in the informal teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the cardiothoracic operating rooms and procedural areas. Clinical responsibilities may include direct patient care and medical direction in the cardiothoracic operating rooms and procedural areas. Primary practice is located at the Philadelphia campus of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include investigator-initiated and collaborative research.  The non-tenure Clinician Educator track involves a substantial commitment to research. Evidence of continuous scholarly productivity reflecting a defined focus will be required. Are you interested in this position but are unsure if it's the right fit? We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/faculty-career-development/career-development/."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172224": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Clinician-Educator Cardiac Critical Care Medicine - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Pediatric Critical Care Medicine with a focus on Pediatric Cardiac Critical Care Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Completion of fellowship training in pediatric critical care medicine or pediatric cardiology is required.  Candidates must be ABP certification in pediatric critical care medicine or pediatric cardiology, the equivalent, or status as a candidate in the examination system. The ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license is mandatory. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching in our formal didactic lecture program as well as the informal teaching of medical students, residents, fellows, and other health care professionals working in the Cardiac Intensive Care Unit (CICU). Attendance and participation in lectures, presentations, and conferences within the division as well as multidisciplinary conferences is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical practice in the Cardiac Intensive Care Unit at our Philadelphia campus of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. this is the primary practice location. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include collaborative research and the mentoring of medical students, residents, and fellows in their own scholarly pursuits. In addition to excellence in teaching and clinical care, responsibilities may include investigator-initiated and collaborative research in addition to the mentoring of medical students, residents, and fellows in their own scholarly pursuits. The non-tenure Clinician Educator track involves a substantial commitment to research. Evidence of continuous scholarly productivity reflecting a defined focus will be required. Are you interested in this position but are unsure if it's the right fit? We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: Faculty Career Development | Faculty Career Development | Office of Academic Affairs | Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/170486": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Clinician-Educator Critical Care Medicine - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Critical Care Medicine with a focus on Pediatric Critical Care Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABP certification or board eligibility and Pennsylvania licensure and completion of fellowship training in pediatric critical care medicine is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching in our formal didactic lecture program as well as the informal teaching of medical students, residents, fellows, and other health care professionals working in the Pediatric Intensive Care Unit. Attendance and participation in lectures, presentations, and conferences within the division as well as multidisciplinary conferences is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical practice in the Pediatric Intensive Care Unit at our Philadelphia and/or King of Prussia campuses and may include practice in the Progressive Care Unit at our Philadelphia campus. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include collaborative research and the mentoring of medical students, residents, and fellows in their own scholarly pursuits."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/170482": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Clinician-Educator General Anesthesiology - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Anesthesiology with a focus on Pediatric Anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspecialty certification, the equivalent, or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology or status as a candidate in the examination system, along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license, is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching both in our formal didactic lecture program as well as in the informal teaching of medical students, residents and fellows rotating through the Operating Rooms. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of clinical anesthesia and medical direction in the Operating Rooms. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include collaborative research, grants and peer reviewed publications. Primary practice located at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and King of Prussia campuses. Experience in pediatric anesthesiology and evidence of scholarship is required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180737": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Comprehensive Ophthalmology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must hold an M.D. or equivalent degree. Clinical responsibilities may include a faculty practice with spanning comprehensive ophthalmic medical and surgical care at Scheie Eye Institute and select satellite locations, with the majority of outpatient services provided at the Penn Medicine location in Wilmington, Delaware. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in didactic and clinical instruction of residents and, as needed, medical students and fellows at Scheie."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175244": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Glaucoma",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania and the Philadelphia VA Medical Center (PVAMC) seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Glaucoma. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents, students, and fellows at Scheie and the Philadelphia VA. Clinical responsibilities may include providing medical and surgical glaucoma care for patients at Scheie, the Philadelphia VA, and one of Scheie's satellite offices."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192679": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Addiction Psychiatry at the Philadelphia VAMC - Clinician Educator Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Philadelphia VA Medical Center (PVAMC) and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of addiction genetics, chronic pain, structural equation modeling and similar multivariate statistics. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Psychology licensure is required. Teaching responsibilities may include providing lectures to psychiatric residents and research mentoring to undergraduate, medical and graduate students. Clinical responsibilities may include providing clinical care at the Philadelphia VAMC to patients with substance use disorders. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include building an independent research program in the genetics of substance use, pain traits, a comorbid psychiatric conditions. Demonstrated success in obtaining extramural research funding is preferred."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186089": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in CBT for Anxiety at the CTSA - Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of cognitive behavioral therapy for anxiety-related disorders across the lifespan, including among youth. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Licensure to deliver psychotherapy in PA and license eligibility in NJ is required. Teaching responsibilities may include supervision and didactics for psychiatry residents, postdoctoral fellows, psychology interns, and psychology externs in cognitive behavioral therapy for anxiety-related disorders across the lifespan. In addition, the ideal candidate will teach workshops to community clinicians on CBT for anxiety across the lifespan with some specialized content for treating youth. Clinical responsibilities may include provision of CBT for anxiety-related disorders in children, adolescents, and adults as well as conducting diagnostic intake evaluations across the lifespan."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/162651": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Stroke/Vascular Neurology – Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of stroke and cerebrovascular disease, with successful completion of an ACGME-certified fellowship in Vascular Neurology. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Board certification in Neurology. Board certification or board-eligible in Vascular Neurology. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include being an attending on the stroke inpatient and consult services at the Penn Medicine hospitals and telestroke/call service across the health system, with possibly additional service at affiliated hospitals if needed, in proportion to clinical effort and as shared with other members of the division. When not on service, the new faculty member will do outpatient sessions commensurate with effort. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189361": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in the Basser Center for BRCA in partnership with the Department of Cancer Biology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Cancer Biology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Cancer Biology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania in collaboration with the Basser Center for BRCA seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the tenure track. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include focused classroom teaching in an existing area of expertise as well as mentoring graduate and undergraduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and other research trainees. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishment and maintenance of an externally funded, independent research program that leads to impactful publications focused on breast, ovarian, prostate, or pancreas cancer, or other cancers associated with inherited mutations in BRCA1 and BRCA2. The Basser Center and the Department of Cancer Biology value a supportive, cohesive, and collaborative culture. Growth of junior faculty is fostered by providing tailored mentoring and faculty development from appointment through tenure and all major career milestones. Successful candidates are expected to have either achieved success in areas broadly related to BRCA-associated cancers, or to have an established focus on the biology of breast, ovarian, pancreas or prostate cancers accompanied by future research plans to investigate the role of BRCA1/2 in these cancers. All candidates are expected to have demonstrated high-quality scholarship through publication in peer-reviewed journals and independent research funding. Basic or translational scientists interested in the mechanisms of tumor development and interception of tumors common in BRCA1/2 mutation carriers are highly sought. Areas of particular interest include: a) Investigation of the haploinsufficent state and how this leads to cancer; b) tissue specificity related to BRCA1 and BRCA2 (why cancers emerge from breast, ovarian, prostate and pancreas when all cells in affected individuals are heterozygous?) c) hormonal influences on DNA repair and tumorigenesis; d) early detection of cancer; and e) models of cancer initiation and interception. The Basser Center for BRCA was established at Penn Medicine's Abramson Cancer Center in 2012 as the first comprehensive center for the research, treatment, and prevention of BRCA-related cancers. More information on the Basser Center for BRCA can be found at www.basser.org. Applications will be evaluated on a rolling basis, but to ensure full consideration applicants are encouraged to apply by September 1. Applicants will be evaluated based on the following required documents: 1. Cover letter (Highlight past and proposed research and its synergies with Penn Cancer Biology, Basser Center, and the University, 1 page maximum). 2. Curriculum vitae (Highlight 3 to 5 impactful publications using several sentences to provide context about the specific advances for the field and the candidate’s role in these studies). 3. Anonymized Executive Summary (one page max): Please provide brief, anonymized responses to the following prompts, with further details to be provided in additional documents: 1) Briefly describe your two most important research contributions to date; 2) Describe your vision for your independent research program, including “big picture” questions that you plan to address in your laboratory; 3) Highlight how your work will contribute to the mission of the Basser Center; 4) Describe any contributions to teaching, mentoring, and scientific community. 4. Statement of significant research contributions and plans for an independent research program (2-3 pages). This document should briefly describe past research accomplishments -research questions, an applicant’s intellectual contributions, the research findings and significance, and future research plan as well as opportunities for integration and collaboration with Penn Cancer Biology, the Basser Center and the University. 5. Statement of Teaching, Mentoring, and Community (1 page). This statement will focus on contributions and commitment to the advancement of collaborative research, mentoring, teaching, and inclusion in science. We seek candidates with a demonstrated track record of and/or plans for promoting an environment focused on collaborative and inclusive research, and high-quality mentoring and teaching. This document should briefly describe candidate’s prior or future actions towards research collaborations, teaching and mentoring of trainees in the lab and classroom, service to the scientific and/or broader community. 6. Reference Letters (3 minimum)"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171563": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Nephrology-Hypertension, Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of care of patients with complex hypertension. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Nephrology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care for patients in both inpatient and outpatient services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Expertise in treatment of patients with complex hypertension and with neuroendocrine tumors, and certification by the American Society of Hypertension is preferred."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158485": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine - AC Track, Lung Transplant Service",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pulmonary and critical care, primarily in lung transplantation as an attending on the inpatient and outpatient services, as well as providing services in the outpatient transplant clinic. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicant should be board certified or board eligible in Pulmonary and Critical Care. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching pulmonary and critical care fellows, house staff and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include consultation, evaluation, and management of outpatient and inpatient lung transplant candidates and recipients within the health system on a growing lung transplant service. Selected candidates will have experience working with advanced practice providers and trainees. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193992": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine - diabetes focus",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Diabetes and diabetes care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification or eligibility in Endocrinology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include conducting clinical and education activities. There will be an opportunity to teach in the endocrine fellowship and internal medicine residency programs in the Perelman School of Medicine. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include providing clinical care for patients with Diabetes and other Endocrine disorders. The selected candidate will be an integral member of the Division of Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism with a practice focus on diabetes."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173476": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine - GU Oncology at Penn Presbyterian Medical Center",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of solid tumors with an emphasis in genitourinary cancer. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Applicants must be board certified or board eligible in Medical Oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents and fellows as well as advanced practice providers, pharmacists and their trainees. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include the care of general oncology patients with an emphasis in genitourinary cancer."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186581": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine, Echocardiography/Multimodality Faculty Position",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Echocardiography. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Internal Medicine and Cardiovascular Diseases. Completed Level III certification in echocardiography is strongly preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and supervising medical students, residents, and fellows in the echocardiography laboratory and if applicable while on rotation. Clinical responsibilities may include reading transthoracic and stress echocardiograms, supervising transesophageal echocardiograms, seeing patients in the echocardiography laboratory and inpatient service or clinic, and reading CT/MRI/nuclear. Located in the heart of Philadelphia, Penn Medicine offers a uniquely dynamic environment that seamlessly integrates world-class academic medicine with the vitality of a major metropolitan center. As part of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Medicine is consistently ranked among the nation’s leading academic health systems, distinguished by its depth of clinical expertise, pioneering research enterprise, and longstanding commitment to innovation in patient care and medical education. Faculty benefit from an unparalleled ecosystem of collaboration, working alongside internationally recognized leaders across disciplines and engaging in cutting-edge, translational research that directly informs clinical practice. The institution’s robust infrastructure—including access to interdisciplinary centers, advanced clinical programs, and expansive research funding—supports meaningful career development across clinical, research, educational, and leadership pathways. Philadelphia itself offers a rich and vibrant cultural landscape, with renowned institutions such as the Philadelphia Museum of Art, the Kimmel Center for the Performing Arts, and a nationally recognized dining scene. The city combines historic character with modern livability, featuring walkable neighborhoods, diverse communities, and a relatively accessible cost of living compared to peer cities. The University provides a comprehensive and highly competitive benefits package, including multiple retirement savings options and generous tuition benefits for eligible dependents—further enhancing the long-term value of a faculty appointment. Collectively, Penn Medicine and Philadelphia represent an exceptional opportunity for individuals seeking to advance their careers within a collaborative, high-impact academic environment while enjoying the cultural, professional, and lifestyle advantages of a premier urban setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192734": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine, Interventional Cardiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Interventional Cardiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Internal Medicine, Cardiovascular Disease, and Interventional Cardiology. Additional advanced fellowship training in structural heart disease or complex coronary/chronic total occlusion (CTO) interventions is highly desired. Teaching responsibilities may include educating medical students, residents, cardiovascular fellows and advanced practice providers. Selected candidates will be expected to contribute to the educational mission of the organization. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include the development of an outpatient clinical practice as well as attending on the inpatient services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and associated practice sites. Located in the heart of Philadelphia, Penn Medicine offers a uniquely dynamic environment that blends world-class academic medicine with the energy of a major metropolitan center. Its strategic position provides seamless access to New Jersey, New York, Maryland, and Washington, D.C., placing faculty at the center of one of the most densely networked healthcare and research corridors in the country. The region supports robust collaboration, diverse patient populations, and extensive professional opportunities across clinical care, research, education, and leadership—making it an exceptionally attractive destination for those seeking both career advancement and a vibrant, accessible place to live and work."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177949": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine/Non-Diabetes Endocrinology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of thyroid cancer and thyroid nodules. Technical skill in performance of radiofrequency is required. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Board certified in Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism required. Teaching responsibilities may include conducting clinical and education activities. Selected candidates will have the opportunity to teach in the endocrine fellowship and internal medicine residency programs in the Perelman School of Medicine. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include providing clinical care for patients with a focus on thyroid cancer and thyroid nodules. The new physician will perform radiofrequency ablation procedures and may also perform thyroid nodule fine-needle aspiration biopsy procedures. The new physician will be an integral member of the Division of Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism with a practice based at the Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine. Selected candidates will have demonstrated excellent qualifications in education and clinical care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188881": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Neurology at CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include bedside teaching and oversight of observers, medical students, residents and fellows in a clinical setting, and formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient service and outpatient clinic. We are recruiting board-eligible or board-certified Child Neurologists to facilitate the new Neuroscience Center’s expansion. The positions offer a blend of outpatient clinic in the CHOP satellites and inpatient service at the CHOP Philadelphia Campus as well the Middleman Family Pavilion at the CHOP King of Prussia Campus. CHOP Neurology satellite outpatient clinics include several Pennsylvania-based locations in Chalfont, Abington, Lancaster, Bryn Mawr, and King of Prussia, as well as New Jersey-based practice locations in Voorhees and Princeton. We seek child neurologists with broad clinical skills who are interested in a dynamic practice combining clinical excellence with academic and teaching opportunities. Neurologists with expertise in epilepsy/clinical neurophysiology, headache, neonatal neurology, critical care neurology, and inpatient neurology are especially encouraged to apply. Program Highlights: • Join a team of 63 Child Neurology attending physicians and scientists. • Our ACGME-accredited 5-year child neurology residency program matches 7 residents per year. • Our Neuroscience Center integrates world-renowned specialists in Child Neurology and Neurosurgery to provide precise diagnoses, individualized clinical care, and cutting-edge surgical treatments to achieve groundbreaking discoveries. • The CHOP Philadelphia Campus is home to a dedicated 24-bed inpatient Neuroscience Unit staffed by an inter-disciplinary team with specialized training in pediatric neuroscience. This state-of-the-art unit houses the Epilepsy Monitoring Unit and is specially equipped to meet the unique medical and surgical needs of infants, children, and young adults with neurological and neurosurgical conditions. • The CHOP Philadelphia Campus is also home to large neonatal, pediatric, and cardiac intensive care units, along with extensive ED and Ward neurology consultation. • Shared call rotation of 5-6 weeks/weekends per year. The Pennsylvania based CHOP satellites are located in the suburbs of Philadelphia. The CHOP King of Prussia Hospital opened in January 2022 and is 45 minutes from the main campus. The goal of the hospital is to increase access for patients to high quality care by CHOP providers convenient to their home. Additional child neurologists will allow for expansion of inpatient neurologic care and a 4-bed epilepsy monitoring unit in this new community hospital. For more information, contact aliced@chop.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178236": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Neurology, Division of General Neurology, AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certification in Neurology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students and residents in the outpatient clinic and inpatient setting and instructing clinical fellows in allied specialties such as ENT, internal medicine, and family medicine. The candidate will help identify and schedule appropriate speakers and topics for the weekly general neurology group case conference and for the resident lecture series and assist with the virtual “Case of the Month” series. Opportunities to teach in the preclinical Brain and Behavior course also are provided. Clinical responsibilities may include personal clinics at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and Pennsylvania Hospital, as well as attending responsibilities for resident clinics at HUP. These personal clinics will primarily be specialized clinics focusing on neuro-otology. There may be a small component of more general neurology clinics, particularly headache patients. Participation in clinical trial recruitment, CME activities, and quality improvement initiatives is welcome."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176284": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Ob/Gyn specializing in Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery (MIGS). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified and trained in Obstetrics and Gynecology and have formal fellowship training in MIGS. Teaching responsibilities may include training and supervision of Ob Gyn residents and medical students. Teaching Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery fellows is in the near future as well. Clinical responsibilities may include gynecologic care and minimally invasive surgery. Our growing practice provides multidisciplinary care of patients with complex conditions such as: *Fibroids and abnormal uterine bleeding, *Chronic pelvic pain and endometriosis and *Abnormal placentation and complex ectopic pregnancies. The MIGS surgeons at Penn Medicine provide expertise in multiple surgical modalities such as laparoscopy, robotics, and operative hysteroscopy. Candidates will join a cadre of surgeons at Penn Medicine who are nationally known for their surgical expertise, education and innovation. The successful candidate will receive fully-covered malpractice insurance and practice in a supportive environment that provides professional and personal fulfillment and career-long learning."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187608": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Obstetrics & Gynecology in Surgery at CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of obstetrics & gynecology and maternal fetal medicine with a focus on prenatal diagnosis and fetal therapy. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. The preferred candidate will be certified or eligible for certification by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology or hold equivalent certification. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic education of medical students, residents and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include activities centering on prenatal diagnosis and counseling, fetal surgical interventions and the management and delivery of pregnancies complicated by congenital anomalies. This position will be housed in the Richard D. Wood Jr. Center for Fetal Diagnosis and Treatment, administered by the Department of Surgery at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. We are recognized as a world class fetal diagnosis & treatment center and a pioneer in the development of new fetal diagnostic and therapeutic procedures."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173369": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Epidemiology, Research Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology and Informatics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biostatistics and Epidemiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of the statistical design and analysis of randomized clinical trials.  Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Additional qualifications include: • A strong background and expertise in Bayesian statistical methods, causal inference, machine learning, pragmatic trial designs with cluster-randomization methods, and complex missing data methodology. • Expertise in statistical programming (R, Python, Stan/BUGS). • Proficiency with clinical trial simulation to support both methodological research and the initial design and subsequent modification of trials. • Experience supporting large-scale trials, clinical research networks, and/or data and safety monitoring board statistical activities. • Experience collaborating with clinician-scientists, particularly physician-scientists. • Proficiency in analyzing and interpreting patient-reported outcome measures such as quality-of-life endpoints, including handling of missing data such as that due to non-response, death, or other intercurrent events. • Demonstrated aptitude working with state-of-the-art computing infrastructure, Overleaf/LaTeX, GitHub, and supporting reproducible research pipelines. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include demonstrated ability to lead peer-reviewed publications in clinical trials methodology and support multi-site collaborative research projects. The Center for Clinical Trials Innovation in the Division of Epidemiology, Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology, and Informatics, in collaboration with the Palliative and Advanced Illness Research Center, seeks candidates with a PhD in Statistical Epidemiology, Biostatistics, Statistics, or a closely related quantitative field, with 1+ years of postdoctoral experience. The ideal candidates will be outstanding early-career researchers who will advance innovative clinical trial methodologies and lead cutting-edge research in the statistical design, analysis, monitoring, and interpretation of complex multi-arm, cluster, pragmatic, Bayesian, adaptive, and platform randomized trials. These faculty will be expected to lead and publish high-impact research in top-tier biostatistics, clinical trial, and clinical research journals; support, prepare, and submit grant applications; and support ongoing randomized trials and trial methodology awards with Penn faculty and external partners. In these roles, they will serve as lead biostatisticians on multi-center randomized clinical trials and methodology projects and grants, develop and evaluate composite outcome measures and interpretation frameworks, apply causal inference methods to augment experimental data interpretation, and provide independent statistical expertise and leadership to research teams."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190631": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Gastrointestinal Surgery (AC track)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of minimally-invasive gastrointestinal surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Surgery or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of fellows, residents and medical students rotating on the GI Surgery service. Clinical responsibilities may include in- and out-patient clinical care of general and gastrointestinal surgery patients – especially within the foregut and hernia realms. This position will be housed at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Preference will be given to candidates possessing fellowship training in minimally-invasive surgery and who possess robotic surgery skills. Advanced endoscopic skills are also welcomed."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194819": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Gastrointestinal Surgery at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of minimally-invasive gastrointestinal surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Surgery or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of fellows, residents and medical students rotating on the GI Surgery service. Clinical responsibilities may include in- and out-patient clinical care of general and gastrointestinal surgery patients – especially within the foregut and hernia realms. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include basic science or clinical studies in the field of gastrointestinal surgery. This position will be housed at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Preference will be given to candidates possessing fellowship training in minimally-invasive surgery and who possess robotic surgery skills. Advanced endoscopic skills are also welcomed."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185978": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Inpatient Psychiatry at HUP Cedar and PAH - AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of assessment and treatment of acute psychiatric conditions, including depression, mania, psychosis, anxiety, and suicidality. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology Board Certification or Eligibility is required. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical supervision of medical students, psychiatry residents, and nurse practitioner students in provision of hospital-based psychiatric care; didactic teaching of psychiatry residents in topics related to hospital-based psychiatric care. Clinical responsibilities may include serving as an attending on a hospitalist team for the psychiatric inpatient units at Pennsylvania Hospital and the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania - Cedar Avenue. Clinical effort will be distributed across weeks of full-time on-unit service, weekend rounding, and off-unit tasks that support clinical care. Attendings will serve as the leader of a multi-disciplinary treatment team, including social workers, nurses, and mental health technicians, with primary responsibility for psychiatric assessment, treatment, and disposition. Attendings may also have opportunities to provide care in Penn's psychiatric crisis centers and/or outpatient clinics. This position will have no mandatory call responsibilities, but attendings will have the option of compensated, voluntary call."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158756": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Medicine in Translational Medicine and Human Genetics - Clinician Educator Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Translational Medicine and Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Translational Medicine and Human Genetics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician-educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of genomic medicine and/or genetics counseling. Applicants must have a PhD and/or MD degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include engaging in funded research involving human genetics, genomic medicine, implementation science in genomics, return of actionable genomic results, or ethical/legal/social implications (ELSI) of genomics research. Evidence of scholarship is required in the Clinician Educator track. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching genetic counseling students, medical students, residents, and fellows, serving as a research mentor to MSGC students and genetic counselors, and potentially participating in the leadership of Penn’s MSGC program. Clinical responsibilities may include seeing patients in the outpatient setting and/or an inpatient consult service. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158752": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Medicine in Translational Medicine and Human Genetics - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Translational Medicine and Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Translational Medicine and Human Genetics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. and/or Ph.D degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students within the clinical setting and participation as an active member of one or more Penn graduate groups. Clinical responsibilities may include seeing patients in the outpatient setting and as an attending on an inpatient consult service. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing an innovative, independent research program in human genetics, genomic medicine, and/or translational science that will attract and maintain extramural funding from various sources. The successful candidate will be expected to publish scholarship in peer reviewed journals. The Division of Translational Medicine and Human Genetics comprises clinical and research faculty with diverse investigative interests and close affiliations with clinical departments at Penn Medicine as well as the neighboring Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Wistar Institute. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158760": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Medicine – AC in Translational Medicine and Human Genetics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Translational Medicine and Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Translational Medicine and Human Genetics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents and fellows within the clinical setting. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients in the outpatient setting and as an attending physician on an inpatient consult service. There may be an opportunity for patient-oriented research in human genetics or genomic medicine, but this is not required. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174289": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Neurology and Pediatrics, Clinician Educator Track at CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and oversight of observers, medical students, residents and fellows in a clinical setting, and formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient service and outpatient clinic. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing an innovative, independent research program that will attract and maintain extramural funding from governmental agencies, private foundations, and industry."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178117": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Neurology and Pediatrics, Tenure Track at CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, neurology residents, neurology fellows, and graduate students. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient and inpatient consultations, workup, diagnosis, and treatment of Neurology patients. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative research programs; co-supervision of postdoctoral fellows, students, and research staff; coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators; and participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181298": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Neurology, General and NIOM, AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Neurophysiologic Intraoperative Monitoring (NIOM). Applicants must have at least one year in an accredited Neurophysiology fellowship. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board eligible in Neurology and Neurophysiology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents, fellows, technicians NIOM and comprehensive General Neurology. Clinical responsibilities may include Neurophysiologic Intraoperative Monitoring and General inpatient and outpatient Neurology."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/170586": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Neurosurgery Academic Clinician Track, at the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania, specializing in brain tumor surgery",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurosurgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurosurgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of brain tumor surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board eligible or certified. Teaching responsibilities may include the education of medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include the neurosurgical management of brain tumors and oversight of the multi-disciplinary care of brain tumor patients with a particular focus on gliomas. Clinical research or scholarship opportunities may include participation in translational and/or clinical trials."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169711": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Neurosurgery, Clinician Educator Track, at the University of Pennsylvania, Perelman School of Medicine, specializing in brain tumor surgery and research",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurosurgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurosurgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of brain tumor surgery and brain tumor research. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicant must be board eligible or certified. Teaching responsibilities may include the education of medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include the neurosurgical management of brain tumors and oversight of the multi-disciplinary care of brain tumor patients, including clinical trials, with a particular focus on gliomas. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include translational and/or basic research in brain tumors, with funding from the National Institutes of Health and other federal funding agencies as PI."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184979": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Neurosurgery, Tenure Track in the Department of Neurosurgery, Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania, specializing in Neuro-Oncology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurosurgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurosurgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of neuro-immuno-oncology, cancer neuroscience, and genomics. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include mentoring undergraduate and graduate students and postdoctoral fellows, as well as providing formal lectures within the department and PSOM. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing both collaborative and independent research programs focused on primary and metastatic brain cancers; coordinating NIH-funded research initiatives independently and in partnership with local, national, and international collaborators; and actively contributing to the preparation of grant applications, progress reports, and scientific manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164613": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Otorhinolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery, Generalist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Otorhinolaryngology - Head and Neck Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Otorhinolaryngology: Head and Neck Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicant must be board certified or board eligible in otolaryngology. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities. Clinical responsibilities may include the surgical and clinical care of otorhinolaryngology patients."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172678": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Otorhinolaryngology: Head and Neck Surgery, Sleep/Laryngology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Otorhinolaryngology - Head and Neck Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Otorhinolaryngology: Head and Neck Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of laryngeal, airway, esophageal and sleep disorders. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Candidates must be fellowship-trained in either laryngology or sleep medicine and be board certified or board eligible in their respective specialty. Teaching responsibilities may include medical student and resident education, as well as delivering formal lectures on an annual basis. Clinical responsibilities may include the medical and surgical management of patients with laryngeal, pharyngo-esophageal, airway, and sleep-related pathologies with clinical duties performed at Pennsylvania Hospital and the Veteran’s Affairs Medical Center of Philadelphia (VAMC)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183046": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Plastic Surgery at Pennsylvania Hospital (AC Track)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of plastic surgery and reconstructive microsurgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidate must be board-certified by the American Board of Plastic Surgery (ABPS). Teaching responsibilities may include education of medical students, residents and microsurgical fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient, inpatient, and surgical care of patients. Responsibilities may include the full spectrum of plastic surgery with a primary focus on breast reconstruction. Position will be based in Philadelphia at Pennsylvania Hospital with potential outpatient sites in suburban NJ or PA. Candidates must have completed an ACGME-accredited plastic surgery residency program and a microsurgical fellowship."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194163": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychiatry in Behavioral Sleep Medicine - Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Philadelphia VA Medical Center (PVAMC) and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of behavioral sleep medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include training and supervision of clinical psychology, trainees and staff psychologists in behavioral sleep medicine topics. Clinical responsibilities may include provision of CBT for insomnia and other behavioral sleep services."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190986": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Urologic Surgery (AC Track)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of outpatient and inpatient urology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Urology or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include instruction of medical students and urology residents. Clinical responsibilities may include surgical and non-surgical care of patients (male and female) with general urological complaints. The clinical practice for this position will be primarily based at Pennsylvania Hospital, with potential coverage responsibilities extending to the South Jersey satellite locations."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193831": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Urology (AC Track)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of urology, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS). Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must have done fellowship in URPS after finishing urology residency and be certified by the American Board of Urology or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include instruction of medical students, urology residents, and URPS fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include surgical and non-surgical care of patients (male and female) with URPS-related urological complaints such as lower urinary tract symptoms, urinary incontinence, pelvic organ prolapse, pelvic floor disorders, etc. The clinical practice for this position will be housed primarily at the Pennsylvania Hospital."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193814": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Urology (CE Track)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of urology, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS). Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must have done fellowship in URPS after finishing urology residency. They must also be certified by the American Board of Urology or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include instruction of medical students, urology residents, and URPS fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include surgical and non-surgical care of patients (male and female) with URPS-related urological complaints such as lower urinary tract symptoms, urinary incontinence, pelvic organ prolapse, pelvic floor disorders, etc. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include pursuit of scientific discovery in urology. Various research paths are acceptable including, but not limited to, basic science or laboratory research, translational research, clinical research, clinical trials, and outcomes research. The clinical practice for this position will be housed primarily at the Pennsylvania Hospital."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188800": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Urology at CHOP Surgery",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pediatric urology, with a focus on minimally invasive surgery and major urologic surgical reconstruction. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Urology or eligible for such certification. All candidates must have completed training through an ACGME-approved pediatric urology fellowship. Teaching responsibilities may include instruction of medical students and residents as well as pediatric urology fellows in the operating room, outpatient clinic, and on inpatient rounds. Clinical responsibilities may include care for urologic patients, including open, endoscopic, and minimally invasive surgery. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include studies in areas of clinical outcomes and urologic reconstruction. A strong research background and demonstrated potential for developing independent research will be preferred, and the successful candidate will be expected to publish in peer-reviewed journals."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/166717": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor on the Academic Clinician Track at the Center for Treatment and Study of Anxiety (CTSA)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of cognitive behavioral therapy for anxiety related disorders. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Psychologist's license in Pennsylvania and license eligibility in New Jersey are required. Teaching responsibilities may include supervision of in-house trainees in cognitive behavioral therapy for anxiety related disorders. Clinical responsibilities may include provision of direct clinical services across the lifespan for patients with anxiety related disorders. Opportunities for involvement in publications and research involvement as independent evaluators or study therapists may become available."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184538": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor on the Academic Clinician Track in Cognitive Behavioral Therapy for Anxiety Disorders",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of cognitive behavioral therapy for anxiety-related disorders. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical teaching for psychiatry residents, psychology post-doctoral fellows, psychology interns, and psychology externs. Clinical responsibilities may include direct clinical care for patients with anxiety-related disorders across the lifespan."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178286": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Position, Academic Clinician Track - Division of Sleep Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Sleep Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Sleep Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Candidates should be board certified or board eligible in Sleep Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include training residents and fellows in addition to precepting medical students and other trainees in the field of Sleep Medicine. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include performing comprehensive evaluations and management of patients with sleep disorders including interpreting polysomnograms, multiple sleep latency tests, and home sleep apnea tests; attending in the sleep disorders clinic, and sleep telemedicine program. Clinical responsibilities will be at the primary outpatient site of the Sleep Division at the University of Pennsylvania as well as Pennsylvania Hospital. Selected applicants will have demonstrated excellent qualifications in education and clinical care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/167619": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Pulmonary & Sleep Medicine – AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Pulmonary Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Pulmonary Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification in Pediatric Pulmonary or Pediatric Sleep Medicine are required. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture and medical education opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include seeing patients in the inpatient and outpatient settings. There may also be opportunities to participate in quality improvement initiatives and clinical or translational research. Research is not required for faculty on the AC Track however the successful candidate may collaborate/contribute to research. The division provides care to children with a diverse spectrum of pulmonary and sleep disorders including through the Cystic Fibrosis Center, Sleep Center, Technology Dependence Center, Asthma Program, Lung Transplant Program, Thoracic Insufficiency Center, Bronchoscopy/Aerodigestive Program, and clinics for children with chronic lung disease of infancy, Interstitial Lung Disease, Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia, and other rare lung diseases."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/167620": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Pulmonary & Sleep Medicine – CE or Tenure Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Pulmonary Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of P ulmonary Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or eq uivalent degree. Board certification in Pediatric Pulmonary or Pediatric Sleep Medicine is required. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include seeing patients in the inpatient and outpatient settings. There may also be opportunities to participate in quality improvement initiatives, medical education, and clinical or translational research. The division provides care to children with a diverse spectrum of pulmonary and sleep disorders including through the Cystic Fibrosis Center, Sleep Center, Technology Dependence Center, Asthma Program, Lung Transplant Program, Thoracic Insufficiency Center, Bronchoscopy/Aerodigestive Program, and clinics for children with chronic lung disease of infancy, Interstitial Lung Disease, Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia, and other rare lung diseases. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative and independent research programs, an outstanding record of research productivity, and participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178470": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Tenure Track Position — Children's Hospital of Philadelphia Cardiovascular Institute and the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of fundamental mechanistic or translational research relevant to pediatric cardiovascular disease, including but not limited to: cardiac development and regeneration, immune or metabolic origins of cardiovascular disease, heritable cardiac diseases such as cardiac channelopathies, cardiomyopathies, and aortopathies/vasculopathies, precision- and genetics-based therapeutics, bioengineering approaches and novel technologies for cardiovascular research and therapeutics. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include participating in graduate and/or medical student education; mentoring trainees at multiple career stages; presenting lectures and leading didactic sessions as appropriate. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient and inpatient consults and attending duties for qualified clinician-scientists. Clinical responsibilities are not applicable for basic scientist candidates. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing and maintaining a scientifically impactful independent research program that has relevance to pediatric heart and vascular disease; sustaining significant extramural funding. Candidates will be members of the newly established CHOP Cardiovascular Institute (CVI). The successful candidate will develop an independent, extramurally supported research program focused on fundamental or translational questions relevant to pediatric heart and vascular biology and disease. CHOP is a world class leader in the delivery of pediatric care, research, and training pediatric leaders of the future. The pediatric cardiology and cardiac surgery groups within the CHOP Cardiac Center are well-known as innovative leaders in the care of children with congenital forms of heart and vascular disease, and in the development of breakthrough therapeutics and diagnostics. Recently, the CHOP CVI was launched with the primary mission of establishing a world-class comprehensive research center that spans basic discovery to translation and clinical implementation relevant to pediatric heart and vascular diseases. The CHOP CVI will be linked in collaborative partnership with the Penn CVI, home to renowned basic and translational scientists. This partnership will provide support and infrastructure for discovery, translational, and clinical research aimed at cardiovascular health and disease across the entire lifespan. Candidates need to demonstrate potential for independent, high-impact scholarship; vision and commitment for leveraging the rich and uniquely collaborative and translational environment at CHOP and Penn to tackle fundamental questions in pediatric cardiology. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine or an academic department in the Perelman School of Medicine that is consistent with the scientific expertise of the successful candidate. Competitive start-up package and laboratory space, protected time for the establishment of an independent research program, and institutional mentoring and career-development resources will be provided. The CHOP CVI is a newly launched, comprehensive research center spanning basic discovery through translation and clinical implementation for pediatric cardiovascular health. CHOP CVI is in close partnership with many key CHOP/Penn Institutes and Centers, including the Penn Cardiovascular Institute, CHOP Cardiac Center, CHOP Center for Mitochondrial and Epigenomic Medicine, and Penn Institute for Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178681": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Tenure Track – Artificial Intelligence in Medicine (CHOP)",
      "description": "Posted: Dec 15, 2025 Deadline: Dec 15, 2027 Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include participating in graduate and/or medical student education; mentoring trainees at multiple career stages; presenting lectures and leading didactic sessions as appropriate. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing and maintaining an independent, extramurally funded research program. The faculty search is in the field of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Medicine. We are particularly interested in candidates who creatively develop and apply novel AI technologies to drive biological discoveries and medical innovations. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: foundational AI models for genetic, multi-omic, imaging, and EHR data; multimodal AI approaches enabling precision diagnostics and therapeutics; and generative AI for biomolecule engineering and design. AI researchers who combine computational and experimental research programs are also welcome to apply. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine. The position is affiliated with the Center for Computational and Genomic Medicine (CCGM) at the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP). CCGM, a CHOP Research Institute Center of Emphasis, is housed in the state-of-the-art Colket Translational Research Building. A generous recruitment package and lab space will be provided, together with excellent institutional and core research resources. The recruitment is part of a campus-wide initiative to promote AI innovations and research-driven precision medicine."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180525": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Academic Specialist in Ob/Gyn & Complex Family Planning",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track.  Expertise is required in the specific area of general obstetrics and gynecology and complex family planning. Successful candidates will primarily report to the Academic Specialist Division and secondarily engage with the Complex Family Planning Division. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must have successfully completed an ACGME-accredited residency and be board certified/eligible by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology in complex family planning. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical training and supervision of medical students, Ob/Gyn residents and Complex Family Planning fellows in both the hospital and outpatient settings and participation in formal teaching curriculum. Clinical responsibilities may include providing full-scope obstetrics and gynecology and complex family planning in the ambulatory and inpatient settings. Excellent clinical and interpersonal skills are required. A commitment to resident and medical student education is required. The successful candidate would join Penn Medicine Division of Academic Specialists and the Division of Complex Family Planning. The Division of Academic Specialists is a group of obstetricians and gynecologists, advanced practice providers including midwives, in a faculty practice at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. The Division of Complex Family Planning is a group of Complex Family Planning subspecialists based at Penn Medicine University City and Penn Medicine Washington Square. Opportunities may be available to participate in quality improvement, clinical research and medical education projects. The successful candidate will receive fully-covered malpractice insurance and practice in a supportive environment that provides professional and personal fulfillment and career-long learning."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193000": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – CE Track - Assistant Director of Clinical Immunology Laboratory - Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of clinical immunology and flow cytometry. A strong preference will be given to applicants with experience in innovation and clinical assay development. Applicants must have an M.D. and/or Ph.D degree. MD applicants must be board certified in Clinical Pathology (AP/CP or CP) and eligible for medical licensure in Pennsylvania. PhD applicants must have appropriate fellowship or postgraduate training and be board eligible or certified by DMLI(ASCP), certified by ABMLI, or hold other appropriate qualifications for leadership in a high-complexity clinical laboratory. Teaching responsibilities may include training Immunology and Rheumatology clinical fellows, residents, medical and graduate students, and clinical laboratory scientists. Clinical responsibilities may include assisting in oversight of the Clinical Immunology Laboratory, clinical test interpretation and consultation, quality assurance, and development and implementation of new diagnostic assays. The candidate will support testing for primary immunodeficiencies/inborn errors of immunity, immune dysregulation disorders, and other complex immune-mediated conditions. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include translational and collaborative work in clinical immunology, immune dysregulation, functional immune testing, emerging immunotherapies, and innovative laboratory diagnostics. The successful candidate will serve as Assistant Director of the Clinical Immunology Laboratory. Demonstrated expertise in flow cytometry and advanced clinical test development is strongly preferred. Experience with functional immune assays and testing related to immunodeficiencies, emerging immunotherapies or cellular therapies is desirable. The candidate will contribute to the development and expansion of the laboratory's diagnostic portfolio."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192743": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, AC of Radiation Oncology [Breast & Gynecologic Service]",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiation Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiation Oncology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Required certifications include being Board Eligible or Board Certified in Radiation Oncology by the American Board of Radiology. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching, training, and mentoring of radiation oncology residents, medical physics residents, medical physics graduate students, and visiting physics residents or trainees from other institutions and countries. In addition to these core responsibilities, this role encompasses both formal and informal teaching engagements, including active participation in resident didactic series, serving in capacities both as a lecturer and as an in-person discussant. Clinical responsibilities may include specialized gynecologic brachytherapy. This role will encompass the delivery of high-dose rate (HDR) brachytherapy for the treatment of cervical, uterine, and vaginal cancers, utilizing state-of-the-art, accredited technology. While the clinical focus of this position is rooted in the management of gynecologic malignancies, it will include care of other patients with breast cancer. The scope of clinical practice will extend beyond brachytherapy to include a comprehensive array of treatment modalities, such as conventional radiation therapy, stereotactic body radiotherapy (SBRT), proton therapy, photon and proton reirradiation, and total body irradiation (TBI), ensuring the highest standard of individualized, multidisciplinary care for all patients served. Penn Radiation Oncology is dedicated to a three-part mission of excellence in patient care, basic and translational research, and the education of residents and students. We are committed to delivering excellence in every area and as such we steadfastly believe that \"Excellence is Standard.\" Penn Radiation Oncology is one of the most comprehensive radiation oncology programs in the world. The outstanding faculty and staff, combined with Penn’s extensive collection of advanced technology, gives patients access to nearly every treatment option available for their cancer. The broad range of radiation treatments available include External-Beam Radiation Therapy (Proton Therapy, Image-guided radiation therapy (IGRT), Intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT), Photodynamic therapy (PDT), Total body irradiation (TBI), Total skin electron beam therapy (TSEBT)), and Stereotactic Radiosurgery (CyberKnife, Edge, Gamma Knife, TrueBeam), as well as Internal Radiation Therapy (brachytherapy, MammoSite). The brachytherapy suite at the Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine is a state-of-the-art, dedicated outpatient facility specializing in high-dose rate (HDR) treatments for prostate, gynecologic, and head/neck cancers. It features advanced in-room imaging, including BK ultrasound and fluoroscopy, and is located next to MRI services for precise 3D treatment planning. With the Abramson Cancer Center of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Radiation Oncology provides patient care at the Ruth and Raymond Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine and fourteen community-based sites."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169829": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, AC Track, Adult Congenital Heart Disease",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Cardiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Cardiology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Adult congenital heart disease, congenital echocardiography. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification or board eligible in Adult Congenital Heart Disease is required. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient adult congenital heart disease clinic, inpatient adult congenital heart disease consult service, congenital echocardiogram interpretation and reporting. Research is not a requirement of faculty on the AC track. Candidates may participate in opportunities involving collaborative clinical research and research mentorship for trainees."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172187": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, AC Track, Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics and/or Neurodevelopmental Disabilities. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include developmental assessments and providing follow up care in an outpatient setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/170909": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, AC Track, Division of Allergy and Immunology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Allergy and Immunology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Allergy/Immunology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Board certified/eligible in Allergy and Immunology. Teaching responsibilities may include high quality teaching of CHOP fellows and residents. Clinical responsibilities may include developing a regional referral base in Allergy and Immunology. Practice sites include CHOP community pediatric specialty care offices in Exton, PA, Lancaster, PA or a combination of locations. Inpatient call is rotated."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/160383": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, AC Track, Infectious Diseases (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Infectious Diseases Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Infectious Diseases in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include high quality teaching of CHOP fellows and residents, as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include providing coverage in one or more of three inpatient consultation services, one service focused on children with general infectious diseases, one dedicated to the care of immunocompromised hosts, one attending-NP service currently focused on NICU and Ortho patients. Additional responsibilities may also include seeing patients in the Division’s busy outpatient clinical practice. In addition to our General Infectious Diseases Clinic, we have dedicated “partner-clinics” to provide collaborative outpatient care to outpatients with other underlying conditions, including malignancies, bone marrow and organ transplantation and cystic fibrosis. As CHOP expands its footprint (i.e., King of Prussia Hospital, potential sites in NJ) and the Division of Infectious Diseases partners with outside organizations, some local travel may be required. Administrative or research responsibilities (i.e., global heath, clinical trials, fellowship leadership and/or education, etc) may be available depending on the needs of the division and candidate interests. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174358": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, AC Track, Pediatric Rehabilitation Physiatrist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Rehabilitation Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Rehabilitation Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of diagnosing and treating various conditions requiring rehabilitation. Familiarity with an electronic medical record is desirable. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be Board-certified/eligible in Pediatric Rehabilitation. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching rotating medical students, residents and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Participation is encouraged in regional, national and international meetings. Clinical responsibilities may include Pediatric Rehabilitation Outpatient clinic and inpatient consultations in acute care setting as well as attending on the inpatient rehabilitation unit and sharing in on-call coverage. Opportunity to participate in patient-oriented research exists."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168196": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician - Division of Pediatric Nephrology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Nephrology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Nephrology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient/consultation services and outpatient nephrology services including transplant clinic, fellows clinic, several multidisciplinary clinic opportunities, and dialysis. Outpatient nephrology services are located at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia-Main Campus and satellite locations in Pennsylvania and New Jersey. The Division of Nephrology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania is at the forefront of clinical care, teaching, and research. The Division is comprised of 15 faculty members and 9 clinical fellows, in addition to our team of nurses, administrators, social workers, dieticians, and research staff. Preference would be 3-5 years Nephrology Attending experience, but not required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181536": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician - Obstetrics and Gynecology including Pediatric and Adolescent Gynecology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania and the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of obstetrics and gynecology and pediatric/adolescent gynecology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology and have completed a fellowship in Pediatric and Adolescent Gynecology or have significant experience in Pediatric and Adolescent Gynecology, with an ABOG-focused practice designation in Pediatric and Adolescent Gynecology. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical training and supervision of medical students and residents and participation in formal teaching curriculum. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient prenatal, pediatric, adolescent and adult gynecology care, labor and delivery coverage, and pediatric and adult gynecologic surgery. The successful candidate would join a group of full-time obstetricians and gynecologists, advanced practice providers including midwives in a faculty practice at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, and join the Division of Adolescent Medicine at the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia. Excellent clinical and interpersonal skills are required. A commitment to resident and medical student education is required. The successful candidate will receive fully covered malpractice insurance and practice in a supportive environment that provides professional and personal fulfillment and career-long learning."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189779": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician in Medical Physics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiation Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiation Oncology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of adaptive therapy, advanced imaging, scripting, or FLASH (ultra-high dose rate) therapy will be preferred. Demonstration of clinical translation of research/new technology is essential. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. ABR board eligibility in therapeutic radiological physics is required, and ABR board certification is preferred or expected within the first two years. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching and training of radiation oncology residents, medical physics residents, medical physics graduate students, etc. Clinical responsibilities may include supporting a full range of clinical physics activities, such as linac-based radiation therapy, brachytherapy, proton therapy, etc. at the Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine and satellite facilities. Penn Radiation Oncology is dedicated to a three-part mission of excellence in patient care, basic and translational research, and the education of residents and medical students. Penn Medicine delivers a broad range of radiation therapy services to its patients, including intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT), high-dose-rate (HDR) brachytherapy, partial breast irradiation, and stereotactic radiosurgery (SRS/SBRT using Gamma Knife /Varian Linac). Patients will also have access to proton therapy at the Roberts Proton Therapy Center, housing the largest proton therapy facility in the USA, comprising four gantry treatment rooms and one fixed beam room. Two additional proton rooms with FLASH capabilities are slated to open in mid 2027 at the Pennsylvania Presbyterian Hospital. Penn is a world leader in proton FLASH research with the first conformal FLASH clinical trial planned this year. Penn Radiation Oncology is not only committed to delivering high-quality radiation therapy, but also to enhancing and improving upon the patient experience by providing a full range of clinical services. An integral component of the Abramson Cancer Center at the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Radiation Oncology, can draw upon the center's full resources to deliver the best possible overall care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194444": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track, CHOP Division of Hematology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Hematology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Hematology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D., D.O., or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/eligible in Pediatrics or Internal Medicine and Hematology strongly preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include active and high-quality teaching opportunities with medical students, residents, fellows and APPs. Clinical responsibilities may include care for patients with a wide breadth of non-malignant hematologic disorders. Patient care responsibilities will involve both in- and outpatient services. There may also be opportunities to participate in quality improvement initiatives and clinical or translational research. Research is not required for faculty on the AC Track however the successful candidate may collaborate/contribute to research. Within the Division of Hematology, we have established clinical and research programs in hemostasis and thrombosis, platelet disorders, sickle cell disease, thalassemia, and bone marrow failure. These programs provide highly specialized multidisciplinary care with team members including social workers, nurses, physical therapists and psychologists. Our division includes 23 hematologists, 12 non-clinical investigators, 4 nurse practitioners and 17 fellows. We are a highly collaborative group who appreciate learning from each other and value clinical care that is thoughtful, thorough and compassionate."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188386": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track, Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Endocrinology and Diabetes Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include high quality teaching of CHOP fellows and residents as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient and outpatient endocrinology services. The Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes comprises nearly 30 faculty with diverse clinical and investigative interests and has clinical programs with nearly 30,000 outpatient visits yearly. Philadelphia is a vibrant city with a unique blend of modern high-rise office buildings and historic districts with centuries of old architecture. The area offers diverse outdoor opportunities, an open and exciting culture, and an outstanding quality of life."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176906": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track, Division of Human Genetics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Human Genetics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, and genetics fellows within the outpatient and inpatient clinical settings and giving clinical lectures to trainees. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching responsibilities. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient clinical care in one or more of the following specialties: clinical genetics, biochemical genetics, mitochondrial medicine, genomic medicine, and can be tailored to the applicants interest and our clinical needs."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161459": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track, Division of Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Neonatology and Newborn Services Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Neonatology & Newborn Services in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. , D.O. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board certified/eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine by the American Board of Pediatrics or in Internal Medicine for tenure and research tracks. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows as well as formal lecture opportunities within the Division and Department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical care and productivity in program development. Clinical care will be provided in the 100 bed Level IV Neonatal/Infant Intensive Care Unit at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and the 38 bed Level III NICU at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, as well as in the Neonatal Follow-Up Program. Duties also include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188682": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track, Human Genetics- Biochemical Geneticist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Human Genetics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of biochemical genetics, with experience or strong interest in mitochondrial disorders, and a commitment to advancing the diagnosis, treatment, and understanding of mitochondrial disorders. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification or board eligibility in Clinical Genetics and Genomics and Biochemical Genetics is required. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department, and mentorship of trainees in clinical genetics and biochemical/mitochondrial medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include providing expert clinical care for patients with biochemical and mitochondrial genetic disorders, collaborating with a multidisciplinary team of physicians, scientists, genetic counselors, and allied health professionals, and contributing to the development and delivery of innovative mitochondrial medicine program in the section of Metabolism and Therapeutic Genetics . Opportunities available to participate in collaborative and independent scholarly activities related to mitochondrial genetic disorders, including clinical research, quality improvement, and educational scholarship. The Division of Genetics and Genomics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania and The Children's Hospital of Philadelphia offers an exciting opportunity to join a world-class academic medical center with a strong commitment to excellence in patient care, education, and research. The successful candidate will join a highly respected group dedicated to advancing mitochondrial medicine within a vibrant environment that values discovery, teamwork, and compassionate patient care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185547": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track, Pediatric Health and Behavior Program/Pediatric Headache Program, CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pediatric psychology. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Completed internship and fellowship in pediatric psychology or clinical care psychology is required. Applicants must have a PA license in psychology. Teaching responsibilities may include supervising behavioral health trainees (including psychology externs and interns); giving lectures to trainees in psychology, psychiatry, and pediatrics; develop curricula. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient consultation and intervention to youth with a wide range of chronic medical conditions and medical traumatic stress within the Pediatric Health and Behavior Program. In addition to, providing outpatient consultation, assessment, and intervention services to youth diagnosed with pediatric chronic migraine and other headache disorders within the Pediatric Headache Program. About the Pediatric Health and Behavior Program (PHAB): an outpatient consultation and psychotherapy program for youth with a wide range of chronic medical conditions and traumatic injuries and their caregivers. PHAB staff includes psychologists, psychiatrists, and administrative staff who work closely together in the treatment of patients. Commonly referred patient populations include autoimmune conditions, neuromuscular disorders, neuroinflammatory disorders, brain injury, atopic diseases, and chronic kidney diseases. The pediatric psychologist will be encouraged and supported to identify a disease area of special interest on which to focus. The pediatric psychologist will collaborate closely with referring medical providers, as well as social workers and other outpatient staff. About the Pediatric Headache Program: provides a comprehensive interdisciplinary approach to the evaluation and treatment of chronic migraine and other headache related diagnoses. Evaluation of chronic migraine and other headache disorders includes a highly interdisciplinary model involving strong collaboration, followed by on-going treatment in the outpatient setting. The psychologist in the Pediatric Headache Program will work closely with the team, including physicians in Neurology, nurse practitioners, nurses, social worker, consultation with psychiatry staff when appropriate, and other team members to provide care and further develop the services provided within the Program. Founded in 1855, The Children's Hospital of Philadelphia is the nation's oldest hospital dedicated solely to the care of children. CHOP has a long-standing and continuing commitment to developing leaders in medicine and science, expanding the frontiers of pediatric care through novel research programs and translational research, and applying those advances to clinical care. The Children's Hospital of Philadelphia is the major provider of primary health care services for children of West and South Philadelphia, and a major tertiary referral center for the greater Delaware Valley area. The CHOP main campus includes inpatient, outpatient, research, and rehabilitation facilities in an interconnected complex of buildings. Annually, CHOP receives approximately 30,000 inpatient admissions, nearly 90,000 emergency room visits, and 1.2 million outpatient visits. CHOP's Delaware Valley Network is expansive, with over 40 locations and 16 Specialty Care Centers and Ambulatory Surgery Centers."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188042": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track, specializing in adult and pediatric complex spinal deformity in the Department of Neurosurgery",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurosurgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurosurgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of spine surgery with specialization in complex spinal deformity surgery, including specialized training in both adult and pediatric spine deformity. Candidates for this position must demonstrate professional and clinical focus in spinal deformity. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be ABNS certified or eligible. Training in a post-graduate spine fellowship is also required. Teaching responsibilities may include education and training of medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include specializing in the practice of complex spinal deformities in pediatric and adult patients. We are seeking candidates with demonstrated excellence in the areas of clinical care and education."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177118": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician – Sleep Center",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Pulmonary Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible in Sleep Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students from the University of Pennsylvania School of Medicine as well as residents and fellows from the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia. Teaching can take place in a variety of settings such as lecturing, small group, clinical and/or didactic sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the care of patients with sleep disorders in the Sleep Center and polysomnogram reading according to the needs of the Sleep Center."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179877": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, Cell Therapy and Transplant, Pediatric Oncology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Oncology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of clinical care directly related to patients with cancer and related disorders undergoing hematopoietic stem cell transplantation and/or receiving cellular immunotherapy. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board-certified in pediatric hematology/oncology (or equivalent). Teaching responsibilities may include didactic and clinical instruction of medical students, residents, fellows in pediatric hematology/oncology or related disciplines. Clinical responsibilities may include enrolling patients in clinical trials, and treating patients enrolled in clinical trials. Opportunities will be available to participate in clinical research related to the care of patients with cancer and related disorders undergoing hematopoietic stem cell transplantation and/or receiving cellular immunotherapy. At least two years of experience as an attending physician after completion of Pediatric Hematology/Oncology Fellowship training is required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168020": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, Division of GI, Hepatology and Nutrition",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of education and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/eligible in pediatric gastroenterology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents and fellows, and participating in family education days as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding outpatient, inpatient and procedural care at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and/or its satellites."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179439": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, General Cardiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Cardiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Cardiology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board Certified/Board Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic lectures to fellows, residents, medical students and nursing staff on topics in general cardiology. Experience in teaching is also required, including curriculum development, and innovative teaching materials. Clinical responsibilities may include Inpatient and Outpatient coverage of General Cardiology Service, Electrophysiology, Pulmonary Hypertension, Catheterization/Interventional Laboratory, Heart Failure/Heart Transplant, Echocardiography and Fetal Echocardiography at Main Hospital and satellite offices in Pennsylvania and New Jersey."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173554": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, General Pediatrics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - General Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of General Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of medical education, quality improvement, patient safety, health services research, clinical outcomes research, or medical informatics, is preferred. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible in Pediatrics. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of residents, fellows, and/or medical students. Clinical responsibilities may include care responsibilities on any of the inpatient and/or outpatient General Pediatrics services."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174414": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, General Pediatrics – Primary Care",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - General Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of General Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of medical education and primary care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible in Pediatrics. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of residents, fellows, and/or medical students. Clinical responsibilities may include care responsibilities in outpatient Primary Care. Experience in clinical teaching, quality, health services and outcomes, or medical informatics is preferred."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194079": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, General Pediatrics-Palliative Care",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - General Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of General Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Fellowship training, education and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be fellowship trained, board certified/eligible in hospice and palliative medicine and board eligibility or certification in Pediatrics or a Pediatric subspecialty as well as eligibility for Pennsylvania licensure. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of residents, fellows, and/or medical students. Clinical responsibilities may include demonstrated excellence in the bedside clinical teaching of residents, fellows, and/or medical students. Enthusiasm and dedication to educating our residents and students is highly valued in our department."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195072": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, Neuro-Oncology, Pediatric Oncology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Oncology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of clinical care of patients with central nervous systems tumors, neurofibromatosis and retinoblastoma. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Required board-certification/eligibility in pediatric hematology/oncology; completion of a dedicated neuro-oncology fellowship. The candidate must have at least two years of experience as an attending physician after completion of fellowship training. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic and clinical instruction of medical students, pediatric residents and hospitalists, and fellows in pediatric hematology/oncology or related disciplines. Clinical responsibilities may include caring for patients on the neuro-oncology inpatient service and in the outpatient neuro-oncology clinic, identifying and enrolling eligible patients in clinical trials, and treating patients enrolled in clinical trials."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175419": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, Pediatric Adolescent Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Adolescent Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Adolescent Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/eligible in Pediatrics, Internal Medicine or Addiction Medicine, and Adolescent Medicine strongly preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in clinical education of medical students, residents, and fellows as a member of the Craig-Dalsimer Division of Adolescent Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient and outpatient primary and specialty care in Adolescent Medicine at The Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Multiple sites of practice are available including a primary care practice, specialty care satellite locations and inpatient units and a behavioral health hospital. Unique opportunities are available for applicants interested in an expanding Eating Disorder program. Opportunities to participate in clinical trials or other clinic-based research projects may be available related to continuous quality improvement, health services, health disparities, resiliency, STDs/HIV, pregnancy prevention, substance use, gender, eating disorders, weight regulation, depression, and suicide. Research is not a requirement for AC Track faculty."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171174": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, Pediatric Dermatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - General Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of General Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of education and clinical care.  Proficiency and experience in quality, health services and outcomes are desired for this position. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible in Dermatology and Pediatric Dermatology. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of residents, fellows, and/or medical students. Clinical responsibilities may include providing dermatologic care in the outpatient Pediatric Dermatology clinic and on the inpatient consult service."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176260": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician, Pediatric Sports Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - General Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of General Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of education and clinical care and MSK ultrasound. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible in Pediatrics and a certificate of Additional Qualification in Sports Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of residents, fellows, and/or medical students. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient sports medicine care sports musculoskeletal injuries including MSK ultrasound and ultrasound guided injections as well as concussion management. Experience in clinical and translational research in musculoskeletal injuries including MSK ultrasound, experience in quality, health services and outcomes is preferred."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168024": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, CE or Tenure Track, Division of  GI, Hepatology and Nutrition",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of e ducation, research, and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified in Pediatrics and/or Gastroenterology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents and fellows, and participating in family education days. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding outpatient, inpatient and procedural care at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and/or its satellites. Candidates must have a reputation as an excellent clinician. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include assisting with augmenting basic, translational and/or clinical research initiatives in liver disease, motility, bile duct development, gastrointestinal allergies, nutrition, inflammatory bowel disease and microbiome research. Evidence of scholarship is required. Clinician Educators are often involved in collaborative, can be independent research, that results in new discoveries/knowledge or extend/advances understanding of knowledge ultimately important to human health/disease. Tenure track faculty are most often involved in independent or innovative collaborative research that results in new discoveries/knowledge or extend/advances understanding of knowledge ultimately important to human health/disease. Additional information about PSOM faculty tracks can be found here: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/assets/user-content/documents/Academic%20Review/COAP/PSOMFacultyTrackDescriptions.pdf"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175422": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, CE Track, Division of Adolescent Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Adolescent Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Adolescent Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/eligible in Pediatrics,  Internal Medicine or Addiction Medicine and Adolescent Medicine strongly preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include inpatient and/or outpatient clinical and teaching responsibilities. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient and/or outpatient primary and specialty care in Adolescent Medicine at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and participate in clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows as a member of the Craig-Dalsimer Division of Adolescent Medicine. Multiple sites of practice are available including a primary care practice, specialty care satellite locations and inpatient units and a behavioral health hospital. Expectations will be to develop and lead a clinical research program in Adolescent Medicine and Young Adult Health funded by career development and/or independent research funding. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include focusing on adolescent or young adult health research in areas such as parent-teen relationships and health, eating disorders, STI and HIV care/prevention, sexual/gender minority youth, substance use, health disparities, and/or medical education. Opportunities for collaborative clinical research are available related to education, continuous quality improvement, health services, health disparities, resiliency, STIs/HIV, pregnancy prevention, smoking, substance use, gender, eating disorders, weight regulation, depression and suicide. We are seeking candidates with a strong record of clinical research productivity and scholarship demonstrating a national reputation."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193123": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, CE Track, Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Endocrinology and Diabetes Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified in Pediatric Endocrinology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of CHOP residents and fellows as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical and translational research in areas such as type 2 diabetes, obesity and metabolic syndrome, type 1 diabetes, cystic fibrosis-related diabetes, neuroendocrine disorders and other endocrine diseases. The Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes comprises nearly 30 faculty with diverse clinical and investigative interests and has clinical programs with nearly 30,000 outpatient visits yearly. Philadelphia is a vibrant city with a unique blend of modern high-rise office buildings and historic districts with centuries of old architecture. The area offers diverse outdoor opportunities, an open and exciting culture and an outstanding quality of life."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188474": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, CE Track, Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes, Pediatric Thyroid Center",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Endocrinology and Diabetes Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree and be board certified in Pediatric Endocrinology with a desire to subspecialize in pediatric thyroidology. Teaching responsibilities may include high quality teaching of CHOP fellows and residents as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Outpatient clinical obligations include general thyroid clinic, a multidisciplinary PTEN Hamartoma Tumor Syndrome Clinic, an Advanced Thyroid Cancer Therapeutics Clinic, and general endocrinology clinic. The Thyroid Center is equipped with point-of-care ultrasound (POCUS) machines to perform bedside head/neck ultrasound in the outpatient clinic setting and the applicant is expected to become proficient in performance and interpretation of POCUS. A multidisciplinary tumor board is conducted monthly with collaborators from cytology (Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania), pathology, radiology, and surgery. Clinic locations are in CHOP Main (University Place, Philadelphia), Voorhees NJ Subspecialty Center, and Chalfont PA Subspecialty Center. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical and/or translational research in thyroid disease, including congenital or acquired thyroid disease, thyroid nodules, thyroid cancer, and thyroid cancer predisposition syndromes. The Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes comprises more than 30 faculty with diverse clinical and investigative interests and has clinical programs with nearly 30,000 outpatient visits yearly. The Pediatric Thyroid Center was established in 2013 and is fully staffed with dedicated administrative support, nursing (RN and NP) support, and both clinical and translational research programs. Philadelphia is a vibrant city with a unique blend of modern high-rise office buildings and historic districts with centuries of old architecture. The area offers diverse outdoor opportunities, an open and exciting culture and an outstanding quality of life."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161305": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, CE Track, Pediatric Rehabilitation Physiatrist (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Rehabilitation Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Rehabilitation Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Pediatric Rehabilitation Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board-certified/eligible in Pediatric Rehabilitation Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities (including journal club) within the division. Clinical responsibilities may include up to 16 weeks as the attending on service for acute inpatient rehabilitation. Responsibilities while on service will include daily patient visits as well as directing weekly team conferences and family team meetings as indicated. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative and independent research programs related to pediatric rehabilitation, co-supervision of trainees and research staff, coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national and international collaborators, and participation in writing grants, reports and manuscripts. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175302": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Emergency Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Emergency Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. ABEM certified or board eligible. Teaching responsibilities may include bedside teaching to medical students, residents, and fellows. Additional teaching responsibilities include lectures, journal clubs, case conferences, simulation teaching, small group discussions, and other formats. Dedication to teaching is highly valued in our department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing emergency medical care to patients presented to the emergency department at HUP Spruce, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, HUP Cedar, ED Observation Unit and Pennsylvania Hospital. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include opportunities to work across departments and schools (there are 6 STEM schools on campus) on multidisciplinary projects.  Independent research is a key component for success in this position and there is a mandatory promotion probationary period that requires evidence of significant scholarship.  Candidates with post-residency research methodology training or fellowship training may have an advantage in meeting the requirements of this track. A reduced clinical schedule is initially available for this position with the expectation that after an introductory period, there will be independent funding to support the clinical reduction. Mentoring is provided and teamwork is encouraged and valued. The Department of Emergency Medicine manages emergency services across any of the sites listed above with a combined annual emergency department census of 145,000 visits. Each site has a unique, diverse, highly acute patient population consisting of local and referral patients. Additionally, the Department collaborates with the Emergency Departments at Lancaster General Hospital, Chester County Hospital, and Princeton Medical Center. Emergency Medicine has a 4 year, highly successful, academically oriented residency program with 56 residents, multiple fellowships, and several nationally acclaimed research programs. There are over 120 faculty across the academic sites and there are close academic affiliations and programmatic alliances with the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center. The Department has active collaborations with other University of Pennsylvania Centers and schools such as the Penn Medicine Center for Healthcare Innovation, Wharton Business School, Leonard Davis Institute for Health Care Economics, and the Center for Clinical Epidemiology, and Biostatistics, among others."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185614": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator or Tenure Track, Adolescent Medicine- HIV/AIDS Research",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Adolescent Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Adolescent Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Board certified/eligible in Pediatrics or Internal Medicine and Adolescent Medicine strongly preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include inpatient and/or outpatient clinical and teaching responsibilities. Clinical responsibilities may include Inpatient and/or outpatient primary and specialty care in Adolescent Medicine at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and participate in clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows as a member of the Craig-Dalsimer Division of Adolescent Medicine. Multiple sites of practice are available including a primary care practice, specialty care satellite locations and inpatient units at CHOP and a behavioral health hospital. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include Primary focus on adolescent or young adult health research relevant to HIV prevention or care, which may interface with related domains of STIs, sexual/gender minority youth, substance use, mental health, health disparities, parent-teen relationships, community-engaged research, and similar areas. While both tenure and clinician-educator track faculty conduct methodological and collaborative research, tenure track faculty focus primarily on independent, investigator driven research while clinician-educator track faculty focus primarily on collaboration.  Depending on the track, expectations will be to develop and lead a research program funded by career development and/or independent research funding. For more information about Perelman School of Medicine Faculty tracks please visit PSOM’s Faculty Career Development page. It is anticipated that this faculty member will be an active participant in the Penn CFAR research community, which provides extensive services and activities geared to advance HIV/AIDS research. We are seeking early career candidates with a strong record of research productivity and scholarship. Opportunities for collaborative clinical research are available related to education, continuous quality improvement, health services, health disparities, resiliency, STIs/HIV, pregnancy prevention, smoking, substance use, gender, eating disorders, weight regulation, depression and suicide."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183252": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator Track, in the Department of Neurosurgery, specializing in Stereotactic and Functional Neurosurgery",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurosurgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurosurgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of stereotactic and functional neurosurgery, including the surgical treatment of pain disorders, neuromodulation-based therapies, deep brain stimulation, and related stereotactic procedures. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Preferred applicant must be board certified or board eligible in Neurosurgery. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of medical students, residents, and fellows within the Department of Neurosurgery. Clinical responsibilities may include the full spectrum of stereotactic and functional neurosurgical procedures, with particular emphasis on pain surgery, neuromodulation therapies, and deep brain stimulation, within a high-volume academic practice. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include the development of an independent, federally funded research program aligned with the candidate’s clinical expertise and the broader research mission of the Department and the University of Pennsylvania. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to participate in and develop translational and clinical research initiatives in neuromodulation and circuit-based therapies. The Division of Stereotactic and Functional Neurosurgery at Penn is a nationally recognized program performing a high volume of neuromodulation and stereotactic procedures each year, with active clinical and translational research initiatives focused on circuit-based therapies for neurological and psychiatric disease. Faculty in the division collaborate closely with investigators across Penn’s neuroscience community, providing a highly collaborative environment for clinical innovation and translational discovery."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192472": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator, Autism, Depression, Transition to Adulthood – CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of autism spectrum disorder in the transition to adulthood age period and a focus on the measurement and treatment of co-occurring Depression. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be eligible for licensure in Pennsylvania. Teaching responsibilities may include supervising behavioral health trainees (including psychology externs, interns, and fellows) in clinical practice and research; giving lectures to trainees in psychology, psychiatry, neurology, and pediatrics. Clinical responsibilities may include assessment, intervention, and consultation services to patients in outpatient settings within the Department of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences, with a focus on patients presenting with concerns related to autism spectrum disorder and/or other neurodevelopmental conditions during the transition to adulthood age range (14 to 25 years). Research or scholarship responsibilities may include contributing to the growth of impactful and transformative research in pediatric health and equity, including a focus on autism spectrum disorder, co-occurring depression, psychometrics of mental health assessment tools, and community engaged science; data analysis using qualitative and advanced multivariate quantitative methods; manuscript preparation and dissemination of research findings. We are seeking applicants with training and experience working in clinical and research settings with autistic/neurodivergent adolescents and young adults and their families, with experience in supporting mental health to autistic adolescents and young adults transitioning to adulthood. The role involves providing comprehensive autism diagnostic evaluations, transition to adulthood evaluations, interventions supporting mental health and patient-centered outcomes for transition-to-adulthood aged autistic people, and active involvement in mental health research initiatives. The ideal candidate will have experience in leading mental health science and community engaged research initiatives."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161243": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator, Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics and/or Neurodevelopmental Disabilities. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include performing developmental and behavioral assessments and provide follow up care including pharmacologic treatment and brief behavioral interventions in an outpatient setting. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative and independent research programs related to developmental or behavioral aspects of pediatric care, the genetic or other etiologies of development and behavioral conditions, or the delivery of health services in the field. Other expectations include supervision of postdoctoral fellows, resident, students, and research staff, coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators, and participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171928": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator, Echocardiography- Pediatric Cardiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Cardiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Cardiology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Echocardiography. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board Certified/Board Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic lectures to fellows, residents, medical students and nursing staff on topics in general cardiology. Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Cardiology have a large fellowship program with active involvement of trainees within the pediatric echocardiography lab. Excellence in teaching is also required, including curriculum development, innovative teaching materials, and mentoring of junior faculty is also expected. Clinical responsibilities may include Inpatient and Outpatient coverage of General Cardiology Service, Fetal Echocardiography at Main Hospital and satellite offices in Pennsylvania and New Jersey. This will be a full-time imaging position with opportunities for additional clinical work in areas of outpatient, fetal cardiology or inpatient cardiology care depending on the candidate’s interest and expertise. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include excellent qualifications in research with established area of research concentration in pediatric echocardiography. The Pediatric Echocardiography Laboratory at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia is one of the largest academic pediatric labs in the country. With strong support of the Cardiac Center and hospital, the echocardiography section includes 30 dedicated Echo faculty covering inpatient and outpatient labs that perform over 40,000 studies per year. The CHOP Echo lab has advanced imaging cores including 3D/modelling, quality improvement, education, and research. There are strong stress echocardiography and contrast echo programs with opportunities for incoming faculty to partner and participate in these areas. Involvement in the robust research, education and quality cores of the CHOP echocardiography lab are strongly encouraged."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179437": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator, Pediatric Cardiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Cardiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Cardiology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board Certified/Board Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic lectures to fellows, residents, medical students and nursing staff on topics in general cardiology. Experience in teaching is also required, including curriculum development and innovative teaching materials. Clinical responsibilities may include Inpatient and Outpatient coverage of General Cardiology Service, Electrophysiology, Pulmonary Hypertension, Catheterization/Interventional Laboratory, Heart Failure/Heart Transplant, Echocardiography and Fetal Echocardiography at Main Hospital and staffing satellite offices in New Jersey and Pennsylvania. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing an area of research concentration in general cardiology. Preferred candidates will have excellent qualifications in research."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189003": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator, Pediatric Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Emergency Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree and be board-certified in Pediatric Emergency Medicine, or board-eligible. Teaching responsibilities may include participating in the clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows as a member of the Division of Emergency Medicine, mentoring of trainees (including fellows and graduate students) in area of applicant’s interest and mentoring of postdoctoral fellows, students, and fellows and supervision of research staff. Clinical responsibilities may include providing direct patient care in an Emergency Department in Philadelphia, PA that has an annual volume of over 100,000 visits. Clinical employment opportunities in Pediatric Emergency Medicine are also being offered at our clinical affiliate institutions; Virtua Voorhees, in Southern New Jersey, King of Prussia Pediatric Hospital in King of Prussia, PA and Christiana Care Health System in Newark, DE. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include include knowledge of current ED studies and participate in patient enrollment, as needed. Additional research responsibilities include establishing a portfolio of collaborative and independent research related to identified field of interest within Pediatric Emergency Medicine, serving as primary author and co-author for reports and manuscripts, serving as principal investigator and co-investigator on federal, state, and foundation grant efforts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174590": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator, Pediatric Oncology- Hematologic Malignancies Program",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Oncology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pediatric leukemia and lymphoma. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board-certified or board-eligible in pediatric hematology/oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic and clinical instruction of medical students, residents, post-doctoral fellows, instructors, and/or clinical research assistants and educational liaison with advanced practice providers. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient and outpatient care focused on children, adolescents, and young adults with hematologic malignancies at the Philadelphia University City Hospital and active involvement in fellowship training and mentoring. The ideal candidate will also have interests in early phase clinical trials of precision medicine therapeutics for children with relapsed/refractory or high-risk leukemias. This position is not intended for applicants with primary clinical interests in cellular immunotherapy or hematopoietic stem cell transplantation. The candidate must have at least two years of experience as an attending physician after completion of fellowship training. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include expanding translational and clinical research efforts in pediatric hematologic malignancies. The successful applicant will be academically productive, collaborative, and able to expand our already robust research enterprise. The successful candidate must have an established record of peer-reviewed scholarship and extramural grant funding and is expected to have 50% independent research effort funding within three years of appointment."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175800": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Movement Disorders Informatics, CE Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of evaluation and management of Parkinson’s disease, related disorders, and other movement disorders. Expertise in botulinum toxin injection, management of neurostimulators, and novel technologies related to clinical assessment, such as the use of advanced computing techniques to analyze clinical data or the implementation of digital health technologies, is preferred.  Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree and be board-certified or board-eligible in Neurology. Completion of a fellowship in Movement Disorders is also required. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient consultations and ongoing care of patients with Movement Disorders. Expertise with botulinum toxin injection and management of neurostimulators is strongly encouraged. Supervision of resident clinic and a minor component of inpatient care of general neurology patients (approximately 1-2 weeks per year) may be required. Clinical care will be primarily at Pennsylvania Hospital, but some coverage of satellite clinics in suburban locations may be available. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include either an independent research program (e.g., K-series award leading to further independent funding) or an active collaborative role in integrated research programs. Participation as a site investigator in clinical trials is also an option. Publication in peer-reviewed journals is expected."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180733": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Oculoplastics Specialist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of oculoplastics. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents, students, and fellows at the Scheie Eye Institute. Clinical responsibilities may include providing medical and surgical oculoplastics care at the Scheie Eye Institute and one of Scheie's satellite offices."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180735": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Oculoplastics Specialist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of oculoplastics. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents, medical students and fellows at the Scheie Eye Institute. Clinical responsibilities may include providing medical and surgical oculoplastics care at the Scheie Eye Institute and one of Scheie's satellite offices. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include collaborative or independent research within the specific area of oculoplastics.  Early career applicants with a demonstrated record of scholarship are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188917": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Research Track at CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure research track. Applicants must have an M.D. and/or Ph.D degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative research programs; supervision of postdoctoral fellows, students, and research staff; coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators; and participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178303": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Research Track, CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of psychiatric genetics, psychiatric neuroimaging, and combined imaging-genetics studies using clinically-acquired brain magnetic resonance imaging archives. Familiarity with PennCNV, parseCNV2, recon-all-clinical, and GAMLSS is preferred. Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include data analysis, disseminating research findings, leading a team of bioinformatics staff, independent grant writing, supervising students."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181190": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Research Track, Division of Allergy and Immunology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Allergy and Immunology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Allergy/Immunology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree.  Candidates should possess skills in natural killer cell biology, quantitative imaging and tumor microenvironment modeling.  Further, they should have expertise in the lytic immunological synapse and natural killer cell deficiency. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include Initiating and conducting independent experiments without direct supervision and with minimal guidance from the principal investigator. Developing new experimental procedures and publishing research results. Collaborating and interacting with other researchers within the home research institute and at other institutions. Developing new experimental procedures and hypotheses for further investigation. Preparing manuscripts and abstracts for publication. Publishing scientific articles in refereed journals, presenting at scientific symposiums. Preparing grant proposals for external funding. Serving as resource person for colleagues and as a mentor for less experienced research personnel. Managing/supervising other research staff or projects and assisting with the management of laboratory operations."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168007": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Research Track, Division of GI, Hepatology and Nutrition",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure research track. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Board certified/eligible in pediatric gastroenterology if MD or equivalent. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include assist in augmenting and leading basic science, translational and/or clinical research initiatives. Successful applicants will have evidence of productivity in high impact journals and a funding track record demonstrating leadership and independence."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/159955": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Specializing in Violence Prevention – Center for Violence Prevention at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of one or more of the six pillars of the center related to Violence Prevention research, with special consideration given to researchers conducting research related to gun violence. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Have demonstrated excellent track record in securing federal grants and have developed a clear line of violence prevention research. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic sessions with graduate students, medical fellows and residents, and postdoctoral fellows as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include patient care depending on the candidate, including but not limited to outpatient treatment, outpatient consultations, inpatient consultations, and inpatient attending responsibilities. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include maintaining an active research laboratory and supervising students, postdoctoral fellows, and research staff. Additional responsibilities include writing grants, reports, and manuscripts, developing collaborative and independent research programs, and coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators. Successful applicants will have evidence of federal funding and demonstrated success in fundamental and/or translational research relevant to violence prevention research. The primary faculty appointment will be in the Department of Pediatrics or the department in the Perelman School of Medicine that provides the best scientific fit. The University of Pennsylvania is a vibrant team-science-oriented environment with elite pediatric-based research collaborators. The Perelman School of Medicine, with world-class medical, biological, and population scientists, is part of an integrated campus including the Schools of Arts & Sciences, School of Education, School of Social Policy and Practice, the Leonard Davis Institute of Health Economics, and the Center of Public Health Initiatives, which provide the ideal setting for cross-disciplinary collaboration and impactful research. CHOP is a world-class leader in the delivery of pediatric care, research, and training pediatric leaders of the future. The Center for Violence Prevention (CVP) develops, implements, and evaluates evidence-based programs to reduce the exposure to and impact of violence on patients and families across clinical and community settings. CVP uses a trauma-informed, community-based participatory research approach which is rooted in racial equity and social justice. The Center consists of six pillars: (1) Aggression and Bullying Prevention; (2) Community Violence & Trauma Support; (3) Intimate Partner Violence (IPV) Prevention; (4) Suicide Prevention; (5) Gun Safety; and (6) Professional Development and Training. CVP is uniquely positioned to conduct research that is authentic and meaningful because we have deep involvement in the programs that we are researching. CVP’s infrastructure supports a growing interdisciplinary network of 23 Scholars, 12 Associates and 50 staff members who provide thought leadership in areas such as gun safety, community violence, intimate partner violence, aggression and bullying, and racial microaggressions. CVP collaborates closely with other CHOP entities such as PolicyLab, Clinical Futures, and the Department of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry. We seek an energetic researcher who can conduct systematic research while, over time, mentor junior faculty, fellows, and graduate students. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179431": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure or Clinician-Educator Track, General Pediatrics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - General Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of General Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of research, education and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified in Pediatrics. Teaching responsibilities may include high quality teaching of CHOP fellows and residents as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient and/or outpatient clinical services in the candidate's sub-specialty, including supervision of residents and fellows (if applicable). Research or scholarship responsibilities may include experience in health services, quality, epidemiology, implementation and dissemination research as well as medical informatics."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191889": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track — Children's Hospital of Philadelphia Cardiovascular Institute and the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia, CHOP Cardiovascular Institute (CVI) and the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of fundamental mechanistic or translational research relevant to pediatric cardiovascular disease, including but not limited to: cardiac development and regeneration, immune or metabolic origins of cardiovascular disease, heritable cardiac diseases such as cardiac channelopathies, cardiomyopathies, and aortopathies/vasculopathies, precision- and genetics-based therapeutics, bioengineering approaches and novel technologies for cardiovascular research and therapeutics. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Pediatrics or an academic department in the Perelman School of Medicine that is consistent with the scientific expertise of the successful candidate. Teaching responsibilities may include participating in graduate and/or medical student education; mentoring trainees at multiple career stages; presenting lectures and leading didactic sessions as appropriate. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient and inpatient consults and attending duties for qualified clinician-scientists. Clinical responsibilities are not applicable for basic scientist candidates. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing and maintaining a scientifically impactful independent research program that has relevance to pediatric heart and vascular disease; sustaining significant extramural funding. Candidates will be members of the newly established CHOP Cardiovascular Institute (CVI). The successful candidate will develop an independent, extramurally supported research program focused on fundamental or translational questions relevant to pediatric heart and vascular biology and disease. CHOP is a world class leader in the delivery of pediatric care, research, and training pediatric leaders of the future. The pediatric cardiology and cardiac surgery groups within the CHOP Cardiac Center are well-known as innovative leaders in the care of children with congenital forms of heart and vascular disease, and in the development of breakthrough therapeutics and diagnostics. Recently, the CHOP CVI was launched with the primary mission of establishing a world-class comprehensive research center that spans basic discovery to translation and clinical implementation relevant to pediatric heart and vascular diseases. The CHOP CVI will be linked in collaborative partnership with the Penn CVI, home to renowned basic and translational scientists. This partnership will provide support and infrastructure for discovery, translational, and clinical research aimed at cardiovascular health and disease across the entire lifespan. Candidates need to demonstrate potential for independent, high-impact scholarship; vision and commitment for leveraging the rich and uniquely collaborative and translational environment at CHOP and Penn to tackle fundamental questions in pediatric cardiology. Competitive start-up package and laboratory space, protected time for the establishment of an independent research program, and institutional mentoring and career-development resources will be provided. The CHOP CVI is a newly launched, comprehensive research center spanning basic discovery through translation and clinical implementation for pediatric cardiovascular health. CHOP CVI is in close partnership with many key CHOP/Penn Institutes and Centers, including the Penn Cardiovascular Institute, CHOP Cardiac Center, CHOP Center for Mitochondrial and Epigenomic Medicine, and Penn Institute for Diabetes, Obesity and Metabolism."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180369": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, Human Genetics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Human Genetics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of human genetics, and may include expertise in one or more of the following: computational biology, statistical genetics, population genetics, biomedical informatics, complex genetics, clinical genetics, pharmacogenetics/genomics, functional genomics, structural variation analysis, cancer genetics, human phenomics, and genomic medicine. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. The candidate must be board certified in medical genetics and genomics. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient or outpatient services at CHOP’s Main campus and other sites. The Division leads multiple outpatient clinical programs, including 13 programs, providing care in over 7,500 outpatient encounters per year. Multispecialty programs within the Division include clinical experts in genetics, pediatrics, psychology, oncology, endocrinology, cardiology, pathology, among other disciplines, who are frequently partnered with leaders in associated research fields. The Division has a strong inpatient presence at the Main CHOP Hospital Campus in Philadelphia with three consultative services (mitochondrial medicine, metabolism, and clinical genetics) and a primary metabolism inpatient service. The Division also maintains virtual consultative services at the new CHOP community-based hospital in King of Prussia and external hospitals. Numerous inpatient attendings provide primary and consultative care for over 2,500 inpatient encounters per year. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative and independent research programs related to human genetics, co-supervision of postdoctoral fellows, students, and research staff, coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators, and participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/167021": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, Infectious Diseases",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Infectious Diseases Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Infectious Diseases in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include high-quality teaching of CHOP fellows and residents, as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include providing coverage in one or more of three inpatient consultation services: a service focused on children with general infectious diseases, a service dedicated to the care of immunocompromised hosts, and an attending-NP service currently focused on NICU and Orthopedic patients. Clinical responsibilities may also include seeing patients in the Division’s busy outpatient clinical practice. In addition to our General Infectious Diseases Clinic, we have dedicated “partner clinics” to provide collaborative outpatient care to patients with other underlying conditions, including malignancies, bone marrow and organ transplantation, and cystic fibrosis. Additionally, as CHOP expands its footprint (i.e., King of Prussia Hospital, potential sites in NJ) and the Division of Infectious Diseases partners with outside organizations, some local travel may be required. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include fundamental or translational research in the field of infectious diseases. Applicants with a strong record of research productivity and interest in fundamental or translational research in the field of infectious diseases will be considered. The Division of Infectious Diseases at the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia invites applications for an outstanding laboratory investigator to join the vibrant research environment in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania and the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia Research Institute (http://www.research.chop.edu). The Division has a strong track record of basic and clinical research across the spectrum of pediatric infections and host-microbe interactions. Candidates will also benefit from the larger research community across the University of Pennsylvania campus, which encompasses expertise in virology, immunology, bacteriology, parasitology, and the microbiome."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/157653": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, Pediatric Cardiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Cardiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Cardiology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology by the American Board of Pediatrics. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient and/or outpatient care for patients with congenital heart disease. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include a body of work that demonstrates intellectual independence, co-supervision of postdoctoral fellows, students, and research staff, coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators, participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts. The successful candidate must develop, grow and maintain independent extramural funding, and have scholarship in high-impact publications. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189541": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Tenure Track, Pediatric Nephrology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Nephrology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Nephrology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board certified/eligible in pediatric nephrology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and mentoring graduate students, medical students, pediatric residents, and pediatric nephrology fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include the treatment of children and adolescents with a wide range of kidney diseases, in the inpatient, outpatient, satellite campus, and dialysis settings. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include a strong interest and track record in clinical, basic science, and/or translational research involving patients with kidney disease, program administration skills, and commitment to direct and grow clinical programs in their specific area of interest. Significant research and clinical resources and space for the research and clinical programs will be provided to the successful candidate. The Division of Nephrology at the Children’s Hospital is at the forefront of clinical care, teaching, and research. The Division is comprised of 21 faculty members and 6 clinical fellows, in addition to our team of nurses, administrators, social workers, dieticians, and research staff. The CHOP Division of Nephrology provides comprehensive care for children, adolescents, and young adult patients with kidney disease."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181528": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Academic Clinician, Pediatric Behavioral Health (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Pediatric Psychology. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must have completed an accredited predoctoral internship and postdoctoral fellowship in pediatric or child clinical psychology. Licensure as a Psychologist in the State of Pennsylvania is required prior to beginning the position. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and training activities through our APA-accredited clinical child psychology internship training program, as well as with psychology and psychiatry trainees at various levels of training. Clinical responsibilities may include assessment, consultation and treatment services to children and families with acute and/or chronic illnesses across inpatient and outpatient settings, and working closely with multidisciplinary teams."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185973": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Academic Clinician-Hematopathologist-Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine/Hematopathology Division",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of flow cytometry/hematology/hematopathology. Knowledge and/or certification in Molecular Pathology and/or Pathology Informatics is preferred although not absolutely necessary. Applicants must hold an M.D., M.D./Ph.D., or equivalent degree and be certified by the American Board of Pathology (AP/CP or CP-only). Teaching responsibilities may include training of medical students, residents, fellows and post-doctoral students, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the Department and Hematopathology Division. Clinical responsibilities may include evaluation and diagnosis of hematopoietic neoplasms and other disorders, through participation in bone marrow, tissue, and flow cytometry services, review of peripheral blood and body fluid smears, and evaluation of hemoglobinopathies. Responsibilities also include weekend call. Eligibility for medical licensure in Pennsylvania and New Jersey"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189174": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Academic Clinician Track-Clinical Microbiology Laboratory at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania is seeking candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in clinical microbiology. Applied and/or translational research in the broad area of clinical microbiology and/or infectious diseases is encouraged. Applicants must have an MD or PhD or MD/PhD degree. MD candidates must be board-certified (or eligible) in clinical pathology (or AP/CP).  MD candidates must be eligible for medical licensure in the State of Pennsylvania and New Jersey. PhD candidates must be board-certified (or eligible) by the American Board of Medical Microbiology. All candidates must have had a minimum of 1-year of subspecialty fellowship training in an accredited program in medical microbiology. Experience in clinical informatics is welcomed. Teaching responsibilities may include active participation in teaching and supervision of fellows, pathology residents, medical students and laboratory staff in areas of medical microbiology. Clinical responsibilities may include: 1.  Serve as a clinical consultant to the medical staff and other providers on test results and interpretation 2.  Fulfill the role as the director of the clinical microbiology laboratory at a regional hospital 3.  Be involved with oversight of clinical test analysis and sign-out, quality management, innovation and test development 4.  Working closely with the various infectious diseases and antimicrobial stewardship clinical teams 5.  Actively participate in the teaching and supervision of fellows, pathology residents, medical students and laboratory staff in areas of medical microbiology"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169682": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Academic Clinician Track-Surgical Pathology with Expertise in Thoracic Pathology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of thoracic pathology. Applicants with additional cardiac pathology experience will be highly considered. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. American Board of Pathology, AP-only or AP/CP. Teaching responsibilities may include medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include participation in the thoracic pathology service at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and its affiliates, general frozen section service, autopsy service, and night/weekend call. Additional subspecialty interests to be combined with the Thoracic Pathology service will be considered. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include opportunities that may be available to participate in clinical research and mentor trainees on academic pathway projects if desired."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180972": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Academic Clinician Track-Transfusion Medicine w/Expertise in Apheresis and Cellular Therapy",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Expertise is required in the specific area of apheresis and cellular therapy. Candidates must be boarded in Pathology, CP-only or AP/CP, Board-eligible in Transfusion Medicine and must have completed fellowship training in Transfusion Medicine with significant experience in therapeutic apheresis and cellular collections for hematopoietic stem cell transplants and manufacturing cellular therapies. Teaching responsibilities may include educating pathology residents, Transfusion Medicine and other clinical fellows, and medical students. The candidate will serve as the rotation director for the Transfusion Medicine resident rotations and medical student electives. They will also be the Small Group Course Director for the Transfusion Medicine component of the first-year medical student course, Mechanisms of Disease and Therapeutic Interventions. Clinical responsibilities may include serving as a transfusion medicine attending sharing medical oversight for a high complexity academic blood bank and transfusion service, apheresis unit, and hematopoietic stem cell laboratory."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183650": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Academic Clinician-Neuropathologist, Pathology and Laboratory Medicine, Division of Neuropathology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Neuropathology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree.  Board Certification/Eligibility in Neuropathology and Anatomic Pathology are Required along with eligibility for unrestricted medical license in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Teaching responsibilities may include lectures, didactics and training of medical students, residents, and fellows in Perelman School of Medicine and at Penn Medicine Hospitals, primarily at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include surgical and medical neuropathology service, which in addition to sign-out includes intraoperative consultations (frozens), muscle and nerve biopsies, telepathology, consults, presentations at intradepartmental or multidisciplinary conferences."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174614": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Clinician Educator-Academic Neuropathologist-Division of Neuropathology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. American Board of Pathology certification is required in Anatomic Pathology or Anatomic and Clinical Pathology. American Board of Pathology certification or eligibility in Neuropathology is required. Eligibility for licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and mentoring of neuropathology fellows, medical residents, medical students, graduate students and postdoctoral or other scientists. Clinical responsibilities may include surgical and medical neuropathology, including intraoperative consultations (frozens) and on call duties. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include development of a translational, collaborative research program, preferably on brain tumors. Faculty on the CE track at the Perelman School of Medicine are expected to develop and sustain a record of academic productivity, which includes involvement in collaborative and/or independent research efforts leading to peer-reviewed published works. Faculty on this track are also expected to demonstrate excellence in teaching and clinical care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183707": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Research Track-Faculty Position in Immunology, Lymph Node Biology, and Multicentric Castleman Disease-Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of of human immunology with a focus on lymph node biology, stromal cell biology, and/or immune-mediated diseases (in particular, multicentric Castleman disease and other hyperinflammatory syndromes). Required experience includes multiomic data generation and analysis, in-depth understanding with human clinical data and integration, and strong grounding in molecular and cellular signaling, including biochemical and mechanistic approaches. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing and leading an independent research program focused on immunological mechanisms of disease, in particular, multicentric Castleman disease with emphasis on lymph node, stromal cell biology, immune dysregulation, and hyperinflammation. The candidate must perform reductionist experimental approaches (human and mouse immunology ex vivo and in vivo work) and apply multiomic approaches (e.g., single-cell transcriptomics, spatial analysis, epigenomics, proteomics) to define disease mechanisms by integrating molecular signaling and biochemical pathways with systems-level analyses. The successful candidate will join a highly collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment with strong integration across immunology, pathology, and systems biology. Candidates are expected to establish an externally funded research program and contribute to collaborative initiatives across the Perelman School of Medicine and affiliated institutions."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181904": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Research Track-Human B Cell Immunologist-Department of Pathology & Laboratory Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of human immunology, single cell analysis including multicolor immunophenotyping, RNA-seq, BCR-seq, TCR-seq etc.The ability to collaborate and communicate across basic, translational and clinical research domains is important for this position. Applicants must have a PhD or equivalent and significant research experience for this position. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include directing an independently funded research program with a focus on B cell contributions to protective and pathologic immunity."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192297": {
      "title": "Assistant Professors in CE or Tenure Track - Department of Ophthalmology - NIH K12 Vision Clinician Scientist Program",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in either the tenure or non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an MD, DO, OD, or DVM degree. They may also have a PhD or master’s degree but this is not required. They must be licensed to practice medicine in the US, be board eligible or board certified, and be US citizens or permanent residents. The successful candidate must have demonstrated excellent qualifications in research, clinical care, and education. While both tenure and clinician-educator track faculty conduct methodological and collaborative research, tenure track faculty focus primarily on independent, investigator driven research while clinician-educator track faculty focus primarily on collaboration. Research or scholarship responsibilities will include the establishment of wet-lab, patient-oriented, or bioinformatic research supported by the Department’s K12 grant with potential for eventual K08/K23/R01 funding. Clinical responsibilities may include patient care dedicated to the candidates’ ophthalmic specialty. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents and fellows. The NIH K12 grant, which has been awarded to Penn's Department of Ophthalmology, enables Department selected Scholars to devote 50-75% of their effort to research. It also provides mentoring and other research resources with the goal of having the Scholar transition to an individual NIH K award (KO8 or K23) within three years and an R01within 6 years. Applicants may pursue clinical practice in vitreoretinal surgery, medical retina, glaucoma, cornea, neuro-ophthalmology, oculoplastics, ocular oncology, uveitis, or pediatric ophthalmology.  Research mentorship is available in inherited retinal degeneration (IRD), gene therapy, gene editing, transcriptomics, proteomics, big data, biostatistics, glaucoma, metabolism, optic neuropathy, adaptive optics, dry eye, inflammation, AMD, aging, oxidative stress, ROP, and others. Penn's Department of Ophthalmology K12 Program is located in one of NEl's top-funded Departments. The program has been running for 20 years and has facilitated the careers of numerous academic faculty, many of whom have stayed on faculty at Scheie after completing the program. The candidate must be interested in becoming a Scientist-Clinician planning to devote 50% or more of their time to research throughout their career."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168018": {
      "title": "Associate and/or Full Professor, Research Track, Division of GI, Hepatology and Nutrition",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure research track. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include augmenting and leading basic science, translational and/or clinical research initiatives. For the full professor rank, candidates must show evidence of an international reputation for their scientific accomplishments. Successfull applicants will have evidence of productivity in high impact journals and a funding track record demonstrating leadership and independence. Opportunities may arise to provide research mentorship and clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164536": {
      "title": "Associate Chair of Digital and Computational Pathology, Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia, Clinician Educator - Junior Rank, Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of digital pathology, artificial intelligence, and independent/collaborative research. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. American Board of Pathology Certification, AP or AP/CP, is preferred but not required. Teaching responsibilities may include medical students, residents, fellows and post-doctoral students. Clinical responsibilities may include an anatomic or clinical pathology subspecialty. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include development of an independent or highly collaborative research program (as PI, Co-PI or Co-I) in the area of digital and computational pathology. Faculty on the Clinician Educator (CE) track at the Perelman School of Medicine are expected to develop and sustain a record of academic productivity, which includes involvement in collaborative and/or independent research efforts leading to peer-reviewed published works. Faculty on this track are also expected to demonstrate excellence in teaching while those with clinical responsibilities are also expected to demonstrate excellence in clinical care. Department-wide efforts to increase digital capabilities are underway. In support of these efforts, the Division of Anatomic Pathology has developed a robust digital pathology program, established in 2019, and has digitized approximately 120,000 slides per year. We currently have three whole slide scanners, an archive of over 600,000 whole-slide images, and plans to onboard a new image management system with artificial intelligence capabilities in the next year. The Associate Chair for Digital and Computational Pathology will report directly to the Department Chair and will oversee digital and computational pathology initiatives at CHOP. He/She will work closely with the Division Chief of Anatomic Pathology, Division Chief of Pathology Informatics, Associate Chair of Pathology Informatics, and Director of the Center for Diagnostic Innovation to implement and develop clinical, research and educational programs in Digital and Computational Pathology."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164538": {
      "title": "Associate Chair of Digital and Computational Pathology, Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia, Clinician Educator - Senior Rank, Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of digital pathology, artificial intelligence, and independent/collaborative research. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. American Board of Pathology Certification, AP or AP/CP, is preferred but not required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include medical students, residents, fellows and post-doctoral students. Clinical responsibilities may include an anatomic or clinical pathology subspecialty. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include development of an independent or highly collaborative research program (as PI, Co-PI or Co-I) in the area of digital and computational pathology. Faculty on the Clinician Educator (CE) track at the Perelman School of Medicine are expected to develop and sustain a record of academic productivity, which includes involvement in collaborative and/or independent research efforts leading to peer-reviewed published works. Faculty on this track are also expected to demonstrate excellence in teaching while those with clinical responsibilities are also expected to demonstrate excellence in clinical care. Department-wide efforts to increase digital capabilities are underway. In support of these efforts, the Division of Anatomic Pathology has developed a robust digital pathology program, established in 2019, and has digitized approximately 120,000 slides per year. We currently have three whole slide scanners, an archive of over 600,000 whole-slide images, and plans to onboard a new image management system with artificial intelligence capabilities in the next year. The Associate Chair for Digital and Computational Pathology will report directly to the Department Chair and will oversee digital and computational pathology initiatives at CHOP. He/She will work closely with the Division Chief of Anatomic Pathology, Division Chief of Pathology Informatics, Associate Chair of Pathology Informatics, and Director of the Center for Diagnostic Innovation to implement and develop clinical, research and educational programs in Digital and Computational Pathology."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/157270": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor (with Tenure) in the Department of Neurosurgery specializing in computational modeling of neural recordings in humans and experimental animals",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurosurgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurosurgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of relating neural circuit dynamics to computational processes in the brain in the service of translational neuroengineering, including brain-computer interfaces. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching graduate students, medical students, residents and fellows. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include leading a cutting-edge research program on computational modeling of neural recordings in humans and experimental animals to decipher the neural computations underlying movement, memory, and perception. Preferred applicant must have federal funding as a contact PI. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177044": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor - Academic Clinician Track - Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Neonatology and Newborn Services Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Neonatology & Newborn Services in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine by the American Board of Pediatrics. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows as well as formal lecture opportunities within the Division and Department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical care and productivity in program development. Clinical care will be provided in the 100 bed Level IV NICU at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and the 40 bed Level III NICU at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, as well as in the Neonatal Follow-Up Program. Duties also include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184087": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor - Academic Clinician- Cutaneous Oncologist (Dermatology)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of non-invasive diagnosis and surveillance of pigmented lesions is required. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicant must be board certified or board eligible in the field of Dermatology with focus on cutaneous oncology and skin cancers at increased risk for recurrence or metastasis. Skin cancer expertise, proven by publications, invited lectures, or clinical experience, is strongly preferred. Demonstrated leadership experience or potential is preferred. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include didactics to our world-class residents, fellows, medical students and trainees rotating from other institutions in dermatology and other specialties concerning skin cancer, Mohs micrographic surgery and dermatologic oncology. The faculty member(s) will play a key role in educating our residents on the cutaneous oncology track and research fellow in cutaneous oncology. Clinical responsibilities may include evaluation and treatment of patients with skin cancer, particularly those with a high risk of recurrence or metastasis. Clinical responsibilities will focus on patients in the Penn Dermatology Oncology Center's specialty clinics, including the Pigmented Lesion Clinic, the Rare and Inherited Skin Cancer Clinic, and the High-Risk Skin Cancer Clinic for Organ Transplant Recipients and Immunosuppressed patients. Candidates will benefit from a busy practice and an extensive infrastructure with state-of-the-art facilities and a large support staff of nurses, histotechnicians, research fellows, and coordinators. We seek candidates who demonstrate excellent clinical judgement, professionalism, and commitment to our team. Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in Cutaneous Oncology and building a nationally or internationally recognized career in dermatology. Candidates will enjoy extensive mentorship from our experienced dermatological oncologists and faculty to develop advanced preventive and treatment skills. The Philadelphia region boasts a rich history with excellent restaurants, sports, art, and neighborhoods. Candidates can book easy plane travel to almost any destination worldwide, and train travel along the East Coast is fast and convenient"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177046": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor - Clinician Educator Track - Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Neonatology and Newborn Services Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Neonatology & Newborn Services in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine by the American Board of Pediatrics. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows as well as formal lecture opportunities within the Division and Department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical care and productivity in program development. Clinical care will be provided in the 100 bed Level IV NICU at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and the 40 bed Level III NICU at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Duties may also include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or basic studies and will be dependent on the candidate’s interests and independent support. Evidence of scholarship is required for the Clinician-Educator track."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177048": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor - Research Track - Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Neonatology and Newborn Services Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Neonatology & Newborn Services in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure research track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine by the American Board of Pediatrics or Internal Medicine. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include having a national reputation for collaborative or independent research of high quality with distinctive, original, and expert intellectual contributions. For Full Professor rank, candidates must show evidence of an international reputation for their scientific accomplishments. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in basic laboratory research with a publication record in neonatology, developmental or molecular medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include education of postdocs and fellows as well as formal lecture opportunities within the Division and Department."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177052": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor - Tenure Track - Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Neonatology and Newborn Services Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Neonatology & Newborn Services in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine by the American Board of Pediatrics or Internal Medicine. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include a record of excellence in the teaching of medical students, trainees, post docs and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include consultations for high risk neonatology and maternal and fetal conditions, as well as prenatal genetic diagnosis. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include independent research grant support with a series of peer-reviewed research articles in respected neonatology, developmental or molecular medicine journals, a body of work that demonstrates intellectual independence, supervision of postdoctoral fellows, students, and research staff, coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators, participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187444": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor - Tenure Track - Perinatal Research Center Director - Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Neonatology and Newborn Services Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Neonatology & Newborn Services in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of basic or translational perinatal research. The successful candidate will serve as the Director of a newly formed Perinatal Research Center (PRC). Applicants must have an M.D. and/or Ph.D degree. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include working with medical students, graduate students, postdoctoral fellows and other trainees. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include an integrative approach to research in perinatal biology that extends before and after birth. Within the center, investigators from different fields will participate in collaborative multidisciplinary research with the goal of improving outcomes associated with perinatal/neonatal diseases and to understand the fundamentals of developmental biology. The mission of faculty in the PRC will not only be to foster innovative research focused on fundamental questions in developmental biology and the developmental origins of health and disease, but also to address improvement of neonatal outcomes, health care delivery, and health inequities. The PRC Director will engage, lead, and energize the scientific community across the CHOP Research Institute to build new programs and collaborations at CHOP and the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania. The PRC Director will be provided with space, financial resources and new faculty positions to both advance their own research program and develop a world-class investigative group committed to the mission of the Perinatal Research Center."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184976": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor of Neurosurgery, Tenure Track in the Department of Neurosurgery, Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania, specializing in Neuro-Oncology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurosurgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurosurgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of neuro-immuno-oncology, cancer neuroscience, and genomics. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include mentoring undergraduate and graduate students and postdoctoral fellows, as well as providing formal lectures within the department and PSOM. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include maintaining a robust, federally-funded independent research program and collaborating with other investigators to develop interdisciplinary programs that move scientific discoveries from the laboratory to clinical settings. The position may include leadership and management of core facilities, including multiphoton imaging, -omics, and flow cytometry. Preferred candidate must have a strong track record of federal research funding and a sterling national and international reputation. A continuous record of productivity and high-impact original papers as a project leader are essential."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/167617": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor Pulmonary & Sleep Medicine – AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Pulmonary Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Pulmonary Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification in Pediatric Pulmonary or Pediatric Sleep Medicine are required. Rank will be commensurate with experience.  The successful candidate may have leadership responsibilities. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture and medical education opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include seeing patients in the inpatient and outpatient settings. There may also be opportunities to participate in quality improvement initiatives and clinical or translational research. Research is not required for faculty on the AC Track however the successful candidate may collaborate/contribute to research. The division provides care to children with a diverse spectrum of pulmonary and sleep disorders including through the Cystic Fibrosis Center, Sleep Center, Technology Dependence Center, Asthma Program, Lung Transplant Program, Thoracic Insufficiency Center, Bronchoscopy/Aerodigestive Program, and clinics for children with chronic lung disease of infancy, Interstitial Lung Disease, Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia, and other rare lung diseases."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/167618": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor Pulmonary & Sleep Medicine – CE or Tenure Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Pulmonary Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Pulmonary Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification in Pediatric Pulmonary or Pediatric Sleep Medicine is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include seeing patients in the inpatient and outpatient settings. There may also be opportunities to participate in quality improvement initiatives, medical education, and clinical or translational research. The division provides care to children with a diverse spectrum of pulmonary and sleep disorders including through the Cystic Fibrosis Center, Sleep Center, Technology Dependence Center, Asthma Program, Lung Transplant Program, Thoracic Insufficiency Center, Bronchoscopy/Aerodigestive Program, and clinics for children with chronic lung disease of infancy, Interstitial Lung Disease, Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia, and other rare lung diseases. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include collaborative and independent research programs, an outstanding record of research productivity, and participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169831": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, AC Track, Adult Congenital Heart Disease",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Cardiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Cardiology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Adult congenital heart disease, congenital echocardiography. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification or board eligible in Adult Congenital Heart Disease is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient adult congenital heart disease clinic, inpatient adult congenital heart disease consult service, congenital echocardiogram interpretation and reporting. Research is not a requirement of faculty on the AC track. Candidates may participate in opportunities involving collaborative clinical research and research mentorship for trainees."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174362": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, AC Track, Division of Allergy and Immunology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Allergy and Immunology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Allergy/Immunology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. The preferred candidate will be Board certified/eligible in Allergy and Immunology. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Applicants who are mid-career are encouraged to apply. Teaching responsibilities may include high quality teaching of CHOP fellows and residents. Clinical responsibilities may include developing a regional referral base in Allergy and Immunology. Practice sites include CHOP community pediatric specialty care offices in Abington, PA, Lancaster, PA or a combination of locations. Inpatient call is rotated."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168008": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, Academic Clinician, Division of GI, Hepatology and Nutrition",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of education and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible in Pediatrics Gastroenterology. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents and fellows, participating in family education days. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding outpatient, inpatient and procedural care at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and/or its satellites. Candidates must show evidence of attained recognition in clinical and teaching expertise."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179460": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, Academic Clinician, General Cardiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Cardiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Cardiology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board Certified/ Board Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic lectures to fellows, residents, medical students and nursing staff on topics in general cardiology. Experience in teaching is also required, including curriculum development, innovative teaching materials, and mentoring of junior faculty is also expected. Clinical responsibilities may include Inpatient and Outpatient coverage of General Cardiology Service, Electrophysiology, Pulmonary Hypertension, Catheterization/Interventional Laboratory, Heart Failure/Heart Transplant, Echocardiography and Fetal Echocardiography at Main Hospital and satellite offices in Pennsylvania and New Jersey. Candidates must show evidence of continued excellence in clinical practice, such as innovative accomplishments in delivery of care, clinical productivity, quality improvement initiatives, and must have an identifiable area(s) of special expertise; a regional referral base is required for full Professor rank."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/164369": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, Academic Clinician, General Pediatrics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - General Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of General Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of education and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible in Pediatrics. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include demonstrated excellence in the bedside clinical teaching of residents, fellows, and/or medical students. Enthusiasm and dedication to educating our residents and students is highly valued in our department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical care on any of the inpatient and/or outpatient General Pediatrics services. Candidates must demonstrate a defined area of concentration in clinical and teaching excellence, as well as sustained professionalism."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194063": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, Academic Clinician, General Pediatrics-Palliative Care",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - General Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of General Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Fellowship training, education and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be fellowship trained, board certified/eligible in hospice and palliative medicine and board eligibility or certification in Pediatrics or a Pediatric subspecialty as well as eligibility for Pennsylvania licensure. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of residents, fellows, and/or medical students. Clinical responsibilities may include demonstrated excellence in the bedside clinical teaching of residents, fellows, and/or medical students. Enthusiasm and dedication to educating our residents and students is highly valued in our department."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175421": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, Academic Clinician, Pediatric Adolescent Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Adolescent Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Adolescent Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/eligible in Pediatrics, Internal Medicine or Addiction Medicine and Adolescent Medicine strongly preferred. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Applicants who are mid-career are encouraged to apply. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in clinical education of medical students, residents, and fellows as a member of the Craig-Dalsimer Division of Adolescent Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient and outpatient primary and specialty care in Adolescent Medicine at The Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Multiple sites of practice are available including a primary care practice, specialty care satellite locations and inpatient units and a behavioral health hospital. Unique opportunities are available for applicants interested in an expanding Eating Disorder program. Leadership positions in these clinical areas may also be available. Opportunities to participate in clinical trials or other clinic-based research projects may be available related to continuous quality improvement, health services, health disparities, resiliency, STDs/HIV, pregnancy prevention, smoking, gender, eating disorders, weight regulation, depression, and suicide. Research is not a requirement for AC Track faculty."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168025": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, CE and/or Tenure Track, Division of GI, Hepatology and Nutrition",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of education, research and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified in Pediatrics and/or Gastroenterology. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents and fellows, participating in family education days. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding outpatient, inpatient and procedural care at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and/or its satellites. Candidates must have a reputation as an excellent clinician. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include assisting with augmenting basic, translational and/or clinical research initiatives in liver disease, motility, bile duct development, gastrointestinal allergies, nutrition, inflammatory bowel disease, and microbiome research. Clinician Educators are often involved in collaborative, can be independent research, that results in new discoveries/knowledge or extend/advances understanding of knowledge ultimately important to human health/disease. Tenure track faculty are most often involved in independent or innovative collaborative research that results in new discoveries/knowledge or extend/advances understanding of knowledge ultimately important to human health/disease. Candidates must be nationally recognized experts in the field. Candidates for positions at the rank of Full Professor on the Tenure track must be internationally recognized experts in the field. Additional information about PSOM faculty tracks can be found here: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/assets/user-content/documents/Academic%20Review/COAP/PSOMFacultyTrackDescriptions.pdf"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/159562": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, Clinical Educator or Tenure Track, Nephrology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Nephrology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Nephrology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree.  Applicants must also be board certified/eligible in pediatric nephrology. Applicants must have demonstrated excellence in education, research, and clinical care. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and mentoring junior faculty, graduate students, medical students, pediatric residents, and pediatric nephrology fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include the treatment of children and adolescents with a wide range of kidney diseases, in both the inpatient, outpatient, satellite campus, and dialysis settings. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include a national reputation in clinical, basic science, and/or translational research involving patients with kidney disease, program administration skills, and commitment to direct and grow clinical programs in their specific area of interest. Significant research and clinical resources and space for the research and clinical programs will be provided to the successful candidate. The Division of Nephrology at the Children’s Hospital is at the forefront of clinical care, teaching, and research. The Division is comprised of 15 faculty members and 9 clinical fellows, in addition to our team of nurses, administrators, social workers, dieticians, and research staff. The CHOP Division of Nephrology provides comprehensive care for children, adolescents, and young adult patients with kidney disease. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179461": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor, Clinician Educator, Pediatric Cardiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Cardiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Cardiology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board Certified/Board Eligible in Pediatrics is required. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic lectures to fellows, residents, medical students and nursing staff on topics in general cardiology. Experience in teaching is also required, including curriculum development, innovative teaching materials, and mentoring of junior faculty. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Clinical responsibilities may include Inpatient and Outpatient coverage of General Cardiology Service, Electrophysiology, Pulmonary Hypertension, Catheterization/Interventional Laboratory, Heart Failure/Heart Transplant, Echocardiography, Fetal Echocardiography. This includes staffing of satellite offices in New Jersey and Pennsylvania. Candidates must show evidence of continued excellence in clinical practice, such as innovative accomplishments in delivery of care, clinical productivity, quality improvement initiatives, and must have an identifiable area(s) of special expertise; a regional referral base is required for full Professor rank. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing an area of research concentration in general cardiology and any pediatric cardiology subspecialties. Candidates must show evidence of continued excellence in their research concentration."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174140": {
      "title": "Associate Professor - Neuromuscular Medicine Neurologist - AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Neuromuscular Ultrasound and/or Autonomic expertise. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Applicants must be board-certified in Neurology and Neuromuscular Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching neuromuscular fellows, residents, and medical students during their rotations in the EMG lab, outpatient clinic, and inpatient services. The NM faculty will also provide lectures on topics pertinent to neuromuscular diseases and the Department of Neurology throughout the year. Clinical responsibilities may include seeing neuromuscular patients in the outpatient clinic and perform EMGs; Special interest in CMT is encouraged. If qualified, they may interpret NM ultrasounds and Autonomic studies. Applicants who are mid-career are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180866": {
      "title": "Associate Professor AC Faculty Position – Pulmonary/Critical Care/Sleep, Penn Presbyterian",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Sleep Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Sleep Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Candidates should be board certified or board eligible in Sleep Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include training residents and fellows in addition to precepting medical students and other trainees in the field of Sleep Medicine. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include performing comprehensive evaluations of patients with sleep and respiratory disorders and managing patients with sleep disorders; interpreting polysomnograms, multiple sleep latency tests, and home sleep apnea tests; rounding on the inpatient sleep consult service at Penn Presbyterian; attending in the sleep disorders clinic and sleep telemedicine program. Clinical responsibilities will be at Pennsylvania Presbyterian as well as the primary outpatient site of the Sleep Division at the University of Pennsylvania. Applicants will have demonstrated excellent qualifications in education and clinical care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180739": {
      "title": "Associate Professor Comprehensive Ophthalmology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must hold an M.D. or equivalent degree. Clinical responsibilities may include a faculty practice with spanning comprehensive ophthalmic medical and surgical care at Scheie Eye Institute and select satellite locations, with the majority of outpatient services provided at the Penn Medicine location in Wilmington, Delaware. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in didactic and clinical instruction of residents and, as needed, medical students and fellows at Scheie."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/167377": {
      "title": "Associate Professor Faculty Position, Academic Clinician Track - Division of Sleep Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Sleep Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Sleep Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pulmonary medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Sleep Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include training residents and fellows in addition to precepting medical students and other trainees in the field of Sleep Medicine. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include performing comprehensive evaluations and management of patients with sleep disorders including non-invasive ventilation, interpreting polysomnograms, multiple sleep latency tests, and home sleep apnea tests, attending in the sleep disorders clinic, and sleep telemedicine program. Clinical responsibilities will be at the primary outpatient site of the Sleep Division of the Hospital University of Pennsylvania as well as Pennsylvania Hospital. There will be an expectation of the ability of the selected candidate to provide management and/or leadership."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192693": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Consultation/Liaison Psychiatry - AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Psychiatry and consultation/liaison psychiatry board certifications are required. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical supervision of residents, fellows, and advanced practice trainees in the evaluation and management of patients who are eligible for and/or status-post organ transplants and didactic teaching about transplant psychiatry. Clinical responsibilities may include evaluation and management of patients who are eligible for and/or status-post organ transplants in the hospital and ambulatory setting; serving as a collaborating physician for advanced practice psychiatric providers; participation in transplant selection committee meetings."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172626": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Clinical Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Emergency Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Emergency Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. ABEM certified or board eligible is required. Teaching responsibilities may include bedside clinical teaching of emergency medicine residents and students. Additional teaching responsibilities include lectures, journal clubs, case conferences, simulation teaching, small group discussions, and others. Enthusiasm and dedication to educating our residents and students are highly valued in our department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical care to emergency department patients in one or more of our three city hospitals: Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. Patients seen in our EDs include high acuity, complex patients, as well as patients with less acute illnesses and injuries. Penn Presbyterian Medical Center is a Level 1 Trauma Center. Mid-career faculty with local and/or national recognition in their area of interest/expertise are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187607": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Clinical Obstetrics & Gynecology in Surgery at CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of obstetrics & gynecology and maternal fetal medicine with a focus on prenatal diagnosis and fetal therapy. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. The preferred candidate will be certified or eligible for certification by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology or hold equivalent certification. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic education of medical students, residents and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include activities centering on prenatal diagnosis and counseling, fetal surgical interventions and the management and delivery of pregnancies complicated by congenital anomalies. This position will be housed in the Richard D. Wood Jr. Center for Fetal Diagnosis and Treatment, administered by the Department of Surgery at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. We are recognized as a world class fetal diagnosis & treatment center and a pioneer in the development of new fetal diagnostic and therapeutic procedures."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190632": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Gastrointestinal Surgery (AC track)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of minimally-invasive gastrointestinal surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Surgery or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of fellows, residents and medical students rotating on the GI Surgery service. Clinical responsibilities may include in- and out-patient clinical care of general and gastrointestinal surgery patients – especially within the foregut and hernia realms. This position will be housed at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Preference will be given to candidates possessing fellowship training in minimally-invasive surgery and who possess robotic surgery skills. Advanced endoscopic skills are also welcomed."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194822": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Gastrointestinal Surgery at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of minimally-invasive gastrointestinal surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Surgery or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of fellows, residents and medical students rotating on the GI Surgery service. Clinical responsibilities may include in- and out-patient clinical care of general and gastrointestinal surgery patients – especially within the foregut and hernia realms. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include basic science or clinical studies in the field of gastrointestinal surgery. This position will be housed at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Preference will be given to candidates possessing fellowship training in minimally-invasive surgery and who possess robotic surgery skills. Advanced endoscopic skills are also welcomed."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161489": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Neurosurgery, Clinician Educator or Tenure Track, at the University of Pennsylvania, Perelman School of Medicine, specializing in brain tumor surgery and immunotherapy",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurosurgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurosurgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of brain tumor surgery and brain tumor research in immune and cellular therapies. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicant must be board certified. Teaching responsibilities may include the education of medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include the neurosurgical management of brain and skull base tumors and oversight of the multi-disciplinary care of brain and skull base tumor patients, including clinical trials. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include translational and/or basic research in brain tumors, with funding from the National Institutes of Health and other federal funding agencies as PI. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183352": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Plastic Surgery at Pennsylvania Hospital (AC Track)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of plastic surgery and reconstructive microsurgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidate must be board-certified by the American Board of Plastic Surgery (ABPS). Teaching responsibilities may include education of medical students, residents and microsurgical fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient, inpatient, and surgical care of patients. Responsibilities may include the full spectrum of plastic surgery with a primary focus on breast reconstruction. Position will be based in Philadelphia at Pennsylvania Hospital with potential outpatient sites in suburban NJ or PA. Candidates must have completed an ACGME-accredited plastic surgery residency program and a microsurgical fellowship."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172520": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Urology at CHOP Surgery",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Children's Hospital of Pennsylvania The Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track.*  Expertise is required in the specific area of pediatric urology, with a focus on minimally invasive surgery and major urologic surgical reconstruction. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Urology or eligible for such certification. All candidates must have completed training through an ACGME-approved pediatric urology fellowship. Teaching responsibilities may include instruction of medical students and residents as well as pediatric urology fellows in the operating room, outpatient clinic, and on inpatient rounds. Clinical responsibilities may include care for urologic patients, including open, endoscopic, and minimally invasive surgery. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include studies in areas of clinical outcomes and urologic reconstruction. A strong research background and demonstrated potential for developing independent research will be preferred, and the successful candidate will be expected to publish in peer-reviewed journals. We welcome prospective candidates to learn more about the different Faculty Tracks in the Perelman School of Medicine."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172188": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, AC Track, Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics and/or Neurodevelopmental Disabilities. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include developmental assessments and providing follow up care in an outpatient setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174353": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, AC Track, Pediatric Rehabilitation Physiatrist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Rehabilitation Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Rehabilitation Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of diagnosing and treating various conditions requiring rehabilitation. Familiarity with an electronic medical record is desirable. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be Board-certified in Pediatric Rehabilitation. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching rotating medical students, residents and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Participation is encouraged in regional, national and international meetings. Clinical responsibilities may include Pediatric Rehabilitation Outpatient clinic and inpatient consultations in acute care setting as well as attending on the inpatient rehabilitation unit and sharing in on-call coverage. Opportunity to participate in patient-oriented research exists. Appointment at the Associate rank requires documented meritorious academic service on the faculty of a peer medical school and be recognized for contributions in a designated Area of Concentration. For additional information see the COAP guidelines for the Academic Clinician Track: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/assets/user-content/documents/Academic%20Review/COAP/Perelman%20School%20of%20Medicine%20COAP%20Guidelines.pdf"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187185": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Academic Clinician - Pediatric and Adolescent Gynecology, Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Adolescent Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Adolescent Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of medical and surgical gynecologic care of children and adolescents. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology and have completed a fellowship in Pediatric and Adolescent Gynecology or have significant experience in Pediatric and Adolescent Gynecology, with an ABOG-focused practice designation in Pediatric and Adolescent Gynecology. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical training and supervision of fellows, medical students and residents and participation in formal teaching curriculum. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient pediatric, adolescent, and adult gynecology care and pediatric, adolescent, and adult gynecologic surgery. The successful candidate would join the Division of Adolescent Medicine at the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia, the nation’s largest Adolescent Medicine division. The candidate would also join the Department of Surgery at the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia. The candidate would have an appointment at Hospital University Pennsylvania in the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology. Excellent clinical and interpersonal skills are required. A commitment to fellow, resident and medical student education is required. The successful candidate will receive fully covered malpractice insurance and practice in a supportive environment that provides professional and personal fulfillment and career-long learning."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179420": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Academic Clinician, Division of Integrated Behavioral Health- Cancer Center- CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pediatric psychology with a focus on psycho-oncology. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Pediatric psychology internship and fellowship required; Psychology license or license-eligible in PA and NJ. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic lectures to interns, fellows, residents, as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Other teaching responsibilities may include clinical supervision of psychology externs and interns; lectures to pediatric residents, hematology/oncology fellows, and psychiatry residents. Excellence in teaching is required. Clinical responsibilities may include pediatric psychology consultation and intervention for patients treated in the CHOP Cancer Center including clinical services and program development for patients and families treated at the Voorhees Specialty Care Center and other Cancer Center sites. There are opportunities for engagement in quality improvement and patient safety initiatives in the Cancer Center and the Department of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences including patient and caregiver support and staff wellness."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179416": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Academic Clinician, Division of Integrated Behavioral Health- CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of neuropsychology assessment in clinical care and research protocols with a special focus on autism. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Pediatric neuropsychology internship and fellowship required; certification in pediatric neuropsychology preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include high quality teaching including didactic lectures to interns, fellows, residents, as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Excellence in teaching is required. Other responsibilities may include clinical supervision of psychology externs, interns, and fellows; lectures to pediatric residents, radiology fellows, and psychiatry residents. Clinical responsibilities may include providing inpatient and/or outpatient services. Candidates must show evidence of continued excellence in clinical care and supervision. Other clinical responsibilities may include research assessments for participants in studies in the Radiology Division and clinical assessments in the Neuropsychology and Assessment Outpatient Program including for children with autism. There are opportunities for engagement in quality improvement and patient safety initiatives in the Department of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences. Research is not required for faculty that are on the AC Track."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188485": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, CE Track, Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Endocrinology and Diabetes Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board Certified in Pediatric Endocrinology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of CHOP residents and fellows as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical and translational research in areas such as type 2 diabetes, obesity and metabolic syndrome, type 1 diabetes, cystic fibrosis-related diabetes, neuroendocrine disorders and other endocrine diseases. Applicants should have a track record of publications and established scholarship in the field."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/167192": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, CE Track, Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes, Pediatric Thyroid Center",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Endocrinology and Diabetes Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified in Pediatric Endocrinology. We are seeking candidates who subspecilaize in pediatric thyroidology. Teaching responsibilities may include high quality teaching of CHOP fellows and residents as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Outpatient clinical obligations include general thyroid clinic, a multidisciplinary PTEN Hamartoma Tumor Syndrome Clinic, an Advanced Thyroid Cancer Therapeutics Clinic, and general endocrinology clinic. The Thyroid Center is equipped with point-of-care ultrasound (POCUS) machines to perform bedside head/neck ultrasound in the outpatient clinic setting and the applicant is expected to become proficient in performance and interpretation of POCUS. A multidisciplinary tumor board is conducted monthly with collaborators from cytology (Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania), pathology, radiology, and surgery. Clinic locations are in CHOP Main (University Place, Philadelphia), Voorhees NJ Subspecialty Center, and Chalfont PA Subspecialty Center. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical and/or translational research in thyroid disease, including congenital or acquired thyroid disease, thyroid nodules, thyroid cancer, and thyroid cancer predisposition syndromes. The Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes comprises more than 30 faculty with diverse clinical and investigative interests and has clinical programs with nearly 30,000 outpatient visits yearly. The Pediatric Thyroid Center was established in 2013 and is fully staffed with dedicated administrative support, nursing (RN and NP) support, and both clinical and translational research programs. Philadelphia is a vibrant city with a unique blend of modern high-rise office buildings and historic districts with centuries of old architecture. The area offers diverse outdoor opportunities, an open and exciting culture and an outstanding quality of life."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194507": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Clinician Educator",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Emergency Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. degree and be ABEM certified or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include bedside clinical teaching of emergency medicine residents and students. Additional teaching responsibilities include lectures, journal clubs, case conferences, simulation teaching, small group discussions, and others. Enthusiasm and dedication to educating our residents and students is highly valued in our department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical care to emergency department patients in one or more of our four city hospitals: Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), HUP at 54th and Cedar, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. Patients seen in our EDs include high acuity, complex patients, as well as patients with less acute illnesses and injuries. Penn Presbyterian Medical Center is a Level 1 Trauma Center. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing a scholarly program, with a focus in one or more of the following areas: critical care, clinical patient-oriented research, health systems research, medical education, ultrasound, toxicology, emergency medicine services, administrative leadership, global health, resuscitation, laboratory-based basic mechanisms of illness; and other EM-related sub-specialties. The effort scheduled for this research is offset by the establishment of independent funding support. Promotion on the CE track requires significant scholarly productivity."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185610": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Clinician Educator or Tenure Track, Adolescent Medicine- HIV/AIDS Research",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Adolescent Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Adolescent Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate Professor positions in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/eligible in Pediatrics or Internal Medicine and Adolescent Medicine strongly preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include inpatient and/or outpatient clinical and teaching responsibilities. Clinical responsibilities may include Inpatient and/or outpatient primary and specialty care in Adolescent Medicine at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and participate in clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows as a member of the Craig-Dalsimer Division of Adolescent Medicine. Multiple sites of practice are available including a primary care practice, specialty care satellite locations and inpatient units at CHOP and a behavioral health hospital. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include a primary focus on adolescent or young adult health research relevant to HIV prevention or care, which may interface with related domains of STIs, sexual/gender minority youth, substance use, mental health, health disparities, parent-teen relationships, community-engaged research, and similar areas. While both tenure and clinician-educator track faculty conduct methodological and collaborative research, tenure track faculty focus primarily on independent, investigator driven research while clinician-educator track faculty focus primarily on collaboration.  Depending on the Track, expectations will be to develop and lead a research program funded by independent research funding.  For more information about Perelman School of Medicine Faculty tracks please visit PSOM’s Faculty Career Development page . It is anticipated that this faculty member will be an active participant in the Penn CFAR research community, which provides extensive services and activities geared to advance HIV/AIDS research. Leadership positions in these areas may also be available, such as Co-Director for the Adolescent/Pediatric component of the CFAR Clinical Core. We are seeking candidates with a strong record of research productivity and scholarship demonstrating an established or emerging national reputation. Opportunities for collaborative clinical research are available related to education, continuous quality improvement, health services, health disparities, resiliency, STIs/HIV, pregnancy prevention, smoking, substance use, gender, eating disorders, weight regulation, depression and suicide."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/163529": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Clinician Educator, Division of Human Genetics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Human Genetics in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of human genetics research, with a track record of substantial scholarship. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of medical students, residents, fellows, and genetic counseling students. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient care and/or inpatient consultative services. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include engaging in funded research involving human genetics, genomic medicine, or translational therapeutics."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175778": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Clinician-Educator Academic Movement Disorders Physician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of evaluation and management of Parkinson’s disease, related disorders, and other movement disorders. Expertise in botulinum toxin injection and management of neurostimulators is preferred. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree and be board-certified or board-eligible in Neurology. Completion of a fellowship in Movement Disorders is also required. The successful candidate would be active in national/international organizations like the American Academy of Neurology (AAN) and the Movement Disorders Society (MDS). They would also be active in clinical trials at the organizational as well as the site level. They would mentor and drive academic productivity among fellows and residents. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient consultations and ongoing care of patients with Movement Disorders. Supervision of resident clinic and a minor component of inpatient care of general neurology patients (approximately 1-2 weeks per year) may be required. Clinical care will be primarily at Pennsylvania Hospital, but some coverage of satellite clinics in suburban locations may be available. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include an independent research program (e.g. K-series award leading to further independent funding) or an active collaborative role in integrated research programs. Scholarly productivity in peer-reviewed journals is expected."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180736": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Oculoplastics Specialist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of oculoplastics. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents, medical students, and fellows at the Scheie Eye Institute. Mentorship of early career faculty is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include providing medical and surgical oculoplastics care at the Scheie Eye Institute and one of Scheie's satellite offices. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include collaborative or independent research within the specific area of oculoplastics. Successful candidates will have a demonstrated record of scholarship."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180727": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Oculoplastics Specialist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of oculoplastics. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents, students, and fellows at the Scheie Eye Institute. Clinical responsibilities may include providing medical and surgical oculoplastics care at the Scheie Eye Institute and one of Scheie's satellite offices."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174458": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Specializing in Violence Prevention – Center for Violence Prevention at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of one or more of the six pillars of the center related to Violence Prevention research, with special consideration given to researchers conducting research related to gun violence. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Have demonstrated excellent track record in securing federal grants and have developed a clear line of violence prevention research. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic sessions with graduate students, medical fellows and residents, and postdoctoral fellows as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include patient care depending on the candidate, including but not limited to outpatient treatment, outpatient consultations, inpatient consultations, and inpatient attending responsibilities. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include maintaining an active research laboratory, supervising students and research staff, and mentoring postdoctoral fellows. Additional responsibilities include writing grants, reports, and manuscripts, developing collaborative and independent research programs, and coordinating federally-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators. Successful applicants will have evidence of federal funding and demonstrated success in fundamental and/or translational research relevant to violence prevention. The primary faculty appointment will be in the Department of Pediatrics or the department in the Perelman School of Medicine that provides the best scientific fit. The University of Pennsylvania is a vibrant team-science-oriented environment with elite pediatric-based research collaborators. The Perelman School of Medicine, with world-class medical, biological, and population scientists, is part of an integrated campus including the Schools of Arts & Sciences, School of Education, School of Social Policy and Practice, the Leonard Davis Institute of Health Economics, and the Center of Public Health Initiatives, which provide the ideal setting for cross-disciplinary collaboration and impactful research. CHOP is a world-class leader in the delivery of pediatric care, research, and training pediatric leaders of the future. The Center for Violence Prevention (CVP) develops, implements, and evaluates evidence-based programs to reduce the exposure to and impact of violence on patients and families across clinical and community settings. CVP uses a trauma-informed, community-based participatory research approach which is rooted in racial equity and social justice. The Center consists of six pillars: (1) Aggression and Bullying Prevention; (2) Community Violence & Trauma Support; (3) Intimate Partner Violence (IPV) Prevention; (4) Suicide Prevention; (5) Gun Safety; and (6) Professional Development and Training. CVP is uniquely positioned to conduct research that is authentic and meaningful because we have deep involvement in the programs that we are researching. CVP’s infrastructure supports a growing interdisciplinary network of 23 Scholars, 12 Associates and 50 staff members who provide thought leadership in areas such as gun safety, community violence, intimate partner violence, aggression and bullying, and racial microaggressions. CVP collaborates closely with other CHOP entities such as PolicyLab, Clinical Futures, and the Department of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry. We seek an energetic researcher who can conduct systematic research while, over time, mentor junior faculty, fellows, and graduate students."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188483": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Tenure Track, Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Endocrinology and Diabetes Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified in Pediatric Endocrinology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of CHOP residents and fellows as well as medical students from the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include research in areas such as beta cell biology, insulin signaling, pituitary development and disease as well as many other areas of research. Applicants should have a track record of extramural funding, have an established research program, and an outstanding record of publications."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/163551": {
      "title": "Associate Professor-Clinician Educator Track-Surgical Pathology with expertise in Thoracic Pathology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of surgical pathology with an established focus in Thoracic Pathology. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Certifications American Board of Pathology, AP-only or AP/CP. Teaching responsibilities may include medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include participation in the Surgical Pathology service with coverage of Thoracic Pathology services in Penn Medicine including the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Hospital and Pennsylvania Hospital and its affiliates, general frozen section service, autopsy service and night/weekend call. Coverage of additional pathology subspecialties in addition to thoracic will also be considered. The main practice site will be Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include development of an independent or highly collaborative research program (as PI, Co-PI or Co-I) in the area of anatomic pathology, particularly thoracic pathology."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158754": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/Full Professor of Medicine CE in Translational Medicine and Human Genetics - Penn Center for Genomic Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Translational Medicine and Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Translational Medicine and Human Genetics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Genomic Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include may include teaching medical students, residents and fellows within the clinical setting and serving as a research mentor. Clinical responsibilities may include may include care of patients in the outpatient setting and as an attending on an inpatient consult service. Clinical duties for preferred candidates with a PhD will be consistent with degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include engaging in funded research involving genomic medicine implementation research and clinical care. Evidence of scholarship is required in the Clinician Educator Track. Selected candidates will participate in the Penn Center for Genomic Medicine. The Division of Translational Medicine and Human Genetics comprises clinical and research faculty with diverse investigative interests and close affiliations with clinical departments at Penn Medicine as well as the neighboring Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Wistar Institute. There will be an expectation of the ability of selected candidate to provide management and/or leadership. Rank will be commensurate with experience. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194039": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/Professor in the Department of Cancer Biology in partnership with the Basser Center for BRCA",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Cancer Biology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Cancer Biology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the tenure track. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include focused classroom teaching in an existing area of expertise as well as mentoring graduate and undergraduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and other research trainees. Candidates must have a strong commitment to the educational mission of the University of Pennsylvania. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishment and maintenance of an externally funded, independent research program that leads to impactful publications focused on breast, ovarian, prostate, or pancreas cancer, or other cancers associated with inherited mutations in BRCA1 and BRCA2. The Basser Center and the Department of Cancer Biology value a supportive, cohesive, and collaborative culture. Successful candidates are expected to have either achieved success in areas broadly related to BRCA-associated cancers, or to have an established focus on the biology of breast, ovarian, pancreas or prostate cancers accompanied by future research plans to investigate the role of BRCA1/2 in these cancers. All candidates are expected to have demonstrated high-quality scholarship through publication in peer-reviewed journals and independent research funding. Basic or translational scientists interested in the mechanisms of tumor development and interception of tumors common in BRCA1/2 mutation carriers are highly sought. Areas of particular interest include: a) investigation of the haploinsufficent state and how this leads to cancer; b) tissue specificity related to BRCA1 and BRCA2 (why cancers emerge from breast, ovarian, prostate and pancreas when all cells in affected individuals are heterozygous) c) hormonal influences on DNA repair and tumorigenesis; d) early detection of cancer; and e) models of cancer initiation and interception. The Basser Center for BRCA was established at Penn Medicine's Abramson Cancer Center in 2012 as the first comprehensive center for the research, treatment, and prevention of BRCA-related cancers. More information on the Basser Center for BRCA can be found at www.basser.org. Applications will be evaluated on a rolling basis, but to ensure full consideration applicants are encouraged to apply by November 15. Applicants will be evaluated based on the following required documents: 1. Cover letter (Highlight past and proposed research and its synergies with Penn Cancer Biology, Basser Center, and the University, 1 page maximum). 2. Curriculum vitae (Highlight 3 to 5 impactful publications using several sentences to provide context about the specific advances for the field and the candidate’s role in these studies). 3. Anonymized Executive Summary (one page max): Please provide brief, anonymized responses to the following prompts, with further details to be provided in additional documents: 1) Briefly describe your two most important research contributions to date; 2) Describe your vision for your independent research program, including “big picture” questions that you plan to address in your laboratory; 3) Highlight how your work will contribute to the mission of the Basser Center; 4) Describe any contributions to teaching, mentoring, and scientific community. 4. Statement of significant research contributions and plans for an independent research program (2-3 pages). This document should briefly describe past research accomplishments -research questions, an applicant’s intellectual contributions, the research findings and significance, and future research plan as well as opportunities for integration and collaboration with Penn Cancer Biology, the Basser Center and the University. 5. Statement of Teaching, Mentoring, and Community (1 page). This statement will focus on contributions and commitment to the advancement of collaborative research, mentoring, teaching, and inclusion in science. We seek candidates with a demonstrated track record of and/or plans for promoting an environment focused on collaborative and inclusive research, and high-quality mentoring and teaching. This document should briefly describe candidate’s prior or future actions towards research collaborations, teaching and mentoring of trainees in the lab and classroom, service to the scientific and/or broader community."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192698": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor - Clinician Educator Track - Director of the Division of Anatomic Pathology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Surgical Pathology Subspecialty including Thoracic Pathology, Gastrointestinal Pathology or other surgical pathology subspecialities. Prior physician leadership or administrative experience is preferred. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. The successful candidate will be board-certified in Anatomic Pathology (AP) or Anatomic and Clinical Pathology (AP/CP) by the American Board of Pathology and eligible to obtain an unrestricted license to practice medicine in Pennsylvania. Rank and remuneration will be determined according to the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Teaching responsibilities may include medical students, residents, fellows, and post-doctoral students. Clinical responsibilities may include: • Providing strategic, academic, and operational leadership for the Division of Anatomic Pathology, advancing the division’s academic mission while ensuring the delivery of high-quality diagnostic services. • Maintain excellence in clinical practice through oversight of quality assurance, regulatory compliance, and laboratory operations, with strict adherence to CLIA and CAP standards. • Lead the development and implementation of innovative Anatomic Pathology programs, technologies, and initiatives that align with institutional priorities and support continued growth. • Serve as a key leader on the Executive Pathology Committee, contributing to the integration, coordination, and oversight of Anatomic Pathology services across the University of Pennsylvania Health System. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include: • Playing a pivotal role in advancing the institution’s research and academic mission. • Consistent with the selected academic appointment series, the individual will contribute as a research collaborator or serve as a leader of clinically oriented research programs. • Leveraging the rich collaborative environment of the University of Pennsylvania Health System, the candidate will be expected to champion faculty scholarship, strengthen translational and clinical research efforts, cultivate interdisciplinary collaborations, support grant development and funding opportunities, and maintain a nationally recognized scholarly portfolio through publications, presentations, and academic leadership activities. Candidates should possess national recognition for their professional contributions, exhibit excellent interpersonal and leadership abilities, and have significant experience overseeing large teams while fostering the growth and career development of junior pathologists."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172939": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor Academic Clinician Cardiac Anesthesiologist – CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Pediatric Anesthesiology with a focus on Pediatric Cardiothoracic Anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspeciality certification or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology, the equivalent, or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching in our formal didactic lecture program as well as the informal teaching of medical students, residents, fellows, and other healthcare professionals working in the cardiothoracic operating rooms and procedural areas. Attendance and participation in lectures, presentations, and conferences within the division, as well as multi-disciplinary conferences, is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include direct patient care and medical direction in the cardiothoracic operating rooms and procedural areas. Primary practice is located at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Experience in pediatric cardiothoracic anesthesiology and evidence of academic productivity and leadership in projects related to an area of focus is required. The Academic Clinician track is intended for faculty members who demonstrate impactful contributions to clinical care and education and who develop an Area of Concentration (AoC) in which they become recognized. We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/flpd/career-development/ ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/163487": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor Academic Clinician Cardiac Critical Care Medicine - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Cardiac Critical Care Medicine with a focus on Pediatric Cardiac Critical Care Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABP certification or board eligibility, and Pennsylvania licensure is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching in our formal didactic lecture program as well as the informal teaching of medical students, residents, fellows, and other healthcare professionals working in the Pediatric Cardiac Intensive Care Unit. Attendance and participation in lectures, presentations, and conferences within the division as well as multi-disciplinary conferences are expected. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical practice in the Pediatric Cardiac Intensive Care Unit. The major emphases of the Academic Clinician track are high-quality engagement and impact in clinical care, education, and excellence in a chosen area of concentration, as well as sustained professionalism. Scholarship responsibilities will include but are not limited to education service and leadership, community service, quality and safety, health equity, health policy, global health, and diversity and inclusion. Primary practice is located at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Experience in pediatric cardiac critical care medicine and evidence of academic productivity and leadership in projects related to an area of focus is required. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177414": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor Academic Clinician General Anesthesiology - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Anesthesiology with a focus on Pediatric Anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspecialty certification or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology and Pennsylvania licensure are required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching both in our formal didactic lecture program as well as in the informal teaching of medical students, residents, fellows, and other healthcare professionals in the Operating Rooms. Attendance and participation in presentations, small groups, simulation sessions, and/or multidisciplinary conferences is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include direct patient care and medical direction in the Operating Rooms and other anesthetizing locations at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. The practice locations include the Philadelphia and King of Prussia campuses. The Academic Clinician track is intended for faculty members who demonstrate impactful contributions to clinical care and education and who develop an Area of Concentration (AoC) in which they become recognized. We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/flpd/career-development/ ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172941": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor Clinician-Educator Cardiac Anesthesiologist – CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Pediatric Anesthesiology with a focus on cardiothoracic anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspecialty certification or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology, the equivalent, or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching both in our formal didactic lecture program as well as in the informal teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the cardiothoracic operating rooms and procedural areas. Attendance and participation in lectures, presentations, and conferences within the division as well as multidisciplinary conferences is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include direct patient care and medical direction in the cardiothoracic operating rooms and procedural area. Primary practice is located at the Philadelphia campus of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include investigator-initiated and collaborative research.  The non-tenure clinician educator track involves a substantial commitment to research. Evidence of continuous scholarly productivity reflecting a defined focus and mentoring of medical students, residents, and fellows in their own scholarly pursuits will be required. Are you interested in this position but are unsure if it's the right fit? We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/faculty-career-development/career-development/."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177415": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor Clinician-Educator General Anesthesiology - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Anesthesiology with a focus on Pediatric Anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspecialty certification or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology and Pennsylvania licensure required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching both in our formal didactic lecture program as well as in the informal teaching of medical students, residents and fellows rotating through the Operating Rooms. Attendance and participation in lectures, presentations, and conferences within the division as well as multidisciplinary conferences is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of clinical anesthesia and medical direction in the Operating Rooms and other anesthetizing locations at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Locations include the Philadelphia and King of Prussia campuses. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include investigator-initiated and collaborative research. In addition to excellence in teaching and clinical care, responsibilities include investigator-initiated and collaborative research. The non-tenure Clinician Educator track involves a substantial commitment to research and evidence of continuous scholarly productivity reflecting a defined focus is required. We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178680": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor Tenure Track – Artificial Intelligence in Medicine (CHOP)",
      "description": "Posted: Dec 15, 2025 Deadline: Dec 15, 2027 Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include participating in graduate and/or medical student education; mentoring trainees at multiple career stages; presenting lectures and leading didactic sessions as appropriate. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing and maintaining an independent, extramurally funded research program. The faculty search is in the field of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Medicine. We are particularly interested in candidates who creatively develop and apply novel AI technologies to drive biological discoveries and medical innovations. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: foundational AI models for genetic, multi-omic, imaging, and EHR data; multimodal AI approaches enabling precision diagnostics and therapeutics; and generative AI for biomolecule engineering and design. AI researchers who combine computational and experimental research programs are also welcome to apply. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine. The position is affiliated with the Center for Computational and Genomic Medicine (CCGM) at the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP). CCGM, a CHOP Research Institute Center of Emphasis, is housed in the state-of-the-art Colket Translational Research Building. A generous recruitment package and lab space will be provided, together with excellent institutional and core research resources. The recruitment is part of a campus-wide initiative to promote AI innovations and research-driven precision medicine."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177117": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor, Academic Clinician – Sleep Center",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Pulmonary Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary Medicine in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible in Sleep Medicine. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students from the University of Pennsylvania School of Medicine as well as residents and fellows from the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia. Teaching can take place in a variety of settings such as lecturing, small group, clinical and/or didactic sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the care of patients with sleep disorders in the Sleep Center and polysomnogram reading according to the needs of the Sleep Center."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191895": {
      "title": "Asst. Professor, Pediatric Otolaryngology, AC Track at CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Otorhinolaryngology - Head and Neck Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Otorhinolaryngology: Head and Neck Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Pediatric Otolaryngology with a focus on sleep, airway disorders, otology, and head & neck surgery. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Certification by the American Board of Otolaryngology and successful completion of an ACGME-accredited Pediatric Otolaryngology fellowship is required. Teaching responsibilities may include medical students, residents and fellows, advanced practice providers as well as formal lecture opportunities. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient and outpatient clinical care at CHOP Main/University City and specialty care satellite offices and surgical centers in New Jersey. Research is not required in the academic clinician track."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184500": {
      "title": "Benign Hematology/AC Track Faculty Position, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of hematology & benign hematology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified or board eligible in Hematology and Medical Oncology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, medical residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients in the outpatient practices at the Penn Presbyterian Medical Center and inpatient call. The selected candidate will have experience in general hematology and benign/malignant hematology. Clinical responsibilities will be based on a hospitalist/intensivist model."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/163020": {
      "title": "Biomedical Optics Research Assistant Professor Resuscitation Center - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include collaborative or independent research of high quality with distinctive, original, and expert intellectual contributions. Research experience in biomedical optics and its applications in translational medicine, with a focus on developing and applying advanced optical techniques for monitoring physiological parameters in clinical settings is required. The successful candidate will be expected to secure independent research grant support, usually from federal organizations, in addition to support from participation in collaborative grants. Mentorship of graduate students or postdoctoral fellows, while not required, should be of high quality. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/163751": {
      "title": "Breast Imaging - Academic Clinician - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Breast Imaging. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree.  Applicants must be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with sub-specialty training in Breast Radiology. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision of residents and breast radiology fellows and lecturing to medical students, radiology residents, fellows, and trainees from other departments. In addition, the candidate will prepare learning materials and lectures, teaching posters and presentations for national review. The successful candidate will be an accomplished educator and be expected to serve in an educational leadership role within the Breast Radiology Division. Mentorship of junior faculty is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include utilizing the most advanced breast imaging technology available to provide individually tailored, comprehensive evaluations for the early and precise detection and diagnosis of breast diseases. The successful candidate will also conduct high-quality interventional breast procedures, including mammographic, sonographic, and MRI guided biopsies. Leadership responsibilities may include representation of breast radiology to committees of the department, hospital(s) or School of Medicine, serving as Lead Interpreting Physician, developing operational oversight and efficiency, and designated roles within the department. The University of Pennsylvania School of Medicine leads the nation in medical education, training, clinical care, and research. OnePenn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veteran Affairs Medical Center, as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers located in Pennsylvania and New Jersey. Licenses in Pennsylvania and New Jersey will be required. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192546": {
      "title": "Breast Imaging - Clinician--Educator - Junior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Breast Imaging. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with sub-specialty training in Breast Imaging. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision of residents and breast imaging fellows and lecturing to medical students, radiology residents, fellows, and trainees from other departments. Clinical responsibilities may include utilizing the most advanced breast imaging technology available to provide individually tailored, comprehensive evaluations for the early and precise detection and diagnosis of breast diseases. The successful candidate will conduct high-quality interventional breast procedures, including stereotactic, ultrasound-guided, and MRI-guided biopsies. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing a focused body of research in a field within breast imaging. This includes clinical and translational research on applying imaging methods to the detection, diagnosis, and evaluation of breast disease. The successful candidate will have prior research experience and demonstrated evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship. We will provide ample support and mentorship for research. The clinical mission of the Division of Breast Imaging is to provide individually tailored comprehensive evaluations for the early detection and diagnosis of breast diseases. Our Breast Imaging Division, accredited by the American College of Radiology, provides screening and problem-solving mammography, breast MRI, and multimodality intervention for outpatients at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and its satellite locations."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176877": {
      "title": "Breast Imaging - Instructor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of Breast Imaging. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology (ABR) certified or board-eligible in Diagnostic Radiology and have sub-specialty training in Breast Imaging or equivalent experience. Responsibilities may include utilizing the most advanced breast imaging technology available to provide individually tailored, comprehensive evaluations for the early and precise detection and diagnosis of breast diseases. The successful candidate will conduct high-quality interventional breast procedures, including stereotactic, ultrasound-guided, and MRI-guided biopsies. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop research credentials. Instructors are provided with research and educational support to prepare them for an academic and/or clinical career. A specialized research focus may be developed in consultation with the Division Chief. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center (PAVMC), as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193395": {
      "title": "Cancer Rehabilitation - Assistant Professor - Academic Clinician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of palliative care and/or cancer rehabilitation. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible by the American Board of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation. Candidates should bring to this position expertise through special experiences or additional fellowship training in palliative care or cancer rehabilitation. Teaching responsibilities may include leading multidisciplinary rehabilitation teams and providing high quality education for students, residents and allied professionals. Clinical responsibilities may include working closely with other surgical and non-surgical teams to provide the highest level of interdisciplinary care to a wide range of patients in both inpatient and outpatient care settings. Selected candidates must have excellent, well refined interpersonal skills and leadership abilities to effectively lead our interdisciplinary rehabilitation teams. Candidates should have strong clinical training, enthusiasm, and a commitment to furthering our clinical services and advancing our academic missions. As an academic faculty member, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to provide outstanding teaching and mentoring for Penn medical students and residents as well as allied professionals."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193398": {
      "title": "Cancer Rehabilitation - Associate Professor - Academic Clinician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of palliative care and/or cancer rehabilitation. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible by the American Board of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation. Candidates should bring to this position expertise through special experiences or additional fellowship training in palliative care or cancer rehabilitation. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and mentoring of Penn medical students and residents as well as allied professionals. This position includes leadership responsibilities for the cancer rehabilitation fellowship. Clinical responsibilities may include Clinical responsibilities may include working closely with other surgical and non-surgical teams to provide the highest level of interdisciplinary care to a wide range of patients in both inpatient and outpatient care settings. Selected candidates must have excellent, well refined interpersonal skills and leadership abilities to effectively lead our interdisciplinary rehabilitation teams. Candidates should have strong clinical training, enthusiasm, and a commitment to furthering our clinical services and advancing our academic missions. As an academic faculty member, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to provide outstanding teaching and mentoring for Penn medical students and residents as well as allied professionals."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/157544": {
      "title": "Cardiovascular Imaging - Academic Clinician - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with appropriate sub-specialty training. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision of residents and cardiovascular imaging fellows and lecturing to medical students, radiology residents, fellows and trainees from other departments. Clinical responsibilities may include interpreting in all aspects of cardiovascular radiology, including cardiac CT, cardiac MRI, and vascular CTA and MRA. The successful candidate will also participate in shared after-hours and weekend coverage. The Penn Radiology Cardiovascular Imaging Division offers specialized expertise to the world-renowned Penn Aorta Program. This division handles a high volume and variety of cases, including coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA), CT scans for structural heart disease, TAVR (transcatheter aortic valve replacement), TMVR (transcatheter mitral valve replacement), and TTVR (transcatheter tricuspid valve replacement). Additionally, cardiac MRI is conducted for various clinical indications. The radiologists collaborate closely with cardiologists to provide comprehensive care. Penn Radiology offers clinical services at several locations: the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania and New Jersey. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181142": {
      "title": "Cardiovascular Imaging - Academic Clinician - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with appropriate sub-specialty training. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision of residents and cardiovascular imaging fellows, and lecturing to medical students, radiology residents, fellows, and trainees from other departments. In addition, the candidate will prepare learning materials and lectures, as well as teaching posters and presentations, for national review. The successful candidate will be an accomplished educator and will be expected to serve in an educational leadership role within the Cardiovascular Imaging Division. Mentorship of junior faculty is expected. Clinical responsibilities may include interpreting in all aspects of cardiovascular radiology, including cardiac CT, cardiac MRI, and vascular CTA and MRA. The successful candidate will also participate in shared after-hours and weekend coverage. The Penn Radiology Cardiovascular Imaging Division offers specialized expertise to the world-renowned Penn Aorta Program. This division handles a high volume and variety of cases, including coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA), CT scans for structural heart disease, TAVR (transcatheter aortic valve replacement), TMVR (transcatheter mitral valve replacement), and TTVR (transcatheter tricuspid valve replacement). Additionally, cardiac MRI is conducted for various clinical indications. The radiologists collaborate closely with cardiologists to provide comprehensive care. This position requires 3-5 years of experience. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Penn Radiology offers clinical services at several locations: the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/157534": {
      "title": "Cardiovascular Imaging - Clinician--Educator - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with appropriate sub-specialty training. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision of residents and cardiovascular imaging fellows and lecturing to medical students, radiology residents, fellows and trainees from other departments. Clinical responsibilities may include interpreting in all aspects of cardiovascular radiology, including cardiac CT, cardiac MRI, and vascular CTA and MRA. The successful candidate will also participate in shared after-hours and weekend coverage. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing a focused body of research in a field within cardiovascular radiology. Scholarly works are broad, and include novel cardiovascular imaging techniques, MR and CT physics, health services research, health policy, and artificial intelligence. The department fosters a collaborative environment, encouraging partnerships across clinical disciplines, with basic scientists, and beyond the school of medicine. The successful candidate will have prior research experience and have demonstrated evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship. Ample support and mentorship for research will be provided. The Penn Radiology Cardiovascular Imaging Division offers specialized expertise to the world-renowned Penn Aorta Program. This division performs a high volume of coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA), as well as CT scans for structural heart disease, TAVR (transcatheter aortic valve replacement), TMVR (transcatheter mitral valve replacement), and TTVR (transcatheter tricuspid valve replacement). Additionally, cardiac MRI is conducted for various clinical indications. The radiologists collaborate closely with cardiologists to provide comprehensive care. Penn Radiology offers clinical services at several locations: the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania and New Jersey. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/157542": {
      "title": "Cardiovascular Imaging - Clinician--Educator -Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with appropriate sub-specialty training. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision of residents and cardiovascular imaging fellows and lecturing to medical students, radiology residents, fellows and trainees from other departments. Clinical responsibilities may include interpreting in all aspects of cardiovascular radiology, including cardiac CT, cardiac MRI, and vascular CTA and MRA. The successful candidate will also participate in shared after-hours and weekend coverage. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include leading a focused body of research in the field of Cardiovascular Imaging. This includes novel cardiovascular imaging techniques, MR and CT physics, health services research, health policy, and artificial intelligence. The successful candidate will have prior research experience, have demonstrated evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship, and be expected to provide mentorship to aspiring junior faculty seeking to develop a research career in the field of cardiothoracic imaging. The Penn Radiology Cardiovascular Imaging Division offers specialized expertise to the world-renowned Penn Aorta Program. This division handles a high volume and variety of cases, including coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA), CT scans for structural heart disease, TAVR (transcatheter aortic valve replacement), TMVR (transcatheter mitral valve replacement), and TTVR (transcatheter tricuspid valve replacement). Additionally, cardiac MRI is conducted for various clinical indications. The radiologists collaborate closely with cardiologists to provide comprehensive care. This position requires a minimum of 3-5 years of experience. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Penn Radiology offers clinical services at several locations: the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania and New Jersey. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176881": {
      "title": "Cardiovascular Imaging - Instructor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of Cardiovascular Imaging. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology-certified or eligible, with appropriate sub-specialty training. Responsibilities may include interpreting in all aspects of cardiovascular radiology, including cardiac CT, cardiac MRI, and vascular CTA and MRA. The successful candidate will also participate in shared after-hours and weekend coverage. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop research credentials. Instructors are provided with research and educational support to prepare them for an academic and/or clinical career. A specialized research focus may be developed in consultation with the Division Chief. The Penn Radiology Cardiovascular Imaging Division offers specialized expertise to the world-renowned Penn Aorta Program. This division handles a high volume and variety of cases, including coronary computed tomography angiography (CTA), CT scans for structural heart disease, TAVR (transcatheter aortic valve replacement), TMVR (transcatheter mitral valve replacement), and TTVR (transcatheter tricuspid valve replacement). Additionally, cardiac MRI is conducted for various clinical indications. The radiologists collaborate closely with cardiologists to provide comprehensive care. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center (PAVMC), as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/159149": {
      "title": "CE Track Faculty Position, Genitourinary Cancers - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of genitourinary cancer. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board certified or board eligible in Medical Oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching hematology/oncology fellows, medical residents, and medical students. Additionally, the successful applicant will be expected to provide education, mentorship, and research support to hematology/oncology fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include re of patients with genitourinary cancer, including prostate, bladder, testicular, and renal malignancies in an outpatient setting and as an attending on the inpatient service at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP). Research or scholarship responsibilities may include the ability of the selected candidate to develop and grow an independent research program in translational genitourinary oncology. Evidence of scholarship is required on the clinician educator track. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/159148": {
      "title": "CE Track Faculty Position, Lymphoma/Histiocytosis/Castleman's Disease - Senior ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of lymphoma, histiocytosis, and Castleman's Disease. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board certified or board eligible in Medical Oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching hematology/oncology fellows, medical residents, and medical students. Additionally, the successful applicant will be expected to provide education, mentorship, and research support to hematology/oncology fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients with lymphoma, Histiocytosis, and Castleman's Disease in an outpatient setting and as an attending on the inpatient service at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP). Clinical care will also include evaluating patients for autologous stem cell transplantation and other cellular therapies. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include the ability of the selected candidate to develop and grow an independent research program in translational malignant hematology. The selected candidate will also develop ongoing clinical and research programs for Castleman's disease, working closely with the Castleman's Disease Collaborative Network in the recruitment of patients, both for clinical information and biobanking. The candidate will create a framework for clinical and translational research in histiocytic disorders. Evidence of scholarship is required on the clinician educator track. The successful candidate will have an established record of independent funding, high impact publications, and a strong national/international reputation. There will be an expectation of high-quality research, which leads to scholarship. There will be an expectation of the ability of the selected candidate to provide management and/or leadership. Rank will be commensurate with experience. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192096": {
      "title": "CE Track Faculty Position, Melanoma - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Medical Oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching hematology/oncology fellows, medical residents and medical students. Additionally, the successful applicant will be expected to provide education, mentorship, and research support to hematology/oncology fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include caring for patients with melanoma and other skin cancers in an outpatient setting and as an attending on the inpatient service (solid oncology, cellular immunotherapy, or both) at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP). Research or scholarship responsibilities may include focusing on translational research to enhance the melanoma and skin cancers immunotherapy research program. Scholarly productivity is required on the clinician educator track. The selected candidate will have an interest in translational research aimed at advancing our melanoma and skin cancer immunotherapy research program. Faculty on the Clinician-Educator are expected to demonstrate a strong record of scholarly productivity."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189719": {
      "title": "Center for Inherited Heart Disease, Academic Clinician Track - Junior rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of cardiomyopathy is preferred. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/board eligible in Internal Medicine and Cardiovascular Diseases is required. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in small group workshops and providing clinical education to medical students, medical residents, and cardiology fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include evaluation and treatment of patients with inherited cardiovascular disorders including one or more the following: inherited cardiomyopathy, aortopathy, arrhythmia, and dyslipidemia and others. Candidates will provide services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and associated practice sites. Faculty benefit from an unparalleled ecosystem of collaboration, working alongside internationally recognized leaders across disciplines and engaging in cutting-edge, translational research that directly informs clinical practice. The institution’s robust infrastructure—including access to interdisciplinary centers, advanced clinical programs, and expansive research funding— supports meaningful career development across clinical, research, educational, and leadership pathways. Philadelphia offers a rich and vibrant cultural landscape, with renowned institutions such as the Philadelphia Museum of Art, the Kimmel Center for the Performing Arts, and a nationally recognized dining scene. The city combines historic character with modern livability, featuring walkable neighborhoods, diverse communities, and a relatively accessible cost of living compared to peer cities. The University provides a comprehensive and highly competitive benefits package, including multiple retirement savings options and generous tuition benefits for eligible dependents—further enhancing the long-term value of a faculty appointment. Collectively, Penn Medicine and Philadelphia represent an exceptional opportunity for individuals seeking to advance their careers within a collaborative, high-impact academic environment while enjoying the cultural, professional, and lifestyle advantages of a premier urban setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189716": {
      "title": "Center for Inherited Heart Disease, Academic Clinician, Senior ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of cardiomyopathy. There will be an expectation of the ability of the selected candidate to provide management and/or leadership. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification in Internal Medicine and Cardiovascular Diseases is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in small group workshops and providing clinical education to medical students, medical residents, and cardiology fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include evaluation and treatment of patients with inherited cardiovascular disorders including one or more the following: inherited cardiomyopathy, aortopathy, arrhythmia, and dyslipidemia and others. Candidates will provide services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and affiliated practice sites. Faculty benefit from an unparalleled ecosystem of collaboration, working alongside internationally recognized leaders across disciplines and engaging in cutting-edge, translational research that directly informs clinical practice. The institution’s robust infrastructure—including access to interdisciplinary centers, advanced clinical programs, and expansive research funding— supports meaningful career development across clinical, research, educational, and leadership pathways. Philadelphia offers a rich and vibrant cultural landscape, with renowned institutions such as the Philadelphia Museum of Art, the Kimmel Center for the Performing Arts, and a nationally recognized dining scene. The city combines historic character with modern livability, featuring walkable neighborhoods, diverse communities, and a relatively accessible cost of living compared to peer cities. The University provides a comprehensive and highly competitive benefits package, including multiple retirement savings options and generous tuition benefits for eligible dependents—further enhancing the long-term value of a faculty appointment. Collectively, Penn Medicine and Philadelphia represent an exceptional opportunity for individuals seeking to advance their careers within a collaborative, high-impact academic environment while enjoying the cultural, professional, and lifestyle advantages of a premier urban setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194473": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Genetics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dean's Office Location: Philadelphia Advancing Discovery Defining the Future of Genomic Medicine The Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks an accomplished and visionary scientific leader to serve as Chair of the Department of Genetics. THE OPPORTUNITY The next Chair will lead a highly accomplished, collaborative, and growing department and shape its next phase of scientific distinction, institutional impact, and national prominence. Penn's extraordinary research ecosystem, including Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP), Penn Engineering, the Wistar Institute, and numerous interdisciplinary centers and institutes, offers an exceptional platform for advancing genetics and genomic medicine. DEPARTMENT AND ROLE Established in 1965, the Department of Genetics has been a leading academic community for discovery and innovation in genetics and genomics. Today the Department includes more than 30 faculty members, working across human genetics and genomics, evolutionary and population genetics, genome engineering, epigenetics, RNA biology, functional genomics, computational and statistical genomics, rare disease genetics, cancer genetics, neurogenetics, and precision medicine. The Chair will provide strategic, scientific, educational, and administrative leadership and will: Articulate and execute a bold vision for the future of genetics and genomic medicine. Recruit, mentor, and develop exceptional faculty and sustain a rigorous scientific community. Advance research excellence from fundamental discovery through translational and precision medicine. Strengthen education and training across graduate, medical, postdoctoral, and undergraduate programs. Build interdisciplinary partnerships across Penn, CHOP, the Wistar Institute, and affiliated institutions. Steward departmental resources and core facilities and expand philanthropic engagement and visibility. CANDIDATE PROFILE Candidates must hold an MD, PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent terminal degree and be eligible for appointment to the Standing Faculty at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor at the Perelman School of Medicine of the University of Pennsylvania. The successful candidate will have an internationally respected record of scholarship, sustained scientific productivity, substantial academic leadership experience, demonstrated excellence in mentorship and faculty development, and strong operational and financial acumen. A collaborative leadership style, the ability to lead change and deliver measurable results, and experience with or aptitude for development and donor relations are essential. APPLICATION PROCEDURE Applicants should submit an an online application with curriculum vitae, letter of interest, and research statement, to the attention of Nancy A. Speck, PhD, Chair of the Search Committee. First consideration will be given to applications received by November 10, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193652": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dean's Office Location: Philadelpia The Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania invites applications and nominations for the position of Chair of the Department of Medicine. Founded by John Morgan in 1765, Penn’s Department of Medicine is the nation's first department of medicine and has a rich history, with a long tradition of excellence in patient care, research and education. Since its founding, the Department has shaped the field by pioneering foundational research, clinical care and cutting-edge educational paradigms. The Department has systematically built programs that have become deeply integrated into the fabric of Penn Medicine, the University, and the medical community. In addition to excellence in its tripartite mission, the Department of Medicine has substantive ties to multiple centers, institutes, departments and other schools on campus. The Chair of the Department directs 13 divisions representing the full breadth of internal medicine and its subspecialties, with more than 700 full-time and over 450 associated faculty and Penn Medicine Clinicians, in addition to over 2,100 professional and support staff. The Department performs 880,000 procedures and treats 380,00 inpatients annually at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), the Corporal Michael J. Crescenz Department of Veterans Affairs Medical Center (CVAMC), with four additional hospitals across the region. It provides outpatient services for nearly 780,000 delivered across 73 outpatient practices. The Department is a member of the Clinical Practices of the University of Pennsylvania (CPUP) and the Chair serves as a member of the Board of Directors of CPUP whose primary role is to coordinate the tripartite mission of Penn Medicine’s 18 clinical departments. Qualified candidates hold a MD degree with active board certification in internal medicine or a relevant subspecialty and licensed or eligible for medical licensure in Pennsylvania. Dual degrees are welcome. Candidates’ academic achievement must support appointment at the Professor level in the Standing Faculty of the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania. In addition, candidates must possess strong leadership skills suited to a matrixed environment; the ability to develop and execute innovative strategies; demonstrated experience leading effective clinical operations; a highly respected academic record; a commitment to faculty development, retention, and recruitment; and experience in development and donor relations. The executive search firm, Isaacson Miller, is assisting Penn Medicine with this search. All interested applicants are invited to send their curriculum vitae and letter of interest to the attention of Jasmine Miller at: jmiller@imsearch.com . Applicants must also apply for this position via this online system. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled, although indication of interest is encouraged by November 9, 2026, for full consideration."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186625": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Neurology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dean's Office Location: Philadelphia The Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania invites applications and nominations for the position of Chair of the Department of Neurology. Founded by Dr. Horatio Wood in 1871, Penn Neurology is the nation's first department of neurology and has a rich history, with a long tradition of excellence in patient care, research and education in both adult and pediatric neurology. Since its founding, Penn Neurology has shaped the field by pioneering essential neurologic treatments and diagnostic techniques. The Department has systematically built programs that have become deeply integrated into the fabric of Penn Medicine, the University, and the community. In addition to excellence in its tripartite mission, the Department of Neurology has substantive ties to multiple centers, institutes, departments and other schools on campus. The Chair of the Department directs nearly 200 full-time and associated faculty engaged in a comprehensive range of clinical activities organized into 20 clinical divisions and programs, with an additional 465 professional and support staff. For outpatient care, the Chair oversees 12 facilities and in FY2025, the Department performed over 70,000 outpatient visits, with specialty practice sites contributing to an additional 26,000 visits. In the same year, Penn Neurology discharged over 1,800 inpatients and saw nearly 12,000 consults on the inpatient service. Major hospital sites for clinical and educational activities include the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Pennsylvania Hospital and Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Corporal Michael J. Crescenz Department of Veterans Affairs Medical Center, all institutions of great distinction. The Department is a member of the Clinical Practices of the University of Pennsylvania (CPUP) and the Chair serves as a member of the Board of Directors of CPUP whose primary role is to coordinate the tripartite mission of Penn Medicine’s 18 clinical departments. Qualified candidates hold an MD degree with active board certification in neurology. Dual degrees are welcome. Candidates must qualify for faculty appointment as Associate Professor or Professor rank in the Standing Faculty of the Perelman School of Medicine (PSOM) at the University of Pennsylvania. In addition, candidates must possess strong leadership skills suited to a matrixed environment; the ability to develop and execute innovative strategies; demonstrated experience leading effective clinical operations; a highly respected academic record; a commitment to faculty development, retention, and recruitment; and experience in development and donor relations. The executive search firm, Korn Ferry, is assisting Penn Medicine with this search. All interested applicants are invited to send their curriculum vitae and letter of interest to the attention of Amber Gornik at: amber.gornik@kornferry.com . Applicants must also apply for this position via this posting. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled, although indication of interest is encouraged by June 22, 2026, for full consideration."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182774": {
      "title": "Chief of Breast & Gynecologic Services (Associate or Full Professor)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiation Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiation Oncology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. A minimum of five years of clinical experience in gynecologic brachytherapy, with comprehensive expertise in high-dose rate (HDR) treatment options for cervical, uterine, and vaginal cancers is required. The candidate must have a proven ability to lead and manage a women's health team of four or more faculty physicians, with prior experience in a formal leadership capacity strongly preferred. Additionally, the successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of achievement in research and scholarly activities, reflecting a commitment to advancing the field of gynecologic radiation oncology. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. It is required to be Board Certified in Radiation Oncology by the American Board of Radiology. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching, training, and mentoring of radiation oncology residents, medical physics residents, medical physics graduate students, and visiting physics residents or trainees from other institutions and countries. In addition to these core responsibilities, this role encompasses both formal and informal teaching engagements, including active participation in resident didactic series, serving in capacities both as a lecturer and as an in-person discussant. Clinical responsibilities may include providing highly specialized clinical care with an emphasis on advanced gynecologic brachytherapy. This role will encompass the delivery of high-dose rate (HDR) brachytherapy for the treatment of cervical, uterine, and vaginal cancers, utilizing state-of-the-art, accredited technology. While the clinical focus of this position is rooted in the management of gynecologic malignancies, it will include care of other patients under the Women’s Health Service, such as those with breast cancer. Candidate will oversee the Breast & Gyn Services; candidate's scope of clinical practice will extend beyond brachytherapy to include a comprehensive array of treatment modalities, such as conventional radiation therapy, stereotactic body radiotherapy (SBRT), proton therapy, photon and proton reirradiation, and total body irradiation (TBI), ensuring the highest standard of individualized, multidisciplinary care for all patients served. In addition to these clinical responsibilities, this position carries a significant leadership role within the department. The selected candidate will serve as Chief of both the Breast and Gynecologic Oncology Services, providing strategic oversight, clinical direction, and administrative leadership across both service lines. In this capacity, the candidate will be expected to foster collaboration, drive programmatic growth, and uphold the department's commitment to excellence in patient care, education, and research. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include maintaining an active and productive research program with a focus on women's health, particularly in the area of gynecologic brachytherapy. This will include leading and/or participating in clinical trials that advance the field and contribute to improved patient outcomes. The candidate will be expected to disseminate their scholarly work through publication in peer-reviewed, high-impact scientific journals, with an emphasis on contributing as a first or last author. In addition, the candidate must possess, or demonstrate the clear potential to develop, a nationally and internationally recognized reputation in the field, reflecting a sustained commitment to advancing the science and practice of gynecologic brachytherapy and women's health. Penn Radiation Oncology is dedicated to a three-part mission of excellence in patient care, basic and translational research, and the education of residents and students. We are committed to delivering excellence in every area and as such we steadfastly believe that \"Excellence is Standard.\" Penn Radiation Oncology is one of the most comprehensive radiation oncology programs in the world. The outstanding faculty and staff, combined with Penn’s extensive collection of advanced technology, gives patients access to nearly every treatment option available for their cancer. The broad range of radiation treatments available include External-Beam Radiation Therapy (Proton Therapy, Image-guided radiation therapy (IGRT), Intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT), Photodynamic therapy (PDT), Total body irradiation (TBI), Total skin electron beam therapy (TSEBT)), and Stereotactic Radiosurgery (CyberKnife, Edge, Gamma Knife, TrueBeam), as well as Internal Radiation Therapy (brachytherapy, MammoSite). The brachytherapy suite at the Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine is a state-of-the-art, dedicated outpatient facility specializing in high-dose rate (HDR) treatments for prostate, gynecologic, and head/neck cancers. It features advanced in-room imaging, including BK ultrasound and fluoroscopy, and is located next to MRI services for precise 3D treatment planning. With the Abramson Cancer Center of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Radiation Oncology provides patient care at the Ruth and Raymond Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine and fourteen community-based sites."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176659": {
      "title": "Chief of Minimally Invasive Gynecology Surgery Division, Associate or Full Professor of Ob/Gyn Clinician Educator",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. This role will also serve as Chief of Minimally Invasive Gynecology Surgery Division. Expertise is required in the specific area of minimally invasive gynecologic surgery (MIGS). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified and trained in Obstetrics and Gynecology and have formal fellowship training in MIGS. Rank will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. We are seeking a Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery (MIGS) surgeon with a strong interest in education and leadership to join our expanding practice and lead our Division of Minimally Invasive Gynecology Surgery. Teaching responsibilities may include training and supervision of Ob/Gyn residents and medical students with plans to start a fellowship in Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery. Interest in educational leadership is highly desirable. Faculty appointment is available at the University of Pennsylvania School of Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include gynecologic care and minimally invasive surgery. Our growing practice provides multidisciplinary care of patients with complex conditions such as: *Fibroids and abnormal uterine bleeding, *Chronic pelvic pain and endometriosis and *Abnormal placentation and complex ectopic pregnancies. The MIGS surgeons at Penn Medicine provide expertise in multiple surgical modalities such as laparoscopy, robotics, and operative hysteroscopy. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include basic, translational, clinical and/or health policy research. Collaborative science is highly valued. Applicants should have an established research program and an outstanding record of publications. The new Chief of the Division of Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery will join a cadre of surgeons at Penn Medicine who are nationally known for their surgical expertise, research, education and innovation. This position is a unique opportunity to start a new division with devoted faculty, working closely with colleagues within the Department of Obstetrics & Gynecology who are at the forefront of the field. Preference will be given to candidates with scholarly experience and leadership/development in MIGS. Experience Penn Medicine – an institution known for excellence in research, clinical care, mentorship and inclusion."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193427": {
      "title": "Chief, Complex Benign Gynecology, Associate or Full Professor of Clinical Ob/Gyn, Academic Clinician track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. This role will also serve as Chief of the Division of Complex Benign Gynecology . Expertise is required in the specific area of complex benign gynecologic surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified and trained in Obstetrics and Gynecology and have formal fellowship training in MIGS (Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery). Rank will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Teaching responsibilities may include training and supervision of Ob/Gyn residents and medical students with plans to start a fellowship in Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery. Interest in educational leadership is highly desirable. Faculty appointment is available at the University of Pennsylvania School of Medicine. Clinical responsibilities may include gynecologic care and complex benign gynecology and surgery. Our growing practice provides multidisciplinary care of patients with complex conditions such as: *Fibroids and abnormal uterine bleeding, *Chronic pelvic pain and endometriosis and *Abnormal placentation and complex ectopic pregnancies. The MIGS surgeons at Penn Medicine provide expertise in multiple surgical modalities such as laparoscopy, robotics, and operative hysteroscopy. The new Chief of the Division of Complex Benign Gynecology will join a cadre of surgeons at Penn Medicine who are nationally known for their surgical expertise, research, education and innovation. This position is a unique opportunity to start a new division with devoted faculty, working closely with colleagues within the Department of Obstetrics & Gynecology who are at the forefront of the field. Preference will be given to candidates with leadership/development in Complex Benign Gynecology . Experience Penn Medicine – an institution known for excellence in research, clinical care, mentorship and inclusion."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180925": {
      "title": "Chief, Division of Breast Surgery, Associate or Full Professor of Surgery at HUP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of breast cancer and benign breast disease. Fellowship training in breast surgery, or surgical oncology with breast emphasis, is preferred. Applicants must have an M.D. They must also be certified by the American Board of Surgery. Teaching responsibilities may include education of medical students, residents and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient, inpatient and operative care of patients with benign and malignant breast disease. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or basic science research related to breast diseases. The successful candidate will have an established clinical reputation, record of academic achievement, and a commitment to mentoring junior faculty. This position will be full-time and based primarily at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. It will include the role Chief of the Division of Breast Surgery, with administrative responsibilities as one of 11 division chiefs in the department. Candidates for the position should embrace all parts of our tripartite mission: to be a world leader in clinical care, research and education. They should have a demonstrated record of excellence in one or more components of that mission and are expected to have a record of service and administration, outstanding interpersonal and communication skills, and a compelling vision for the department and the discipline. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Penn Medicine’s Division of Breast Surgery delivers comprehensive surgical care for patients with both benign and malignant breast disease across a broad regional footprint, including three downtown Philadelphia hospitals and multiple practice locations throughout the Main Line, Chester County, and southern New Jersey. Penn Medicine offers a uniquely integrated academic and clinical environment for advancing multidisciplinary breast cancer care across a large and growing regional network. Anchored by the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania (PSOM) and the Abramson Cancer Center, one of the nation’s leading NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Centers, Penn provides Breast Surgery leadership with the infrastructure, collaborative partnerships, and institutional support necessary to expand access to high-quality, evidence-based surgical care. The Division maintains strong partnerships with medical oncology, radiation oncology, plastic and reconstructive surgery, imaging, and pathology, enabling a fully integrated care model that supports advanced surgical approaches, coordinated treatment planning, and access to clinical trials. Penn Medicine is a $12+ billion integrated academic health system comprised of seven hospitals and a large, financially strong physician enterprise (Clinical Practices of the University of Pennsylvania, or CPUP). As Penn Medicine continues to align breast cancer care across its network, there is a substantial opportunity for the Division Chief to lead the system integration of breast surgery services, strengthening collaborative programmatic alignment across all campuses."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158999": {
      "title": "Chief, Division of Genomic Diagnostics at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. and/or Ph.D degree. Molecular Genetic Pathology certification following Pathology residency, or American Board of Medical Genetics certification in Laboratory Genetics and Genomics, is required. Physicians must be eligible/licensed in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching fellows, residents, medical and graduate students, and staff in a variety of settings. Clinical responsibilities may include the development and implementation of tools for diagnostic and translational medicine, establishing and improving standards and methods for the interpretation of multi-omic data, assessing risk factors, and appropriate quantitative interpretation of data in clinical lab settings. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include work in the broad area of genomic diagnostics. We seek candidates with proven leadership skills and expertise in Genomic Diagnostics. The successful applicant serve as Chief of CHOP’s Division of Genomic Diagnostics (DGD) reporting to the Department Chair. The DGD encompasses cancer genomics, constitutional genomics and immunogenetics. With 14 faculty and 69 staff, the DGD offers a significant depth and breadth of clinical diagnostic tests including rapid genome, whole exome, gene panels, SNP arrays, cytogenetics, liquid biopsy and NGS-based HLA typing tests. As a key contributor to CHOP’s Omics and Big Data Initiative, the DGD plays an essential role in supporting the hospital’s precision medicine strategy. In addition, the Division’s faculty are engaged in a broad range of research and educational activities. The successful applicant will be expected to lead with a clear vision for the future of genomic diagnostics, driving innovation by developing new tests and technologies and supporting clinical research initiatives. A key leadership responsibility will involve proactively building and fostering collaborations both within CHOP and with external academic and industry partners to expand the Division’s impact and capabilities. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173290": {
      "title": "Chief, Division of Pain Medicine – Associate/Full Professor (AC)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Fellowship training and/or extensive experience in pain medicine is strongly preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include assisting the fellowship director with educational initiatives and the instruction of medical students, residents, and fellows of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and the Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC) as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of pain medicine and general anesthesia at HUP and PPMC. Additional responsibilities will include leadership of the Division of Pain Medicine across all three missions: Clinical, Education, and Research. This involves accountability for productivity in all three areas and for positively impacting growth in each domain. The successful candidate will be expected to recruit, support, and mentor faculty specializing in pain medicine within the division, including participation and collaboration to improve patient care, and collaboration with other leaders in the Department, Service Line, Hospital, VA and Health System to improve the division. The academic clinician track emphasizes clinical and teaching excellence. Prior leadership experience and record of successful teaching/mentorship is required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194427": {
      "title": "Chief, Division of Pediatric Plastic Surgery, Associate or Full Professor of Surgery at CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pediatric plastic surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Plastic Surgeons or foreign equivalent.  Rank will be commensurate with experience. The next Division Chief will lead one of the largest and most successful pediatric plastic surgery programs in the nation and will be expected to participate in patient care, teaching, and scholarship.  The Division of Pediatric Plastic Surgery is comprised of over 12 faculty and attending physicians with diverse clinical, educational, and investigative interests. Teaching responsibilities may include instruction of medical students, plastic surgery residents and pediatric plastic surgery fellows and APPs.  Educating the next generation of pediatric plastic surgery leaders is a priority of the Division. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient or outpatient services at CHOP’s Main campus, King of Prussia campus and other sites.  The Division leads multiple robust outpatient clinical programs, providing care in almost 16,000 patient outpatient encounters per year. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include pursuit of clinical and/or basic science research related to plastic surgery. The successful candidate will serve as Chief of Pediatric Plastic Surgery in the Department of Surgery at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP), where the clinical practice will be focused."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195641": {
      "title": "Chief, Division of Plastic Surgery, Associate or Full Professor of Surgery at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of plastic surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Fellowship training in plastic surgery is preferred. They must also be certified by the American Board of Surgery. Teaching responsibilities may include education of medical students, residents and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient, inpatient, and operative care of patients. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or basic science research. The successful candidate will have an established clinical reputation, record of academic achievement, and a commitment to mentoring junior faculty. This position will be full-time and based primarily at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. It will include the role Chief of the Division of Plastic Surgery, with administrative responsibilities as one of 11 division chiefs in the department. Candidates for the position should embrace all parts of our tripartite mission: to be a world leader in clinical care, research and education. They should have a demonstrated record of excellence in one or more components of that mission and are expected to have a record of service and administration, outstanding interpersonal and communication skills, and a compelling vision for the department and the discipline. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Penn Medicine’s Division of Plastic Surgery provides comprehensive care across Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and the Philadelphia region, performing more than 4,800 surgeries annually. Clinic locations include the three primary downtown hospitals well as four outlying hospitals. Our Penn Plastic Surgery team specializes in cosmetic and reconstructive surgery, as well as a comprehensive skin care program. We have well-established collaborative reconstruction programs with breast surgery, orthopedics, trauma, sarcoma and soft tissue cancers, and neurosurgery as key partners in this clinical practice. The Division is a national leader and among the world’s largest centers by clinical volume in reconstructive microsurgery. The Division maintains strong partnerships with oncology, trauma and emergency services surgery, imaging, and pathology, enabling a fully integrated care model that supports advanced surgical approaches, coordinated treatment planning, and access to clinical trials. As Penn Medicine continues to further align our comprehensive plastic surgery program across its regional network, there is a meaningful opportunity for the Division Chief to provide leadership in the oversight of plastic surgery services to strengthen collaborative programmatic alignment at satellite locations."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169161": {
      "title": "CHOP - Orthopaedic Spine Surgeon - Assoc/Full Professor - CE Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidate must demonstrate excellent qualifications and clinical care and must be board certified/eligible by the American Board of Orthopaedic Surgery. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or orthopaedic basic science research and will be dependent on the candidates interests and independent support. Evidence of scholarship is required for the Clinician Educator track.  Mid-career applicants are encouraged. Rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193836": {
      "title": "CHOP Sports Medicine Surgeon-CE Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible by the American Board of Orthopaedic Surgery. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or orthopaedic basic science research and will be dependent on the candidates interests and independent support. Candidate must have demonstrated excellent qualifications in education and clinical care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189351": {
      "title": "Clinical Cardiac Electrophysiology, Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine - Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of complex catheter ablation and device implantation. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified in or board eligible in cardiovascular disease. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching responsibilities include teaching CCEP fellows, cardiovascular fellows, medicine residents and medical students on the inpatient consultation service; teaching CCEP fellows and cardiovascular fellows in outpatient clinic; and teaching CCEP fellows in the EP lab. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient clinic of at least one full day per week. Performing procedures in the EP lab approximately 3 days per week. Inpatient consultation service 2 times per month. The selected candidate will have the training and ability to independently perform ablation of supraventricular tachycardia, atrial fibrillation and ventricular tachycardia, as well as to implant traditional, leadless, subcutaneous and extravascular CIEDs. Experience with epicardial access/mapping/ablation, coronary venous mapping, intracardiac echo from the left atrium and ventricle and laser lead extraction are preferred. The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine in the Academic Clinician track in the Clinical Cardiac Electrophysiology Section. Faculty benefit from an unparalleled ecosystem of collaboration, working alongside internationally recognized leaders across disciplines and engaging in cutting-edge, translational research that directly informs clinical practice. The institution’s robust infrastructure—including access to interdisciplinary centers, advanced clinical programs, and expansive research funding— supports meaningful career development across clinical, research, educational, and leadership pathways. Philadelphia itself offers a rich and vibrant cultural landscape, with renowned institutions such as the Philadelphia Museum of Art, the Kimmel Center for the Performing Arts, and a nationally recognized dining scene. The city combines historic character with modern livability, featuring walkable neighborhoods, diverse communities, and a relatively accessible cost of living compared to peer cities. The University provides a comprehensive and highly competitive benefits package, including multiple retirement savings options and generous tuition benefits for eligible dependents—further enhancing the long-term value of a faculty appointment. Collectively, Penn Medicine and Philadelphia represent an exceptional opportunity for individuals seeking to advance their careers within a collaborative, high-impact academic environment while enjoying the cultural, professional, and lifestyle advantages of a premier urban setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189901": {
      "title": "Clinical Cardiac Electrophysiology, Assistant Professor of Medicine - Clinician Educator Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of complex catheter ablation and device implantation. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/board eligible in cardiovascular disease and clinical cardiac electrophysiology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching CCEP fellows, cardiovascular fellows, medicine residents, and medical students on the inpatient consultation service; teaching CCEP fellows and cardiovascular fellows in outpatient clinic; and teaching CCEP fellows in the EP lab. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient clinic of at least one full day per week. Performing procedures in the EP lab approximately 3 days per week. Inpatient consultation service 2 times per month. Selected candidates will have the training and ability to independently perform ablation of supraventricular tachycardia, atrial fibrillation and ventricular tachycardia, as well as to implant traditional, leadless, subcutaneous and extravascular CIEDs. Experience with epicardial access/mapping/ablation, coronary venous mapping, intracardiac echo from the left atrium and ventricle and laser lead extraction are preferred. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include conducting and publishing research studies to advance the field of cardiac electrophysiology. Mentoring of CCEP clinical and research fellows is often involved. The successful candidate will be expected to lecture on his/her research at regional and national conferences. Establishing an innovative and independent research program that will attract and maintain extramural funding from governmental agencies, private foundations, and industry is expected. A strong track record of publication and familiarity with advanced statistical methods are preferred. Faculty benefit from an unparalleled ecosystem of collaboration, working alongside internationally recognized leaders across disciplines and engaging in cutting-edge, translational research that directly informs clinical practice. The institution’s robust infrastructure—including access to interdisciplinary centers, advanced clinical programs, and expansive research funding— supports meaningful career development across clinical, research, educational, and leadership pathways. Philadelphia offers a rich and vibrant cultural landscape, with renowned institutions such as the Philadelphia Museum of Art, the Kimmel Center for the Performing Arts, and a nationally recognized dining scene. The city combines historic character with modern livability, featuring walkable neighborhoods, diverse communities, and a relatively accessible cost of living compared to peer cities. The University provides a comprehensive and highly competitive benefits package, including multiple retirement savings options and generous tuition benefits for eligible dependents—further enhancing the long-term value of a faculty appointment. Collectively, Penn Medicine and Philadelphia represent an exceptional opportunity for individuals seeking to advance their careers within a collaborative, high-impact academic environment while enjoying the cultural, professional, and lifestyle advantages of a premier urban setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187079": {
      "title": "Clinical Cardio-Oncologist, Academic Clinician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates should be board certified or board eligible in cardiovascular diseases. Teaching responsibilities may include educating medical students, residents, cardiovascular fellows and advanced practice providers. Selected candidates will be expected to contribute to the educational mission of the organization. Clinical responsibilities may include attending on the inpatient and outpatient services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and associated practice sites. As the Cardio-Oncology program is a part of the Consultative (general) Cardiology Section, candidates should be prepared to provide services for general cardiology patients based on the needs of the division. Opportunities for non-invasive imaging will be considered on an individual basis taking into consideration applicant expertise and divisional priorities. Penn Faculty benefit from an unparalleled ecosystem of collaboration, working alongside internationally recognized leaders across disciplines and engaging in cutting-edge, translational research that directly informs clinical practice. The institution’s robust infrastructure—including access to interdisciplinary centers, advanced clinical programs, and expansive research funding—supports meaningful career development across clinical, research, educational, and leadership pathways. Philadelphia itself offers a rich and vibrant cultural landscape, with renowned institutions such as the Philadelphia Museum of Art, the Kimmel Center for the Performing Arts, and a nationally recognized dining scene. The city combines historic character with modern livability, featuring walkable neighborhoods, diverse communities, and a relatively accessible cost of living compared to peer cities. The University provides a comprehensive and highly competitive benefits package, including multiple retirement savings options and generous tuition benefits for eligible dependents—further enhancing the long-term value of a faculty appointment. Collectively, Penn Medicine and Philadelphia represent an exceptional opportunity for individuals seeking to advance their careers within a collaborative, high-impact academic environment while enjoying the cultural, professional, and lifestyle advantages of a premier urban setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189444": {
      "title": "Clinical Cardio-Oncologist, Academic Clinician - Senior ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates should be board certified or board eligible in cardiovascular diseases. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include include educating medical students, residents, cardiovascular fellows and advanced practice providers. Selected candidates will be expected to contribute to the educational mission of the organization. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include attending on the inpatient and outpatient services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and associated practice sites. As the Cardio-Oncology Program is a part of the Consultative (general) Cardiology Section, candidates should be prepared to provide services for general cardiology patients based on the needs of the division. Opportunities for non-invasive imaging will be considered on an individual basis taking into consideration applicant expertise and divisional priorities. We seek accomplished individuals who will contribute to the continued growth and strategic advancement of Penn's expanding Cardio-Oncology Program through excellence in patient care, education, mentorship, and interdisciplinary collaboration with the Abramson Cancer Center and related oncology specialties. Selected candidates will be given ample mentorship to achieve clinical and clinical research productivity with a goal of maintaining and growing both national and regional prominence in the field. Members of the Penn Cardio-Oncology program work collaboratively with medical oncologists, radiation oncologists and surgeons in the NCI-designated Abramson Comprehensive Cancer Center to provide exceptional care for complex conditions in both the inpatient and outpatient setting. The ideal candidate will be committed to the continued growth and clinical development of the division. Faculty benefit from an unparalleled ecosystem of collaboration, working alongside internationally recognized leaders across disciplines and engaging in cutting-edge, translational research that directly informs clinical practice. The institution’s robust infrastructure—including access to interdisciplinary centers, advanced clinical programs, and expansive research funding— supports meaningful career development across clinical, research, educational, and leadership pathways. Philadelphia itself offers a rich and vibrant cultural landscape, with renowned institutions such as the Philadelphia Museum of Art, the Kimmel Center for the Performing Arts, and a nationally recognized dining scene. The city combines historic character with modern livability, featuring walkable neighborhoods, diverse communities, and a relatively accessible cost of living compared to peer cities. The University provides a comprehensive and highly competitive benefits package, including multiple retirement savings options and generous tuition benefits for eligible dependents—further enhancing the long-term value of a faculty appointment. Collectively, Penn Medicine and Philadelphia represent an exceptional opportunity for individuals seeking to advance their careers within a collaborative, high-impact academic environment while enjoying the cultural, professional, and lifestyle advantages of a premier urban setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187321": {
      "title": "Clinical Geriatrics Faculty Position - Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Geriatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Geriatrics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABIM or ABFM certification and Geriatric Medicine certification/eligibility is required. Teaching responsibilities may include training medical students, residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include ambulatory geriatric care (office based, home care and/or nursing home care), and inpatient care (hospital and/or Sub-Acute Rehabilitation)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172851": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor of Radiation Oncology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiation Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiation Oncology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of proton therapy. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Applicants are required to be Board Eligible for the American Board of Radiology. Responsibilities may include ongoing evaluation and management of patients diagnosed with cancer, and the delivery of radiation therapy-related care; conduct patient consultations and treatment across various cancer disease sites utilizing a variety of treatment modalities, including proton therapy. Role may include research activities, including initiating clinical trials. Education responsibilities may include teaching, training and mentoring of radiation oncology residents, medical physics residents, medical physics graduate students, visiting physics residents or trainees from other institutions or other countries, etc. Other informal and formal teachings include but are not limited to participating in resident didactic series, both as a lecturer and as an in-person discussant. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to build and establish a clinical practice in the Radiation Oncology department. The applicant may also participate in educational and clinical research activities. Penn Radiation Oncology is dedicated to a three-part mission of excellence in patient care, basic and translational research, and the education of residents and students. We are committed to delivering excellence in every area and as such we steadfastly believe that \"Excellence is Standard.\" Penn Radiation Oncology is one of the most comprehensive radiation oncology programs in the world. The outstanding faculty and staff, combined with Penn’s extensive collection of advanced technology, gives patients access to nearly every treatment option available for their cancer. The broad range of radiation treatments available include External-Beam Radiation Therapy (Proton Therapy, Image-guided radiation therapy (IGRT), Intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT), Photodynamic therapy (PDT), Total body irradiation (TBI), Total skin electron beam therapy (TSEBT)), Stereotactic Radiosurgery (CyberKnife, Edge, Gamma Knife, TrueBeam), as well as Internal Radiation Therapy (brachytherapy, MammoSite). With the Abramson Cancer Center of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Radiation Oncology provides patient care at the Ruth and Raymond Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine and fourteen community-based sites"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169383": {
      "title": "Clinician Educator - Assistant Professor – Mohs and Dermatological Surgeon",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree and be board-certified or board-eligible upon completion of both an ACGME-accredited residency in dermatology and a fellowship in Micrographic Surgery and Dermatologic Oncology. Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in Mohs surgery and reconstruction and to building a nationally or internationally recognized career in academic dermatologic surgery. Candidates will enjoy extensive mentorship from our experienced surgeons and faculty to develop advanced surgical skills and an academic niche. Teaching responsibilities may include didactics and bedside dermatologic surgery instruction to our world-class residents, fellows, and medical students. We seek enthusiastic candidates who are dedicated to teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include Mohs and reconstructive surgery in our ambulatory practices in Philadelphia or Penn Medicine Radnor. Candidates will benefit from a busy surgical practice and an extensive infrastructure with state-of-the-art facilities and a large support staff of nurses, histotechnicians, research fellows, and coordinators. Our Mohs surgeons use immunostains for melanoma and other rare tumors, and we mentor candidates to develop these skills. We seek candidates who demonstrate excellent clinical judgement, professionalism, and commitment to our team. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include publishing and lecturing about advances to prevent and treat skin cancer. Faculty enjoy extensive support with research fellows, statisticians, and regulatory coordinators for research or clinical trials. Candidates will accelerate their careers with our team-based approach to research. The Philadelphia region boasts a rich history with excellent restaurants, sports, art, and neighborhoods. Candidates can book easy plane travel to almost any destination worldwide, and train travel along the East Coast is fast and convenient."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169384": {
      "title": "Clinician Educator - Associate or Full Professor – Mohs and Dermatological Surgeon",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree and be board-certified or board-eligible upon completion of both an ACGME-accredited residency in dermatology and a fellowship in Micrographic Surgery and Dermatologic Oncology.  Mid-career individuals are encouraged to apply. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in Mohs surgery and reconstruction and have a nationally or internationally recognized career in academic dermatologic surgery. Teaching responsibilities may include didactics and bedside dermatologic surgery instruction to our world-class residents, fellows, and medical students. We seek enthusiastic candidates who are dedicated to teaching and mentoring. Clinical responsibilities may include Mohs and reconstructive surgery in our ambulatory practices in Philadelphia or Penn Medicine Radnor. Candidates will benefit from a busy surgical practice and an extensive infrastructure with state-of-the-art facilities and a large support staff of nurses and histotechnicians. Our Mohs surgeons use immunostains for melanoma and other rare tumors, and we mentor candidates to develop these skills. We seek candidates who demonstrate excellent clinical judgement, professionalism, and commitment to our team. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include publishing and lecturing about advances to prevent and treat skin cancer. Faculty enjoy extensive support with research fellows, statisticians, and regulatory coordinators for research or clinical trials. The Philadelphia region boasts a rich history with excellent restaurants, sports, art, and neighborhoods. Candidates can book easy plane travel to almost any destination worldwide, and train travel along the East Coast is fast and convenient."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193119": {
      "title": "Clinician Educator, Addiction Psychiatry (Senior Rank Faculty)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of mechanisms underpinning substance use and the treatment of substance use and misuse. Applicants with experience in novel therapeutics (e.g., psychedelics, incretin mimetics) in the treatment of substance use disorders are encouraged to apply. Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D degree. Board certification in Psychiatry is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, psychiatry residents, and postdoctoral fellows, as well as lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical evaluation and provision of treatment for adults with substance use disorders. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative and independent research programs related to the understanding and treatment of substance use disorders. Scholarship includes developing and maintaining a program of federally funded research."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191069": {
      "title": "Clinician Scientist on the Clinician Educator or Tenure Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Family Medicine and Community Health Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Family Medicine and Community Health at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, fellows, and junior faculty, as well as formal lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include supervision of the department’s inpatient service as well as the opportunity to provide outpatient clinical care in a department or community based clinic setting, such as our school-based health clinic, our mobile care program with partners, or in a variety of other community-based clinical settings addressing the health care needs of populations that are at high risk of experiencing adverse health outcomes. Clinical effort will be structured to support the development and sustainability of an externally funded, independent research portfolio. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include establishing and maintaining an innovative, independent, and nationally recognized program of health policy research with direct relevance to primary care and community health. Areas of focus may include the design, evaluation, and reform of health care delivery systems; insurance coverage and access to care; primary care payment and workforce policy; policies addressing health equity and the social determinants of health; and federal, state, or local health policy affecting underserved populations. The successful candidate will be expected to develop a sustained program of federally funded research and to collaborate with investigators across the Perelman School of Medicine and the University of Pennsylvania while building an independent national reputation in health policy. The department seeks an early-career clinician-scientist with demonstrated potential to become a national leader in health policy research as it pertains to primary care and community health. Candidates must have an established record of scholarly productivity and evidence of successful federal research funding as Principal Investigator, Multiple Principal Investigator, or recipient of a federal career development award. Competitive applicants will have current or prior support from agencies such as the National Institutes of Health (NIH), Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality (AHRQ), Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), Patient-Centered Outcomes Research Institute (PCORI), or comparable federal funding agencies, with a demonstrated trajectory toward sustained independent funding. Applicants should have a strong record of peer-reviewed publications commensurate with career stage and a clear commitment to advancing the science of primary care through rigorous, impactful research."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191134": {
      "title": "Community & Academic Physician - Assistant Professor AC track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Family Medicine and Community Health Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Family Medicine and Community Health at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Community-based primary care and academic medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be Board Certified in Family Medicine. Fellowship training or a Certificate of Added Qualifications (CAQ) is not required. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the education of Family Medicine residents and medical students. Supervision and precepting of learners in both community and academic settings. Engagement with interdisciplinary learner teams across clinical environments. Teaching is a valued component of this position. Clinical responsibilities may include partial clinical effort in outpatient primary care at an FQHC or community health center. Additional non-continuity clinical work in an academic Family Medicine setting, which may include outpatient acute care and precepting and/or attending on the Family Medicine inpatient teaching service. Experience with comprehensive primary care for patients of all ages, including prenatal care services, is desired. Candidates interested in inpatient hospital medicine have the opportunity to incorporate this into their clinical effort, though it is not a required component of the position. This full-time clinical role spans both community and academic settings. The Department of Family Medicine and Community Health has established partnerships with multiple Federally Qualified Health Centers (FQHCs) in West Philadelphia, providing physician services with the goal of reducing health care disparities and improving access to care for underserved communities. The Department is expanding its physician presence at an existing FQHC partner location and seeks a motivated candidate who is committed to practicing in this setting. This is a unique hybrid position that combines community-based primary care at an FQHC with clinical and teaching responsibilities in an academic Family Medicine setting. The ideal candidate will bring a deep commitment to health equity and be energized by the opportunity to serve patients in low-resource environments while contributing to the education of the next generation of family physicians. The ideal candidate will demonstrate: Experience working in an FQHC, community health center, or comparable setting (valued but not required). Experience caring for patients from disadvantaged or low-resource backgrounds, with a genuine motivation to practice in an FQHC environment (valued). Experience with comprehensive primary care across the lifespan, including prenatal care (desired). A passion for teaching Family Medicine residents and medical students. A strong, demonstrated commitment to addressing health disparities in marginalized and underserved communities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188187": {
      "title": "Complex Medical Dermatology Instructorship",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must have completed dermatology residency by the fellowship start date. Our estimated start date is July 31, 2027. Applications will need to be completed in full by October 15, 2026. Responsibilities may include management of patients both acutely and longitudinally, gaining experience in prescribing and managing a range of systemic immunomodulatory and immunosuppressive medications. Members of the program are expected to be actively engaged in teaching residents both in clinical settings and in formal didactics, and mentorship in education is a key part of the program. Additionally, participants in this program are expected to be involved in research and publishing and will have opportunities to join projects that are in progress, and mentorship and support in launching their own investigative work. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to to be mentored in not only the diagnosis and management of patients with complex medical dermatological diseases but also in teaching and research. This is a mentored experience under the direction of Dr. Misha Rosenbach, Fellowship Director, and is focused on developing skills to care for the most challenging and complex patients in dermatology, including inpatient consultative dermatology and outpatient advanced medical dermatology. The focus is on diagnosis, evaluation, and management of patients with skin signs of systemic disease, autoimmune/inflammatory diseases, and hospitalized patients with cutaneous disease. Participants are in a hybrid role bridging ongoing training and learning in a mentored environment, and early faculty responsibilities as an independently practicing dermatologist. This ‘fellowship’ is structured to include: • Collaborative complex medical dermatology outpatient clinics adjacent to and embedded with our advanced medical dermatology team (Drs. Rosenbach, Micheletti, Werth, and Vleugels) • Independent outpatient medical dermatology clinics with close mentorship available • Inpatient dermatology consult service with evolving responsibilities over the course of the year – from observer/helper, to teacher, to supervised independent practice. The ideal participant is a senior dermatology resident or junior faculty person planning a career in academic medical dermatology with a component of inpatient consultative dermatology."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168428": {
      "title": "Critical Care Anesthesiologist - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of critical care anesthesia. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Teaching responsibilities may include the instruction of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the operating rooms and wards of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), and Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of critical care services at HUP, PPMC, and PAH, as well as the provision of clinical anesthesia services at HUP or PPMC. There are additional opportunities to participate in our innovative critical care programs, including tele-critical care and mobile ECMO. Our intensivists usually have one \"home\" unit and may rotate through one or two additional ICUs depending on the number of ICU weeks worked. The Academic Clinician track emphasizes clinical and teaching excellence. Are you interested in this position but are unsure about if it's the right fit? We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Office of Academic Affairs website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/faculty-career-development/"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168430": {
      "title": "Critical Care Anesthesiologist - Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of critical care anesthesia. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include the instruction of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the operating rooms and wards of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), and Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of critical care services at the HUP, PPMC, and PAH, as well as the provision of clinical anesthesia services at HUP or PPMC. There are additional opportunities to participate in our innovative critical care programs, including tele-critical care and mobile ECMO. Our intensivists usually have one \"home\" unit and may rotate through one or two additional ICUs depending on the number of ICU weeks worked. Applicants in mid-career are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193204": {
      "title": "Division Chief - Breast Imaging - Academic Clinician - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. The selected candidate will serve as the Division Chief of Breast Imaging in the Department of Radiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with subspecialty training in Breast Radiology. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision of residents and fellows and didactic teaching for medical students, radiology residents, fellows, and learners from other departments. In addition, the candidate would be expected to participate in educational and/or other scholarly activities within and beyond Penn Radiology, such as preparing learning materials, lectures, and educational exhibits for national meetings, as well as mentorship and sponsorship. Clinical responsibilities may include interpretation of breast imaging studies and performance of procedures involving all modalities (tomosynthesis (including contrast-enhanced mammography), ultrasound, and MRI) at a subspecialty level commensurate with a quaternary care center. The successful candidate will also participate in shared after-hour coverage, as needed. Successful applicants should have a compelling, patient-first vision for Breast Imaging, focused on delivering exceptional care to the communities that Penn serves, while also breaking new ground in the field, and leading at national and international levels. They should demonstrate strong leadership skills, and a national reputation for clinical excellence and for prioritizing research and innovation. A track record of mentoring learners and/or junior faculty will be considered an important strength, as will doing so in the context of research and other scholarly activities. Administrative responsibilities will span the tripartite mission, and include operational execution, as well as recruiting, developing, and retaining a distinct group of faculty dedicated to practicing in a highly subspecialized and dynamic environment. The section interprets close to 65,000 examinations per year performed at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Pennsylvania Hospital, and additional associated practices. Research resources within Penn Radiology include dedicated 1.5T, 3T, and 7T MRI systems and a comprehensive scientific infrastructure with programs focusing on applications of quantitative image analysis, imaging genomics, molecular imaging and precision diagnostics, hyperpolarized gases, artificial intelligence, and health services research. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veteran Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania and New Jersey; a new site of care in Delaware is expected in the Spring of 2027. This position requires a minimum of 5+ years of experience. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Candidates in this track must have demonstrated exceptional clinical and teaching skills. The application deadline is Monday, November 23rd, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192559": {
      "title": "Division Chief - Breast Imaging - Clinician--Educator - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician-educator track. The selected candidate will serve as the Division Chief of Breast Imaging in the Department of Radiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates in this track must have demonstrated exceptional clinical, research, and teaching skills. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with subspecialty training in Breast Radiology. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision of residents and fellows and didactic teaching for medical students, radiology residents, fellows, and trainees from other departments. In addition, the candidate would be expected to participate in educational and/or other scholarly activities within and beyond Penn Radiology, such as preparing learning materials, lectures, and educational exhibits for national meetings, as well as mentorship and sponsorship. Clinical responsibilities may include interpretation of breast imaging studies and performance of procedures involving all modalities (tomosynthesis (including contrast-enhanced mammography), ultrasound, and MRI) at a subspecialty level commensurate with a quaternary care center. The successful candidate will also participate in shared after-hour coverage, as needed. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include leading a focused body of research in a field within breast imaging. This includes the application of imaging to detect, diagnose or evaluate diseases of the breast, as well as studies of the clinical impact of imaging in the diagnosis of these diseases. The successful candidate in the clinician-educator track will have prior research experience, have demonstrated evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship, and be expected to provide mentorship to aspiring junior faculty seeking to develop a research career in the field of Breast Imaging. Successful applicants should have a compelling, patient-first vision for Breast Imaging, focused on delivering exceptional care to the communities that Penn serves, while also breaking new ground in the field, and leading at national and international levels. They should demonstrate strong leadership skills, and a national reputation for clinical excellence and for prioritizing research and innovation. A track record of mentoring learners and/or junior faculty will be considered an important strength, as will doing so in the context of research and other scholarly activities. Administrative responsibilities will span the tripartite mission, and include operational execution, as well as recruiting, developing, and retaining a distinct group of faculty dedicated to practicing in a highly subspecialized and dynamic environment. The section interprets close to 65,000 examinations per year performed at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Pennsylvania Hospital, and additional associated practices. Research resources within Penn Radiology include dedicated 1.5T, 3T, and 7T MRI systems and a comprehensive scientific infrastructure with programs focusing on applications of quantitative image analysis, imaging genomics, molecular imaging and precision diagnostics and therapies, hyperpolarized gases, artificial intelligence, and health services research. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veteran Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania and New Jersey; a new site of care in Delaware is expected in the Spring of 2027. This position requires a minimum of 5+ years of experience. Rank will be commensurate with experience. The application deadline is Monday, November 23rd, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172822": {
      "title": "Division Chief of Cardiac Anesthesiology, Academic Clinician - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. The selected candidate will also serve in the role of Division Chief of Cardiac Anesthesiology at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia. Expertise is required in the specific area of Anesthesiology with a focus on Pediatric Cardiac Anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspecialty certification or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology and Pennsylvania licensure are required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities include developing systems for mentoring faculty and staff in the division to promote productive, rewarding careers and academic advancement. Clinical responsibilities include the provision of clinical anesthesia and medical direction in the Cardiac Operating Rooms and other anesthetizing locations at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. The Division Chief oversees the clinical activities of the Division and coordinates with leaders across the enterprise to optimize clinical operations. The Division supports numerous clinical programs, delivering over 3,100 anesthetics annually to children with congenital and acquired heart disease in the cardiac ORs, catheterization labs, and non-OR locations such as MRI. The Academic Clinician track is intended for faculty members who demonstrate impactful contributions to clinical care and education and who develop an Area of Concentration (AoC) in which they become recognized. We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/flpd/career-development/ . We are looking for an inspirational and innovative leader to lead one of the highest-profile premier academic pediatric cardiac anesthesiology divisions. The successful candidate will transform the division in pursuit of achieving CHOP’s mission of excellence in clinical care, education, research, and advocacy. The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine maintains a robust, well-funded research enterprise, encompassing basic science, translational, clinical, and health services research programs that span all areas of anesthesiology and critical care medicine. Operating within the Department’s matrixed leadership structure, the Division Chief will play a pivotal role in supporting the Associate Chair of Research, the Associate Chief of Research, and the Department’s Research Council in advancing the Division’s research and academic missions. The Division Chief will collaborate with these Departmental leaders in developing and fostering collaborative research programs, managing infrastructure to support ongoing research efforts, allocating academic time and resources, and supporting and fostering funded research within the Division and across the Department. The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine’s mission is to innovate, deliver clinical excellence, and globally educate and lead pediatric anesthesiology, critical care, and pain medicine. Our vision is to lead the way in providing exceptional patient care, and be a department where people are valued, and data powers change. Our core values are: • “We not Me,” Building a community based on compassion, collaboration, and teamwork. • “Teach and Learn,” Personal and collective growth through accountability, humility, and trust. • “Elevate Together,” Shared commitment to excellence, innovation, and advancement. The Division of Cardiac Anesthesiology is in a phase of dynamic growth and expansion and currently includes: 17 Attending Anesthesiologists, 7 Cardiac CRNAs, 1 Advanced Cardiac Anesthesiology Fellow and 1 Nurse Practitioner. The Division Chief will report directly to the Chair of the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine and will work closely with the Physician Practice Director, Chief Cardiac CRNA, other Division Chiefs, Associate Chairs, and the Vice Chair. Philadelphia is an ideal East Coast location, combining rich history, a vibrant arts and culture scene, diverse culinary experiences, and a variety of housing options both within the city and its surrounding areas. Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia is a national leader in the advancement of healthcare for children and is consistently in the top 5 in the US News & World Report. Our world-class physicians are internationally recognized experts committed to providing children with the highest quality and most advanced care, delivered with compassion, integrity, and respect. Inquiries regarding this position should be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Paul Stricker via email at STRICKERP@chop.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178299": {
      "title": "Division Chief of Cardiac Anesthesiology, Clinician-Educator - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. The selected candidate will also serve in the role of Division Chief of Cardiac Anesthesiology at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia. Expertise is required in the specific area of Anesthesiology with a focus on Pediatric Cardiac Anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification with subspecialty certification or board eligibility in Pediatric Anesthesiology and Pennsylvania licensure are required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities include developing systems for mentoring faculty and staff in the division to promote productive, rewarding careers and academic advancement. Clinical responsibilities include the provision of clinical anesthesia and medical direction in the Cardiac Operating Rooms and other anesthetizing locations at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. The Division Chief oversees the clinical activities of the Division and coordinates with leaders across the enterprise to optimize clinical operations. The Division supports numerous clinical programs, delivering over 3,100 anesthetics annually to children with congenital and acquired heart disease in the cardiac ORs, catheterization labs, and non-OR locations such as MRI. The non-tenure Clinician Educator track involves a substantial commitment to research and evidence of continuous scholarly productivity reflecting a defined focus is required. We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/flpd/career-development/ . We are looking for an inspirational and innovative leader to lead one of the highest-profile premier academic pediatric cardiac anesthesiology divisions. The successful candidate will transform the division in pursuit of achieving CHOP’s mission of excellence in clinical care, education, research, and advocacy. The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine maintains a robust, well-funded research enterprise, encompassing basic science, translational, clinical, and health services research programs that span all areas of anesthesiology and critical care medicine. Operating within the Department’s matrixed leadership structure, the Division Chief will support the Associate Chair of Research, the Associate Chief of Research, and the Department’s Research Council in advancing the Division’s research and academic missions. The Division Chief will collaborate with these Departmental leaders in developing and fostering collaborative research programs, managing infrastructure to support ongoing research efforts, allocating academic time and resources, and supporting and fostering funded research within the Division and across the Department. The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine’s mission is to innovate, deliver clinical excellence, and globally educate and lead pediatric anesthesiology, critical care, and pain medicine. Our vision is to lead the way in providing exceptional patient care, and be a department where people are valued, and data powers change. Our core values are: • “We not Me,” Building a community based on compassion, collaboration, and teamwork • “Teach and Learn,” Personal and collective growth through accountability, humility, and trust • “Elevate Together,” Shared commitment to excellence, innovation, and advancement The Division of Cardiac Anesthesiology is in a phase of dynamic growth and expansion and currently includes: 17 Attending Anesthesiologists, 7 Cardiac CRNAs, 1 Advanced Cardiac Anesthesiology Fellow and 1 Nurse Practitioner. The Division Chief will report directly to the Chair of the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine and will work closely with the Physician Practice Director, Chief Cardiac CRNA, other Division Chiefs, Associate Chairs, and the Vice Chair Philadelphia is an ideal East Coast location, combining rich history, a vibrant arts and culture scene, diverse culinary experiences, and a variety of housing options both within the city and its surrounding areas. Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia is a national leader in the advancement of healthcare for children and is consistently in the top 5 in the US News & World Report. Our world-class physicians are internationally recognized experts committed to providing children with the highest quality and most advanced care, delivered with compassion, integrity, and respect. Inquiries regarding this position should be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Paul Stricker, via email at STRICKERP@chop.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182597": {
      "title": "Division Chief of CICU Academic Clinician - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Critical Care with a focus on Pediatric Cardiac Critical Care Medicine. The selected candidate will also serve in the role of Division Chief of Cardiac Critical Care Medicine at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be ABP certified/board-eligible and eligible for medical licensure in Pennsylvania. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include include developing systems for mentoring faculty and staff in the division to promote productive, rewarding careers and academic advancement. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of clinical cardiac critical care and medical direction in the Cardiac Intensive Care Unit at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. The Division Chief oversees the clinical activities of the Division and coordinates with leaders across the enterprise to optimize clinical operations. The Division supports numerous clinical programs across the Cardiac Center with the CICU capacity of 32 beds with surge capabilities for 40, and a growing average length of stay, reflecting the complexity of patient population. The Academic Clinician track is intended for faculty members who demonstrate impactful contributions to clinical care and education and who develop an Area of Concentration (AoC) in which they become recognized. We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/flpd/career-development/ . We are looking for an inspirational and innovative leader to lead one of the highest-profile premier academic pediatric cardiac critical care divisions. The successful candidate will transform the division in pursuit of achieving CHOP’s mission of excellence in clinical care, education, research, and advocacy. The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine maintains a robust, well-funded research enterprise, encompassing basic science, translational, clinical, and health services research programs that span all areas of anesthesiology and critical care medicine. Operating within the Department’s matrixed leadership structure, the Division Chief will play a pivotal role in supporting the Associate Chair of Research, the Associate Chief of Research, and the Department’s Research Council in advancing the Division’s research and academic missions. The Division Chief will collaborate with these Departmental leaders in developing and fostering collaborative research programs, managing infrastructure to support ongoing research efforts, allocating academic time and resources, and supporting and fostering funded research within the Division and across the Department. The Division of Cardiac Critical Care Medicine is in a strong phase and currently includes: 23 Attending physicians and two cardiac critical care advanced fellows. The Division Chief will report directly to the Chair of the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine and will work closely with the Physician Practice Director, Cardiac Center Chiefs and Leadership, other Division Chiefs, Associate Chairs, and the Vice Chair. Philadelphia is an ideal East Coast location, combining rich history, a vibrant arts and culture scene, diverse culinary experiences, and a variety of housing options both within the city and its surrounding areas. Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia is a national leader in the advancement of healthcare for children and is consistently in the top 5 in the US News & World Report. Our world-class physicians are internationally recognized experts committed to providing children with the highest quality and most advanced care, delivered with compassion, integrity, and respect. Inquiries regarding this position should be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Paul Stricker via email at STRICKERP@chop.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182593": {
      "title": "Division Chief of CICU Clinician Educator - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Critical Care with a focus on Pediatric Cardiac Critical Care Medicine. The selected candidate will also serve in the role of Division Chief of Cardiac Critical Care Medicine at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree . Candidates must be ABP certified/board-eligible and eligible for medical licensure in Pennsylvania. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include developing systems for mentoring faculty and staff in the division to promote productive, rewarding careers and academic advancement. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of clinical cardiac critical care and medical direction in the Cardiac Intensive Care Unit at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. The Division Chief oversees the clinical activities of the Division and coordinates with leaders across the enterprise to optimize clinical operations. The Division supports numerous clinical programs across the Cardiac Center with the CICU capacity of 32 beds with surge capabilities for 40, and a growing average length of stay, reflecting the complexity of patient population. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include substantial commitment to research and evidence of continuous scholarly productivity reflecting a defined focus is required. We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Life and Professional Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/flpd/career-development/ . We are looking for an inspirational and innovative leader to lead one of the highest-profile premier academic pediatric cardiac critical care divisions. The successful candidate will transform the division in pursuit of achieving CHOP’s mission of excellence in clinical care, education, research, and advocacy. The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine maintains a robust, well-funded research enterprise, encompassing basic science, translational, clinical, and health services research programs that span all areas of anesthesiology and critical care medicine. Operating within the Department’s matrixed leadership structure, the Division Chief will support the Associate Chair of Research, the Associate Chief of Research, and the Department’s Research Council in advancing the Division’s research and academic missions. The Division Chief will collaborate with these Departmental leaders in developing and fostering collaborative research programs, managing infrastructure to support ongoing research efforts, allocating academic time and resources, and supporting and fostering funded research within the Division and across the Department. The Division of Cardiac Critical Care Medicine is in a strong phase and currently includes: 23 Attending physicians and two cardiac critical care advanced fellows. The Division Chief will report directly to the Chair of the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine and will work closely with the Physician Practice Director, Cardiac Center Chiefs and Leadership, other Division Chiefs, Associate Chairs, and the Vice Chair. Philadelphia is an ideal East Coast location, combining rich history, a vibrant arts and culture scene, diverse culinary experiences, and a variety of housing options both within the city and its surrounding areas. Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia is a national leader in the advancement of healthcare for children and is consistently in the top 5 in the US News & World Report. Our world-class physicians are internationally recognized experts committed to providing children with the highest quality and most advanced care, delivered with compassion, integrity, and respect. Inquiries regarding this position should be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Paul Stricker, via email at STRICKERP@chop.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175184": {
      "title": "Division Chief; Associate or Full; Tenure or Clinician Educator Track; Pediatric Hematology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Hematology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Division of Hematology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. The next Division Chief will lead one of the largest and most successful pediatric hematology programs in the nation and will be expected to participate in patient care, teaching, and scholarship.  The Division of Pediatric Hematology is comprised of over 32 faculty and attending physicians with diverse clinical, educational, and investigative interests, as well as 23 post-doctoral research fellows, 18 pediatric hematology oncology fellows and over 100 staff members. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, fellows, and APPs. The Division has responsibilities for training large numbers of medical students, residents, and fellows. Educating the next generation of pediatric hematology leaders is a priority of the Division, which holds an NIH T32 training grant in addition to dedicated and endowed training funds. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient or outpatient services at CHOP’s Main campus, King of Prussia campus and other sites.  The Division leads multiple robust outpatient clinical programs, including Bone Marrow Failure, Hemophilia, Platelet, Sickle Cell Disease and Thalassemia programs, providing care in over 6500 patient outpatient encounters per year. Multispecialty programs within the Division include leaders in pediatrics, nursing, psychology, and social work who are frequently partnered with leaders in associated research fields. The Division has a strong inpatient presence, which consists of a large teaching service at the Main CHOP Hospital Campus in Philadelphia. Numerous inpatient attendings provide primary and consultative care for over 5,900 inpatient encounters per year. The successful applicant will have a strong track record of scholarship and research. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include contributions to the field of pediatric hematology.  The Division encompasses a well-funded research enterprise, including basic science, translational, clinical and health services research programs and spanning all areas of the field.   Areas of research focus include hemoglobinopathies, hemostasis and thrombosis, and bone marrow failure. In addition, the Division is advancing transfusion medicine and cell-based therapies for hematologic diseases, including pioneering approaches for sickle cell disease, thalassemia, and hemophilia.  The next Division Chief will lead a large group of investigators, supporting their research endeavors through advocacy, mentorship, and development of philanthropic partnerships. The next Division Chief will have substantive opportunity to grow both clinical and investigative programs in the division that advance the field and CHOP’s mission. The Division Chief reports to the Chair of the Department of Pediatrics and works closely with the other Division Chiefs, the Associate Chairs, and the Vice Chair in the Department of Pediatrics. The Division Chief will oversee the clinical, research, and educational activities of the Division, lead recruiting efforts in the Division, and ensure career mentoring for all faculty and fellows in the Division. Inquiries about the position should be sent to the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Angela Ellison at ellisona@chop.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/174722": {
      "title": "Epidemiology (General) – Assistant Professor Positions",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology and Informatics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biostatistics and Epidemiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in either the non-tenure clinician educator track or the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of epidemiologic methods development and application, with the ability to establish oneself as a research leader in their area of specialization. While both tenure and clinician-educator track faculty conduct methodological and collaborative research, tenure track faculty focus primarily on methodological research while clinician-educator track faculty focus primarily on collaboration. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in departmental PhD, MSCE, and MS training programs. Candidates are expected to have a strong commitment to teaching and mentoring. Clinical responsibilities may include participation in clinical research, contributing expertise in study design and data analysis, and providing essential leadership to many of the clinical research programs at Penn Medicine. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing an independent, extramurally funded research program and/or serving as a key scientific collaborator in team-based science. We are particularly interested in candidates whose work aligns with one or more of the following strategic areas: •\tClimate Change and Health Epidemiology •\tHealth Equity and Social Epidemiology •\tImplementation Science The Division of Epidemiology includes over 65 full-time faculty with either a primary or secondary appointment who have diverse expertise across many different health-related and methodological areas. Ours is one of three divisions constituting the Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology and Informatics, an integral part of Penn Medicine, one of the nation’s top medical school and academic health systems, with strong links to the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia, one of the nation’s top children’s hospitals. The University of Pennsylvania’s twelve schools share a compact urban campus, providing a vibrant, collaborative environment with unique access to health and biomedical data and clinical research collaborators."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194579": {
      "title": "Executive Director of the Healthy Weight and Obesity Medicine Program",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pediatric obesity medicine, pediatric weight management, and population health; significant leadership experience in a complex academic medical or healthcare environment; demonstrated ability to lead multidisciplinary teams and build collaborative programs across organizational boundaries; strong record of clinical innovation, scholarship, or research; demonstrated commitment to improving health outcomes for children and adolescents; experience partnering with communities, schools, public health organizations, payers, and policymakers; and excellent communication, relationship-building, and organizational leadership skills. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Qualifications include board certification in pediatrics and obesity medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows and delivering formal lectures in the Department of Pediatrics. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient care for pediatric patients who are overweight or obese. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing independent and collaborative research programs related obesity medicine and nutrition. The successful candidate will work across clinical, research, public health, community, policy, and health-system domains to build a nationally distinctive model of pediatric obesity care. Important collaborators will include leaders of CHOP Primary Care, Population Health, Community Impact, Research Institute, and relevant subspecialty divisions, among others. In addition to leading the Obesity Program, the Executive Director will serve as a key institutional leader for obesity-related initiatives within the CHOP Community Outcomes Accelerator, the CHOP PolicyLab, the CHOP Population Health Initiative, and the CHOP Research Institute, creating a powerful platform for translating evidence into practice and improving outcomes at scale. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae and cover letter via Interfolio. Inquiries about the position should be sent to the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Joseph St. Geme at StGemeIIIJ@chop.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190926": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Infectious Diseases - Transplant Infectious Diseases Clinical Research",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Infectious Diseases Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Infectious Diseases in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Transplant Infectious Diseases. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Infectious Diseases. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching Infectious Diseases fellows, residents and medical students as well as mentoring of masters level clinical research trainees, and course instruction. Clinical responsibilities may include include inpatient weeks at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania as well as outpatient sessions at the Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include designing and implementing observational and interventional studies focused on the identification, treatment, and prevention of infections in the transplant patient population. Scholarship is required in the clinician-educator track. The major focus of this position is to further develop the Infectious Diseases Division's research program focused on Transplant Infectious Diseases. Development of a research focus on diagnosis, treatment and prevention of infections in this population will build on an extensive clinical program in Transplant Infectious Diseases and be highly complementary to the research activities of investigators in other disciplines. Numerous opportunities to collaborate with current research faculty exist."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177099": {
      "title": "Faculty Position, Ambulatory Practices - Academic Clinician, Junior rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - General Internal Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of General Internal Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine is required. Teaching responsibilities may include precepting residents and interns throughout their General Medicine rotations. Successful candidates will also have the opportunity to participate in UME or GME educational programs. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include sessions providing direct patient care in one of our ambulatory sites, Edward S. Cooper, Penn Internal Medicine University City, Penn Center for Primary Care, Pennsylvania Hospital Wood Clinic. Clinical responsibilities may also include serving as inpatient attending at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center or Pennsylvania Hospital. Providing after hours phone coverage may also be included."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177097": {
      "title": "Faculty Position, Ambulatory Practices - Academic Clinician, Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - General Internal Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of General Internal Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine is required. Teaching responsibilities may include precepting residents and interns throughout their General Medicine rotations. Successful candidates will also have the opportunity to participate in UME or GME educational programs. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per/year of active and high-quality teaching responsibilities. Clinical responsibilities may include sessions providing direct patient care in one of our ambulatory sites, Edward S. Cooper, Penn Internal Medicine University City, Penn Center for Primary Care, Pennsylvania Hospital Wood Clinic. Clinical responsibilities may also include serving as inpatient attending at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center or Pennsylvania Hospital Providing after hours phone coverage may also be included. Prior experience as faculty at other academic institutions in general medical practice at the Associate or Full Professor rank is required. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching with institutional awards, completion of a graduate program or professional certificate program, or significant institutional, regional or national leadership roles. Successful candidates will benefit from Penn’s robust mentorship and faculty development programs and rich opportunities in quality/process improvement, informatics, medical education, and health care innovation. There will be an expectation of the ability of candidates to provide management and/or leadership. Rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190726": {
      "title": "Faculty Position, VA Medical Center, Division of Hematology/Oncology, Academic Clinician Track - Junior rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Philadelphia VA Medical Center (PVAMC) and the Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification or board eligibility in Medical Oncology and/or Hematology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching hematology/oncology fellows, residents, and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities include caring for patients with classical hematologic disorders and hematologic malignancies. A focus on multiple myeloma and plasma cell disorders is of particular interest. Candidates may engage in clinical investigation, but experience and/or advanced training in the conduct of clinical trials is not required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190724": {
      "title": "Faculty Position, VA Medical Center, Division of Hematology/Oncology, Academic Clinician Track - Senior ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Philadelphia VA Medical Center (PVAMC) and the Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification or board eligibility in Medical Oncology and/or Hematology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching hematology/oncology fellows, residents, and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include caring for patients with classical hematologic disorders and hematologic malignancies. A focus on multiple myeloma and plasma cell disorders is of particular interest. Candidates may engage in clinical investigation but experience and/or advanced training in the conduct of clinical trials is not required. There will be an expectation of the ability of selected candidates to provide management and/or leadership. Rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188627": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in The Department of Physiology and The Cardiovascular Institute",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Physiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Physiology and the Cardiovascular Institute (CVI) at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the tenure track . Applicants must have a Ph.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree. We are seeking candidates with significant postdoctoral training or similar experience. The position comes with a competitive start-up package and lab space, protected time for the establishment of an independent research program and mentoring by supportive faculty in the Physiology Department and CVI. Teaching responsibilities may include graduate and medical student instruction and training graduate students and postdoctoral fellows. Research or scholarship responsibilities include developing a successful, extramurally supported research program. We seek investigators with demonstrated excellence in research grounded in fundamental mechanistic investigation that leverages molecular, biophysical, cellular and/or organismal insights to inform physiological or pathological processes in the cardiovascular system, particularly those emphasizing emerging areas, novel technologies, and interdisciplinary areas. Areas of interest include but are not limited to mitochondrial biology, cardiovascular metabolism, mechanotransduction, calcium signaling, vascular biology, cardiovascular-related interorgan communication, and gene regulation; research excellence will be weighed more strongly than specific research interests. In addition to the world-class facilities available at the University, the Department of Physiology and CVI are supported by extensive shared resources, including Super-Resolution Imaging, Muscle Physiology and Mechanics, Small Animal Cardiovascular Phenotyping, and Metabolomics Cores. The ideal candidate will have a vision for leveraging the rich, uniquely collaborative, environment at the University of Pennsylvania to tackle fundamental questions in cardiovascular biology. The Perelman School of Medicine, one of the top ranked medical schools in the country for NIH funding, offers access to state-of-the-art core facilities ( https://www.med.upenn.edu/cores/ ) and opportunities for appointments in numerous additional institutes and centers ( https://www.med.upenn.edu/psom/centers.html ). Retention and success of junior faculty is at the core of our mission, and multiple support programs and career development opportunities are provided (e.g., https://www.med.upenn.edu/evdresearch/the-richards-society.html ). The School of Medicine is integrated within the campus of the University of Pennsylvania, a world-class institution with an easily walkable campus located near central Philadelphia. Interested individuals should submit: 1.) Cover Letter 2.) Curriculum Vitae 3.) Research Statement (3-page limit) 4.) 4 Confidential Letters of Recommendation. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, with those received by September 1, 2026, given priority. Interested individuals should submit: 1.) Cover Letter 2.) Curriculum Vitae 3.) Research Statement (3-page limit) 4.) 4 Confidential Letters of Recommendation. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, with those received by September 1, 2026, given priority."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194060": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in the Division of Addiction Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Family Medicine and Community Health Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Addiction Medicine within the Department of Family Medicine and Community Health at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for multiple faculty positions in Addiction Medicine in the non-tenure Academic Clinician (AC) track. Successful candidates will hold an M.D. or D.O. degree and must have primary board in a recognized ABMS or AOA Specialty and must be board certified in Addiction Medicine. They should have experience in hospital-based addiction medicine consultation and in underserved and vulnerable patient care and an interest in a career in academic medicine. Preferred candidates will have completion of an Addiction Medicine fellowship; experience in inpatient consultation services; experience caring for patients with opioid use disorder and other substance use disorders; experience working in Bridge/OTP or low-barrier treatment programs. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the education and supervision of residents, fellows, and medical students in inpatient, consultative, ambulatory, and Bridge/OTP settings. Opportunities for educational leadership and program development may be available for the right candidate. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical care based primarily at Pennsylvania Hospital, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, HUP Cedar, Bridge/Opioid Treatment Services (OTP) services, and other Penn Medicine-affiliated clinical settings. Faculty may participate in ambulatory addiction medicine, Bridge/OTP services, treatment of opioid and other substance use disorders, hospital-based addiction treatment, community-based addiction services, resident and fellow supervision, and multidisciplinary care coordination. All faculty members will devote a portion of their clinical effort to inpatient Addiction Medicine consult services at one or more Penn Medicine hospitals, including Pennsylvania Hospital, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, and HUP Cedar. The Division of Addiction Medicine is recruiting for three full-time faculty positions that will support Penn Medicine's growing addiction medicine clinical, educational, and community programs. These positions offer flexibility in clinical practice location and scope while supporting access to evidence-based addiction treatment across Penn Medicine. The Division of Addiction Medicine serves diverse patients across Philadelphia, including many individuals and communities that have historically experienced barriers to health care access and health equity. We seek candidates who demonstrate a commitment to caring for medically and socially complex patient populations and who have experience working in underserved communities and resource-limited clinical settings. Academic Clinician faculty are not required to maintain an independent research program; however, scholarly activity, quality improvement, curriculum development, and educational innovation are encouraged and supported."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161040": {
      "title": "Full/Associate Professor-Tenure Track-Alzheimer’s Disease Genetics and Genomics-Division of Neuropathology and Neurodegeneration",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of human genetics/genomics, computer science, bioinformatics, neuroscience, neurology, or related fields. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or Ph.D equivalent degree required. Teaching responsibilities may include mentoring of PhD students, postdoctoral researchers, teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as formal course directing and lecture opportunities within the Perelman School of Medicine. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include (1) Identification of genetic risk factors for Alzheimer’s Disease utilizing PNGC’s extensive data collection and cutting-edge genomic analysis tools; (2) Development of genomic biomarkers for early diagnosis and risk prediction using genetic and genomic approaches; (3) Functional genomics and mechanisms of neurodegeneration genetic susceptibility; (4) Therapeutic target discovery and validation by integrating human genetic and functional data; (5) Investigation of the genetic basis of neurodegenerative diseases across diverse populations to understand health disparities. The Penn Neurodegeneration Genomics Center (PNGC) at the University of Pennsylvania is a premier research institute at the forefront of understanding the genetic mechanisms underlying neurodegenerative diseases. PNGC is renowned for its interdisciplinary approach, combining genomics, bioinformatics, neuroscience, and clinical research. Our faculty members benefit from the center’s substantial grant funding and leadership roles in major consortia and unparalleled opportunities for high-impact research and access to extensive biobank resources. PNGC is uniquely positioned to drive groundbreaking discoveries in conditions including Alzheimer’s disease, Progress Supranuclear Palsy, and other related dementias. As a tenure-track faculty member, the appointee will display accomplishment in developing a nationally or internationally recognized independent research program supported by extramural funding and synergizing with the PNGC AD genetics portfolio. For full professor appointment leadership in the field should be evident. Priorities will be given to candidates with strengths in managing large collaborative genomics research projects, can contribute to or synergize with our primary Alzheimer’s disease (AD) genetics portfolio. Additionally, as a senior faculty member in the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine and PNGC, the candidate is expected to participate in departmental and PNGC service activities, such as committees or other leadership roles. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195674": {
      "title": "General Nephrology Faculty Position, Assistant Professor - Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of general nephrology, including the evaluation and management of acute kidney injury, chronic kidney disease across all stages, kidney failure, and dialysis (in-center and home modalities), with the clinical skills necessary to provide high-quality inpatient and outpatient nephrology care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board certified or board eligible in Nephrology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, internal medicine residents, and nephrology fellows at the Perelman School of Medicine, the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, and affiliated Penn Medicine sites through clinical supervision, bedside teaching, and other educational activities. Clinical responsibilities may include providing comprehensive inpatient and outpatient care for patients with a broad range of kidney diseases, including acute kidney injury, chronic kidney disease (CKD), and end-stage kidney disease (ESKD). Responsibilities may include ambulatory general nephrology care, inpatient nephrology consultations, and management of patients receiving in-center and home dialysis at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and affiliated clinical sites. Opportunities may also include clinical involvement in specialized areas of nephrology based on the candidate's expertise and the needs of the Division. The Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks an outstanding candidate for an Assistant Professor position on the Academic Clinician track specializing in general nephrology. The Division is one of the nation's leading academic nephrology programs, with a long tradition of excellence in patient care, education, and discovery. Faculty provide comprehensive kidney care across general and consultative nephrology, chronic kidney disease, hypertension, and in-center and home dialysis, and train nephrology fellows in an ACGME-accredited fellowship program. The successful candidate will join a collaborative, collegial group of clinicians, educators, and investigators, with access to the clinical, educational, and research resources of Penn Medicine. We seek a dedicated clinician who demonstrates strong clinical skills, a commitment to high-quality patient care, and enthusiasm for teaching and interdisciplinary collaboration. Candidates with focused clinical interests, such as home dialysis, glomerular disease, onco-nephrology, or hypertension, are encouraged to apply. Participation in clinical research, quality improvement, and educational scholarship is encouraged and supported but not required. Faculty on the Academic Clinician track are expected to maintain an active, high-quality teaching commitment (100 teaching credits per year)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195672": {
      "title": "General Nephrology Faculty Position, Associate or Full Professor - Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of general nephrology, including advanced clinical experience in the evaluation and management of acute kidney injury, chronic kidney disease across all stages, kidney failure, and dialysis (in-center and home modalities), with a demonstrated record of clinical excellence, teaching effectiveness, and contributions to academic clinical practice. Additional expertise in areas such as glomerular disease, onco-nephrology, or hypertension is welcome. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board certified or board eligible in Nephrology. Teaching responsibilities may include providing clinical education, supervision, and mentorship to medical students, internal medicine residents, and nephrology fellows at the Perelman School of Medicine, the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, and affiliated Penn Medicine sites. Responsibilities may also include leading educational activities, contributing to curriculum development, and supporting the professional development of trainees through bedside teaching, clinical supervision, and formal educational sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include providing comprehensive inpatient and outpatient care for patients with complex kidney diseases, including acute kidney injury, chronic kidney disease (CKD), and end-stage kidney disease (ESKD). Responsibilities may include ambulatory general nephrology care, inpatient nephrology consultations, and management of patients receiving in-center and home dialysis at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and affiliated clinical sites. The successful candidate may also contribute to clinical program development, quality improvement initiatives, and multidisciplinary care coordination, with opportunities for clinical leadership based on experience and the needs of the Division. The Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks an experienced general nephrologist for an Associate Professor position on the Academic Clinician track. The Division is one of the nation's leading academic nephrology programs, with a long tradition of excellence in patient care, education, and discovery. Faculty provide comprehensive kidney care across general and consultative nephrology, chronic kidney disease, hypertension, and in-center and home dialysis, and train nephrology fellows in an ACGME-accredited fellowship program. The successful candidate will join a collaborative, collegial group of clinicians, educators, and investigators, with access to the clinical, educational, and research resources of Penn Medicine. We seek an accomplished clinician with a demonstrated record of excellence in patient care, clinical teaching, and interdisciplinary collaboration. The ideal candidate will bring substantial experience in general nephrology and a commitment to mentoring trainees, supporting the development of clinical services, and contributing to the continued growth of the Division. Candidates with additional expertise in home dialysis, glomerular disease, onco-nephrology, or hypertension are encouraged to apply. Participation in clinical research, quality improvement, and educational scholarship is encouraged and supported but not required. Faculty on the Academic Clinician track are expected to maintain an active, high-quality teaching commitment (100 teaching credits per year). There will be an expectation of the ability of the selected candidate to provide management and/or leadership. Academic rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185755": {
      "title": "General Non-Invasive Cardiologist",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of outpatient and inpatient consultative cardiology. Highly motivated and ambitious candidates who are interested in general cardiology as well as those with a focused interest in developing a clinical practice in emerging specialties including cardio-oncology, women's cardiovascular disease, aortopathy and aortic medicine, vascular medicine, HIV cardiovascular disease, and geriatric cardiology are highly desired. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible in cardiovascular disease. Teaching responsibilities may include the education of medical students, residents, cardiovascular fellows and advanced practice providers. Selected candidates will be expected to contribute to the educational mission of the organization. Clinical responsibilities may include the development of an outpatient clinical practice as well as attending on the inpatient services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and associated practice sites and involvement in non-invasive imaging. Physicians in the consultative cardiology section work closely with the other clinical sections including heart failure and electrophysiology as well as the cardiac and vascular surgeons to provide exceptional care for complex conditions in both the inpatient and outpatient setting. The ideal candidate will be committed to the continued growth and clinical development of the division. Located in the heart of Philadelphia, Penn Medicine offers a uniquely dynamic environment that blends world-class academic medicine with the energy of a major metropolitan center. Its strategic position provides seamless access to New Jersey, New York, Maryland, and Washington, D.C., placing faculty at the center of one of the most densely networked healthcare and research corridors in the country. The region supports robust collaboration, diverse patient populations, and extensive professional opportunities across clinical care, research, education, and leadership—making it an exceptionally attractive destination for those seeking both career advancement and a vibrant, accessible place to live and work."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193129": {
      "title": "General Obstetrics and Gynecology, Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of obstetrics and gynecology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical training and supervision of medical students and residents and participation in formal teaching curriculum. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient prenatal and gynecology care, labor and delivery coverage, and gynecologic surgery. The successful candidate would join Penn Medicine Division of Academic Specialists, a group of full-time obstetricians and gynecologists, advanced practice providers including midwives, in a faculty practice at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Excellent clinical and interpersonal skills are required. A commitment to resident and medical student education is required. The successful candidate will receive fully-covered malpractice insurance and practice in a supportive environment that provides professional and personal fulfillment and career-long learning."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158182": {
      "title": "General Obstetrics and Gynecology, Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of obstetrics and gynecology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified/eligible by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical training and supervision of medical students and residents and participation in formal teaching curriculum. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient prenatal and gynecology care, labor and delivery coverage, and gynecologic surgery. The successful candidate would join Penn Medicine Division of Academic Specialists, a group of full-time obstetricians and gynecologists, advanced practice providers including midwives, in a faculty practice at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania. Excellent clinical and interpersonal skills are required. A commitment to resident and medical student education is required. The successful candidate will receive fully-covered malpractice insurance and practice in a supportive environment that provides professional and personal fulfillment and career-long learning. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188055": {
      "title": "Genitourinary Cancers - Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Genitourinary Cancers. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification or board eligible in Medical Oncology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching hematology/oncology fellows, house staff and medical students. Applicants must have excellent qualifications in teaching. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients with genitourinary cancer, including prostate, bladder, testicular, and renal malignancies in an outpatient setting and as an attending on the inpatient service."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188057": {
      "title": "Genitourinary Cancers, Associate or Full Professor - Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Genitourinary Cancers. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification or eligible in Medical Oncology is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching hematology/oncology fellows, house staff and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Applicants must have excellent qualifications in teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care for patients with genitourinary cancer, including prostate, bladder, testicular, and renal malignancies in an outpatient setting and as an attending on the inpatient service. There will be an expectation of the ability of selected candidates to provide management and/or leadership."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177727": {
      "title": "Geriatrics Hospitalist position - Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Geriatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Geriatrics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Geriatric Medicine including clinical care and education. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABIM or ABFM certification and Geriatric Medicine certification/eligibility is required. Teaching responsibilities may include training medical students, residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include hospital care on the Acute Care for Elderly (ACE) unit."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190718": {
      "title": "GI Oncology at Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of gastrointestinal cancers. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board certified or board eligible in Medical Oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching hematology/oncology fellows, residents, and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients with gastrointestinal cancers in an outpatient setting and as an attending on the inpatient service. Enrolling patients onto clinical trials is an important role in this position."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191705": {
      "title": "Gynecologic Oncologist, Assistant Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Gynecology Oncology and minimally invasive surgery. Successful applicants must have demonstrated excellent qualifications in education and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified in Ob/Gyn and ACGME-fellowship trained in Gynecologic Oncology and board certified in gynecologic oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching Gyn Oncology fellows, Ob/Gyn residents and medical students and participate in clinical research including clinical trials. Clinical responsibilities may include out-patient consultations for women with gynecologic cancers as well as in-patient consultation and operative care primarily based at Pennsylvania Hospital. The successful candidate will join an established Division of Gynecologic Oncology at PENN Medicine and its affiliated hospitals. Candidates should have excellent surgical skills including minimally invasive surgery. The division is a member of the Gynecologic Oncology Group (GOG/NRG). Candidates will enjoy full coverage professional liability insurance."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192912": {
      "title": "Gynecologic Oncology, Assistant Professor of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Clinician-Educator",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Gynecologic Oncology and have demonstrated excellent qualifications in education, research, and clinical care. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Candidate must be BC/BE in Ob/Gyn and Gynecologic Oncology and subspecialty trained in Gynecologic Oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and supervising medical students, Ob/Gyn residents and Gynecologic Oncology fellows, and participation in formal curriculum. Clinical responsibilities may include out-patient consultations for women with gynecologic cancers as well as in-patient consultation and operative care at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Pennsylvania Hospital, Chester County Hospital and Penn Medicine satellite practice sites. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include basic, translational, clinical and/or health policy research. Collaborative science is highly valued. Expertise in advanced observational study methods including coding and analyses of large databases. A strong advocate of multinational collaborations is a bonus. Candidate will join a group of 10 physicians and physician scientists who provide clinical services at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Pennsylvania Hospital and Chester County Hospital. The Division has an ACGME-accredited Fellowship in Gynecologic Oncology with six fellows (2/year) and participates in the Division participates in the NRG cooperative group trials and a very active Section of Population Science research."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171707": {
      "title": "Heart Failure Cardiologist, Director of the LVAD and MCS program, Associate Professor of Clinical Medicine - PPMC",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. The selected candidate will also serve as the Director of the LVAD and MCS program. Expertise is required in the specific area of training in VAD and Pulmonary Hypertension. Subspeciality training with demonstrated skills is required in advanced heart failure: LVAD and MCS. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board Certification in Internal Medicine, Cardiovascular Diseases, and Heart Failure is required. Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, a premier tertiary care hospital within the University of Pennsylvania Health System, is seeking a full-time, board-certified Heart Failure Cardiologist to serve as Director of the LVAD and MCS program. The ideal candidate will have demonstrated excellence in the management of mechanical circulatory support (MCS), as well as a strong interest in program development, quality improvement, and multidisciplinary collaboration. The selected candidate will be expected to serve as a mentor and leader. Previous leadership experience is a plus. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and supervision of medical students and residents, including training of cardiovascular fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include serving as Medical Director for the LVAD/MCS Program, overseeing patient selection, perioperative management, and long-term care. Managing the cardiogenic shock and mechanical circulatory support program. Collaborating closely with cardiothoracic surgery, transplant, critical care, and other specialties to identify patient candidates and optimize outcomes. Leading efforts to enhance programmatic quality, efficiency, and volume, with a focus on growth and national excellence. Contributing to transplant evaluation and management, with flexibility in the degree of involvement based on candidate interests. Outpatient office care, inpatient consultations at Penn Presbyterian as well as affiliated satellite offices. This is an outstanding opportunity for an individual with leadership experience who enjoys working in a vibrant urban environment with an abundance of cultural resources, including music, art, theatres, and fine dining (www.upenn.edu/life-at-penn/philadelphia). Philadelphia offers easy access to New York and Washington DC. Additionally, Wissahickon Valley Park, Valley Forge."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175957": {
      "title": "Hospitalist Scholars – Subspecialty Track, Instructor position",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hospital Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hospital Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/board eligible in General Internal Medicine or Family Medicine is required. Responsibilities may include nights and weekends at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, as well as limited weekend shifts at Good Shepherd Penn Partners Long Term Acute Care Hospital (LTACH). In addition to a competitive salary and generous benefits, Scholars are eligible to receive an annual bonus, which can be applied towards loan repayment at the end of each year of clinical service completed. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to work with mentors in the sub-specialty field of their choice. Through this mentorship, scholars will gain experience and insight into the field while engaging in scholarly projects intended to result in presentations at scientific meetings or peer-reviewed publications. Additional opportunities for mentorship within hospital medicine are also available. Scholars will participate in structured career development activities, along with other junior faculty in the Division of Hospital Medicine, intended to create a solid foundation for independent practice of inpatient medicine. This Instructor position in Hospital Medicine is a part of a unique career development program known as the Penn Hospitalist Subspecialty Scholars Program. This program is designed specifically for recent graduates of internal medicine residencies seeking a short-term (1-3 years) hospitalist position before moving on to the next phase of their career – typically a sub-specialty fellowship or secondary residency."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189725": {
      "title": "Inpatient Geriatric Faculty Position - Assistant Professor, Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Geriatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Geriatrics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABIM or ABFM certification and Geriatric Medicine certification/eligibility is required. Teaching responsibilities may include training medical students, residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient care on a geriatric co-management/consultative service and Acute Care of the Elders Unit."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189724": {
      "title": "Inpatient Geriatric Faculty Position - Associate/Full Professor, Academic Clinician Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Geriatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Geriatrics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABIM or ABFM certification and Geriatric Medicine certification/eligibility is required. Teaching responsibilities may include training medical students, residents, and fellows. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include inpatient care on a geriatric co-management/consultation service and Acute Care of the Elders Unit. There will be an expectation of the ability of selected candidates to provide management and/or leadership. Rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172312": {
      "title": "Instructor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Responsibilities may include development of research credentials, including scholarship. Clinical duties and the teaching of residents, medical students, and/or fellows is also required. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to attend several educational seminars to prepare them for an academic career."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172844": {
      "title": "Instructor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Emergency Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of Emergency Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABEM certified or board eligible. Responsibilities may include teaching third and fourth year medical students, Emergency Medicine residents, Ultrasound fellows, and house staff rotating from other clinical departments, i.e. Medicine and Pediatric Emergency Medicine. Instructors will also provide emergency medical care to patients presented to the emergency department at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to complete a Masters of Science in Clinical Epidemiology through the Center for Clinical Epidemiology and Biostatistics (CCEB) in the Department of Biostatistics and Epidemiology."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183932": {
      "title": "Instructor (Dermatology)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board Certified/Eligible in Dermatology is required. Responsibilities may include additional professional training in general dermatology and complex medical dermatology while developing expertise in teaching, administration, or clinical research. The applicant must have demonstrated research interest related to dermatology with a desire to start an independent career. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop expertise in a focused area of clinical research, and enhanced experience within a specialized clinical program. The individual will have opportunities to apply for sponsored research funding, including Career Development Awards from foundations."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168366": {
      "title": "Instructor - Anesthesiology and Critical Care",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Responsibilities may include teaching and clinical responsibilities. Teaching responsibilities for this position include the instruction of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the operating rooms and wards of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and the Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC) as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities for this position include the provision of clinical anesthesia at HUP and PPMC. Opportunities are available with a focus in neuroanesthesia, obstetrical, cardiovascular, and/or critical care, including tele-critical care. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to participate in several educational seminars to prepare them for an academic career. Are you interested in this position but are unsure about if it's the right fit? We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Office of Academic Affairs website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/faculty-career-development/ The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE and individuals from all backgrounds are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176535": {
      "title": "Instructor - Ultrasound Fellow",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hospital Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hospital Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified or eligible in General Internal Medicine or Family Medicine is required. Responsibilities may include nights and weekends at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center and/or Good Shepherd Penn Partners Long Term Acute Care Hospital (LTACH). The successful applicant will have an opportunity to receive mentorship and structured career development within Hospital Medicine. Application and recruitment will be handled in concert with the Department of Emergency Medicine. This Instructor position in Hospital Medicine is part of a unique non-ACGME fellowship with the Department of Emergency Medicine. The incumbent will be provided didactic and clinical training in ultrasound, while also working clinically as an attending physician on hospital medicine services."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175455": {
      "title": "Instructor -- Pathology and Laboratory Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of Pathology and/or Laboratory Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be Board Certified and Board Eligible in Anatomic and/or Clinical Pathology or another pathology-related specialty. Responsibilities may include supporting the clinical and educational missions of the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop an individual training experience in research skills and teaching, while developing a career in an academic setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/166757": {
      "title": "Instructor at the Center for the Treatment and Study of Anxiety",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Clinical licensure in Pennsylvania is required. Responsibilities may include teaching at all levels of medical education, providing supervision as needed, providing clinical care, helping conduct studies of the presentation and treatment of psychiatric disorders, and other duties as assigned. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to advance the research, teaching, and clinical missions of the Center for Treatment and Study of Anxiety."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169221": {
      "title": "Instructor in Community Psychiatry",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Active PA medical license and ABPN eligibility or certification are also required. Responsibilities may include providing psychiatric care in a community setting; participating in seminar series and supervision; completing policy, quality, and/or administrative projects; engaging and consulting with local administrative and policy partners; teaching at all levels of medical education; and other duties as assigned. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to gain subspecialty experience in community psychiatry; develop leadership, quality improvement, and teaching skills; gain policy and administrative experience through close relationships with city and community partners; engage in scholarly pursuits and attend conferences; and benefit from mentorship and networking opportunities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158713": {
      "title": "Instructor in Department of Genetics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Genetics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of human genetics, developmental genetics, epigenetics, functional genomics, or computational genomics. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Responsibilities may include designing and carrying out genetic experiments, as well as preparation of manuscripts and supervision of students. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to receive mentorship in grants writing and grants proposals suitable to early-stage academic investigators. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171560": {
      "title": "Instructor in Glomerular Disease Onco-Nephrology - Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension Division",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certification or board eligibility (ABIM) in Nephrology is required. Responsibilities may include treating patients with glomerular disease or treating kidney disorders in the setting of cancer and its treatments. The successful applicant will have the opportunity to participate in the many educational activities of the Division, including teaching medical students, residents, and fellows. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to receive specialized clinical and research training with patients with glomerular disease and in the field of onco-nephrology (kidney disease in the setting of cancer and its treatments). The ideal candidate will have the opportunity to develop expertise in clinical epidemiology, laboratory research, or translational research and be committed to pursuing an academic career in nephrology."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/170150": {
      "title": "Instructor in Population Mental Health",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of implementation science, mental health/substance use services research, and clinical psychology. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Psychology license or license eligible as a psychologist in PA or equivalent preferred. Responsibilities may include conducting and supporting mental health services and implementation science research focused on increasing access to evidence-based interventions for mental health and substance use disorders in traditionally underserved communities. Opportunities to teach and mentor students and clinicians in training and to conduct clinical work in the Psychiatry department within the candidate's area of specialization are available. We are particularly interested in candidates who conduct research in partnership with historically underserved communities, service systems, and indigenous populations and who can contribute to our growing global mental health program. The candidate will be assisted in developing a career in an academic setting per their assigned section within the department of Psychiatry. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop an individual mentored experience in research skills and teaching while developing a career in an academic setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173183": {
      "title": "Instructor in Statistical Genetics of Substance Use Disorders",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of statistical genetics, bioinformatics, machine learning, and substance use disorders. Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Responsibilities may include conducting statistical analyses of large datasets using statistical genetics methods and bioinformatics software. Using machine learning methods to conduct multi-omics analyses. Providing instruction to trainees and supervising their use of these methods. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to access large genetic and epigenetic datasets for analysis."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177803": {
      "title": "Instructor in the Department of Neurosurgery specializing in Neuroendovascular and Cerebrovascular Surgery",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurosurgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurosurgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of neuroendovascular and cerebrovascular surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates should have completed fellowships in endovascular neurosurgery and cerebrovascular microsurgery. Responsibilities may include neuroendovascular and microsurgical treatment of cerebrovascular disorders including aneurysms, AVMs, ischemic disorders of the brain and spine, and hemorrhagic and ischemic strokes at Penn Medicine and affiliated hospital sites. Research or scholarship opportunities may include collaborations on clinical research in cerebrovascular and neurovascular technology. The successful applicant will be responsible for the education of medical students and residents, and fellows within the neuroendovascular fellowship. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to grow their expertise in the management of complex hemorrhagic and ischemic stroke cases and other cerebrovascular disorders with faculty supervision and mentorship. There is also an opportunity to develop skills in building a clinical practice and a referral network."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192068": {
      "title": "Instructor in Translational Medicine and Human Genetics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Translational Medicine and Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Translational Medicine and Human Genetics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of human genetics, developmental genetics, epigenetics, functional genomics, or computational genomics. Applicants must have an Ph.D. and/or M.D. degree. Responsibilities may include designing and carrying out genetic experiments, as well as preparation of manuscripts and supervision of students. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to receive mentorship in grant writing and grant proposals suitable to early-stage academic investigators."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158751": {
      "title": "Instructor in Translational Medicine and Human Genetics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Translational Medicine and Human Genetics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Translational Medicine and Human Genetics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of human genetics, developmental genetics, epigenetics, functional genomics, or computational genomics. Applicants must have an Ph.D. and/or M.D. degree. Responsibilities may include designing and carrying out genetic experiments, as well as preparation of manuscripts and supervision of students. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to receive mentorship in grant writing and grant proposals suitable to early-stage academic investigators. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187578": {
      "title": "Instructor in Translational Neuroscience",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of neurophysiology, systems neuroscience, translational neuroimaging, or related fields. Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Responsibilities may include conducting translational neuroscience research focused on mechanisms of electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) and neuromodulation using mouse models and human neuroimaging approaches; designing and performing experiments involving in vivo optical imaging, electrophysiology, behavioral phenotyping, and computational analysis; contributing to the development and implementation of clinical translational research protocols related to ECT and other neuromodulation interventions; analyzing and interpreting experimental data; preparing manuscripts and presentations for scientific meetings and peer-reviewed publication; assisting with mentorship and training of students and research staff; and participating in collaborative interdisciplinary research activities within the Department of Psychiatry and affiliated neuroscience programs. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to work closely with faculty across psychiatry, neurology, neuroscience, engineering, and neuroimaging; leverage advanced optical imaging and systems neuroscience approaches in both animal models and human studies; contribute to ongoing clinical and translational investigations in ECT and related interventions; pursue career development and extramural funding opportunities; and participate in the education and mentorship of trainees within Penn Psychiatry’s physician-scientist training environment. Prior experience with translational neuroscience research, in vivo imaging, electrophysiology, computational analysis, or neuromodulation approaches is preferred. Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively in an interdisciplinary research environment are highly desirable."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/166835": {
      "title": "Instructor of Musculoskeletal Imaging",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible. The successful candidates must also have completed a diagnostic radiology residency. Responsibilities may include providing final interpretations of x-ray and bone radiographs. The successful candidate will also participate in shared after-hour and weekend coverage, case review series, and didactic lectures with residents and musculoskeletal imaging fellows. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop research and advanced clinical expertise credentials. Instructors are provided with research and educational support to prepare them for an academic and/or clinical career. A specialized research focus may be developed in consultation with the division chief. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veteran Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania and New Jersey."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173817": {
      "title": "Instructor of Neurology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. The successful candidate will have demonstrated excellent qualifications in education and research and be Board-Certified or Board Eligible in Neurology. Responsibilities may include clinical experiences in both the in-patient and out-patient settings that will be specific to the division and expertise of the individual candidate. These responsibilities will vary and may include Cognitive Neurology, Epilepsy, General Neurology, Multiple Sclerosis, Neurointensivist, Neurogenetics, Neuromuscular Disease, Neuro-ophthalmology, Neuro-psychology, Parkinson's Disease, Movement Disorders, Sleep Disorders, Stroke or Critical Care related topics. The candidate will be assisted in developing a career in an academic setting per their assigned division within the department of Neurology. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop an individual training experience in research skills and teaching while developing a career in an academic setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/166286": {
      "title": "Instructor of Nuclear Medicine Imaging and Therapy",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board eligible or have specialty certification in nuclear medicine, either current American Board of Nuclear Medicine certification or a CAQ in nuclear radiology from the American Board of Radiology, and have completed a nuclear medicine or nuclear radiology ACGME-approved training program. Responsibilities may include performing and interpreting nuclear medicine stress tests, EKGs, evaluating and treating patients with therapeutic radio-pharmaceuticals and general nuclear medicine studies. Candidates must have extensive PET/CT experience. The successful candidate will also participate in shared after-hour and weekend coverage, case review series, and didactic lectures with residents and nuclear medicine imaging and therapy fellows. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop research credentials. Instructors are provided with research and educational support to prepare them for an academic and/or clinical career. A specialized research focus may be developed in consultation with the division chief. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veteran Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania and New Jersey."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178871": {
      "title": "Instructor of Ob/Gyn in Global Women's Health Fellowship",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This position is for a two-year fellowship that provides intensive clinical experiences both domestically and internationally, as well as academic support for a scholarly project and a master’s degree. Please visit UPenn’s Global Women's Health Fellowship site at https://www.pennmedicine.org/departments-and-centers/obstetrics-and-gynecology/education-and-training/fellowship-programs/womens-health-global-fellowship. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to two (2) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be trained in Obstetrics and Gynecology and board certified/eligible in Ob/Gyn. Responsibilities may include conducting basic, translational and/or clinical research in women's global health. Additional training will be provided in clinical and/or basic science research related to this field. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to participate in clinical responsibilities as a member of the Academic Specialists in Penn Ob/Gyn Associates."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181603": {
      "title": "Instructor of Pediatric Neurology at CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Instructor position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include developing a research program that leads to new understanding in the pathobiology of neuromuscular disorders at a basic science and translational level. Clinical duties will include serving as an attending in the pediatric neuromuscular disease clinic with the option to also attend in the adult neuromuscular clinic. Successful candidates must have expertise in the diagnosis and management of neuromuscular disorders. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop an individual training experience in research skills and teaching in an academic setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/141400": {
      "title": "Instructor of Surgery",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of surgery (one or more surgical specialties). Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Responsibilities may include research in a surgical clinical or educational subspecialty and teaching of medical students, research-rotation residents and lab personnel regarding laboratory policy and procedures. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop an individual training experience in research skills and teaching, while developing a career in an academic setting. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/163224": {
      "title": "Instructor Position - Division of Geriatric Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Geriatrics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Geriatrics in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in geriatric Medicine. Responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, fellows, older adults and their care partners; providing clinical care in the House Calls program, ambulatory care practice and/or in the hospital Acute Care for the Elderly (ACE) unit; participation in Geriatrics Workforce Enhancement Program (GWEP) activities; and courses, grant writing, manuscript writing, or other scholarship and research which will be determined through discussion with Division Chief and/or mentor. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to enhance their teaching skills and clinical abilities, advance their professional development as well as develop additional skills that are aligned with their career goals. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187357": {
      "title": "Instructor Position - Division of Hematology/Oncology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certified or eligible in hematology and/or oncology is required. Responsibilities may include developing expertise in research skills, including scholarship, clinical care related to research, and developing skills teaching medical students, residents and/or fellows. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop individual training experiences in research and/or teaching that will allow him/her to attain personal career objectives while developing a career in an academic setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177550": {
      "title": "Instructor Position - Division of Pulmonary, Allergy & Critical Care Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include developing expertise in research skills, including scholarship, clinical care related to research, and teaching medical students, residents and/or fellows. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to gain additional training in both clinical expertise and research."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183275": {
      "title": "Instructor Position - Renal Electrolyte and Hypertension Division",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of Nephrology. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board Certified or Board Eligible (ABIM) in Nephrology is required. Responsibilities may include the opportunity to care for patients at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), or the Graduate Dialysis Unit. There will also be opportunities to participate in the many educational activities of the Division, including teaching medical students, residents, and fellows. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop an individualized training experience in research, teaching, or patient care in preparation for the next stage of their career."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178848": {
      "title": "Instructor Position - Ultrasound Fellow",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hospital Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hospital Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/board eligible in general internal medicine or family medicine is required. Responsibilities may include nights and weekends at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania and Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, as well as limited weekend shifts at Good Shepherd Penn Partners Long Term Acute Care Hospital (LTACH). The successful applicant will have an opportunity for mentorship and structured career development within hospital medicine. Application and recruitment will be handled in concert with the Department of Emergency Medicine. This Instructor position in Hospital Medicine is a part of a unique non-ACGME fellowship with the Department of Emergency Medicine. The incumbent will be provided didactic and clinical training in ultrasound, while also working clinically as an attending physician on hospital medicine services. Additional opportunities for mentorship and structured career development within hospital medicine are also available. Application and recruitment is handled in concert with the Department of Emergency Medicine."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177140": {
      "title": "Instructor Position, Division of Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include developing expertise in research skills, including scholarship, clinical care related to research, and teaching medical students, residents and/or fellows. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to gain additional training in both clinical expertise and research."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176868": {
      "title": "Instructor Position, Division of Rheumatology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Rheumatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Rheumatology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of research: i) laboratory-based research that relates to general fields of autoimmunity, inflammation, musculoskeletal medicine, or rheumatology; ii) clinical epidemiology related to autoimmunity, musculoskeletal medicine, or rheumatology; or iii) health services research related to autoimmune diseases, musculoskeletal medicine, or rheumatology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Rheumatology. Responsibilities may include research under the mentorship of a senior investigator and clinical work within the Division of Rheumatology. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop independence in research through writing grants and peer-reviewed publications."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175886": {
      "title": "Instructor, Biostatistics",
      "description": "Posted: Oct 15, 2025 Deadline: Oct 15, 2027 Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology and Informatics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biostatistics and Epidemiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of statistics or biostatistics. Areas we are currently focusing on include, but are not limited to, imaging statistics, causal inference, and AI with applications within biostatistics. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Responsibilities may include leadership and collaboration in the development and application of advanced statistical methodology. The ability to establish oneself as a research leader in their area of specialization is required and developing a research portfolio through publication in leading journals and acquiring research funding to support this program are expected. Presentations at national and international scientific meetings are also required to demonstrate innovation and impact. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to collaborate with and, potentially, mentor students and postdoctoral researchers; and develop an independent research program with opportunities to write and submit articles to peer-reviewed publications as well as participate in writing grant applications."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187355": {
      "title": "Instructor/Hospitalist Position, Division of Hematology-Oncology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Instructor positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified/eligible in specialty if applicable. Responsibilities may include providing inpatient care and supervising both house staff and well-trained nurse practitioners. Ideal candidates will have experience as a practicing hospitalist as well as experience in hematology and/or oncology. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop further as a hospitalist during a time in their career when they will need to illustrate additional professional training. Selected candidates will also gain additional training through practicing advanced medicine in a complex and diverse patient population. Applicants should have excellent qualifications in education and clinical care."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193578": {
      "title": "Interventional Radiology - Academic Clinician - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Interventional Radiology. Preference will be given to candidates with extensive experience in lymphatic interventions. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. American Board of Radiology certified with CAQ and completion of fellowship training in Interventional Radiology or completion of a residency in Interventional Radiology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision and teaching of residents and fellows during procedures and conferences and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center. In addition, the candidate will prepare learning materials and lectures, teaching posters and presentations for national review. Clinical responsibilities may include performing minimally invasive image-guided interventional procedures as well as performing and/overseeing interventional studies and consultations with patients and referring physicians. These responsibilities will include a focus in lymphatic interventions, with 50% of clinical time devoted to lymphatics. The successful candidate will also participate in the Interventional Radiology off-hours on call program, including evening, night and weekend coverage. The IR division has an active outpatient clinic and consulting service as well as an inpatient admitting service. The IR Division at Penn has considerable depth of expertise, performing more than 15,000 procedures annually. More than half of them are therapeutic, covering every aspect of the field. Penn Interventional Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193580": {
      "title": "Interventional Radiology - Academic Clinician - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Interventional Radiology. Preference will be given to candidates with extensive experience in lymphatic interventions. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. American Board of Radiology certified with CAQ and completion of fellowship training in Interventional Radiology or completion of a residency in Interventional Radiology is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision and teaching of residents and fellows during procedures and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center. In addition, the candidate will prepare learning materials and lectures, teaching posters, and presentations for national review. Clinical responsibilities may include performing minimally invasive image-guided interventional procedures as well as performing and/overseeing interventional studies and consultations with patients and referring physicians. These responsibilities will include a focus on lymphatic interventions, with 50% of clinical time devoted to lymphatics. The successful candidate will also participate in the Interventional Radiology off-hours on-call program, including evening, night, and weekend coverage. The IR division has an active outpatient clinic and consulting service as well as an inpatient admitting service. The IR Division at Penn has considerable depth of expertise, performing more than 15,000 procedures annually. More than half of them are therapeutic, covering every aspect of the field. Penn Interventional Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193392": {
      "title": "Interventional Spine Medicine - Academic Clinician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of general musculoskeletal skills. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must have demonstrated excellent qualifications in clinical care. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible by the American Board of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation. Candidates should bring to this position expertise through special experiences or additional fellowship training in Interventional Spine, Pain Management or Musculoskeletal Medicine. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and mentoring of Penn medical students and residents as well as allied professionals. Clinical responsibilities may include working closely with other surgical and non-surgical teams to provide coordinated interdisciplinary care for patients as part of our Spine Center. Selected candidates must have excellent, well refined interpersonal skills and leadership abilities to effectively lead our interdisciplinary rehabilitation teams. Candidates should have strong clinical training, enthusiasm, and a commitment to furthering our clinical services and advancing our academic missions. As an academic faculty member, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to provide outstanding teaching and mentoring for Penn medical students and residents as well as allied professionals."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188103": {
      "title": "Lung Transplant Surgeon, Assistant Professor of Surgery",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include instruction of medical students and surgical residents. Clinical responsibilities may include lung transplant, adult cardiac or thoracic surgery, and all aspects of care for patients undergoing lung transplantation. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical and/or basic science research on topics in the field of lung transplantation. The successful candidate will support surgical aspects of the program’s clinical operations, academic initiatives, and strategic growth, working in close partnership with the Penn Transplant Institute and a multidisciplinary team of renowned transplant surgeons, pulmonologists, and support. The successful candidate will practice primarily in Philadelphia. They may also participate in other areas of either cardiac surgery or thoracic surgery as well as mechanical circulatory support and ECMO."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/157828": {
      "title": "Medical Dermatologist - Assistant Professor (Clinician-Educator)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Dermatology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Dermatology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician-educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board-certified or board-eligible in Dermatology. Teaching responsibilities may include an interest in academics and teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include participation in clinical outpatient and inpatient dermatology. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing a focused body of research in one or more of the following areas: autoimmune skin diseases, graft versus host disease, atopic dermatitis, psoriasis, cutaneous T cell lymphoma, wound healing, clinical epidemiology, cutaneous malignancy, or other related diseases.  The successful candidate will have prior research experience and have demonstrated evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship. Support and mentorship for research will be provided. Philadelphia is a historic city offering a unique blend of centuries-old architecture, vibrant culture and art, diverse lifestyle, outdoor activities, and an outstanding quality of life.  The Perelman School of Medicine is consistently rated as one of the top medical institutions in the United States, and the dermatology department has always been at the forefront of academic medicine since its founding in 1874. This position offers a competitive salary, generous benefits, and a highly stimulating professional career. Visit Benefits & Pay (upenn.edu) for information on the benefits available to faculty; additional benefits may be available to physicians."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171364": {
      "title": "Medical Director of Living Donor Liver Transplantation - Senior ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Gastroenterology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Gastroenterology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of the clinical, regulatory and administrative responsibilities surrounding living donation for liver transplant. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates should be board certified in Gastroenterology and Hepatology, and in Transplant Hepatology. Rank will commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include outpatient precepting of transplant hepatology fellows and internal medicine residents in primary hepatology clinics (variable frequency) as well as inpatient teaching service attending and/or consult service that includes direct supervision of transplant hepatology fellows, gastroenterology/hepatology fellows, internal medicine residents, interns and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include 6 ½ day clinical sessions per week including 2 sessions (1 day) outpatient endoscopy and 1-2 sessions dedicated to evaluation of potential living donor candidates and/or potential liver transplant recipients. Up to 12 weeks inpatient teaching service attending and/or consult service may be required. The Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology is a vibrant, highly interactive, and collaborative academic and clinical environment with about 76 faculty, 26 fellows, and more than 200 staff. The Division provides clinical care in programs dedicated to General Gastroenterology, IBD, Neurogastroenterology, Esophagus, Advanced Therapeutics, Hepatology, GI Genetics, Nutrition/small bowel and Women’s GI Health. The Medical Director of Living Donor Liver Transplantation will specifically oversee the operational, administrative and clinical responsibilities related to Living Donor Liver Transplant with goals of patient safety, efficiency and capacity maximization. The Medical Director will participate in all general as well as living donor-specific transplant hepatology-related clinical and administrative meetings. There will be an expectation of the ability of the selected candidate to provide management and/or leadership in the role. Rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195606": {
      "title": "Medical Director, Kidney Transplant Program - Academic Clinician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of the clinical, regulatory and administrative leadership of an adult kidney transplant program. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Board certification in Nephrology is required, and candidates must meet OPTN/UNOS criteria to serve as a primary kidney transplant physician. Teaching responsibilities may include instruction and supervision of nephrology and transplant nephrology fellows, internal medicine residents, and medical students in the inpatient transplant service, consult service, and outpatient transplant clinics. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include evaluation and management of kidney and kidney-pancreas transplant candidates and recipients, as well as living kidney donor candidates, in the outpatient setting, and attending on the inpatient kidney transplant service. The selected candidate will have experience working with advanced practice providers, transplant coordinators, and trainees. The Medical Director will oversee the clinical, operational, and regulatory responsibilities of the Kidney Transplant Program in partnership with the Surgical Director and Penn Transplant Institute leadership, with goals of patient safety, access to transplant, organ utilization, and program growth. Responsibilities include stewardship of waitlist management, selection committee processes, quality and performance improvement, and compliance with OPTN/UNOS, CMS, and SRTR requirements. The Medical Director will serve as an internal and external spokesperson for the program and participate in all transplant-related clinical and administrative meetings. The Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension Division is a highly collaborative academic and clinical environment with over 50 faculty and ACGME accredited general nephrology and transplant nephrology fellowships. The Division provides exceptional clinical care across general nephrology, dialysis, transplant nephrology as well as specialty areas such as glomerular disease, rare and inherited kidney disease, polycystic kidney disease, onconephrology, neuroendocrine tumor and hypertension. Penn performed the region's first kidney transplant in 1966, and the Penn Transplant Institute is the largest transplant center in the region. The ideal candidate will be an experienced transplant nephrologist with strong leadership skills who is committed to patient-centered care, equitable access to transplantation, and multidisciplinary collaboration. Rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169398": {
      "title": "Medical Director, Lung Transplant Program",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certification is required in Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include pulmonary and critical care fellows, house staff and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year and active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include consultation, evaluation, and management of outpatient and inpatient lung transplant candidates and recipients within the health system on a growing lung transplant service. The selected candidate will have experience working with advanced practice providers and trainees. The selected candidate will drive strategic growth, ensure clinical excellence, lead quality improvement, and support innovative research and education initiatives. The ideal candidate will be an experienced transplant pulmonologist with strong leadership skills committed to patient-centered care and multidisciplinary collaboration."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184498": {
      "title": "Multiple Myeloma, AC Track Faculty Position",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Hematology/Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Hematology-Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of multiple myeloma. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Board certified or board eligible in Medical Oncology or Hematology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching hematology/oncology fellows, residents, and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include care of patients with myeloma and amyloidosis, including autologous stem cell transplantation and CAR T cell therapy. Selected candidates will provide patient care in an outpatient setting and as an attending on the inpatient service at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP). Within the outpatient setting candidates will provide care to patients in collaboration with a multidisciplinary team of nurse practitioners, nurses, and transplant and cellular therapy coordinators. As an attending, candidates will provide care to patients on the hematologic malignancies service. Engagement in clinical investigation is a high priority in this position. Experience and/or advanced training in the conduct of clinical trials is preferred but not required. Participation in our weekly myeloma clinical trials meeting is required. It will also be expected that selected candidates participate in our weekly myeloma case conference as well as our weekly amyloidosis case conference."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176967": {
      "title": "Musculoskeletal Imaging - Academic Clinician - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. The ideal candidate should be American Board of Radiology certified or eligible with sub-specialty training in MSK Radiology. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision and teaching of residents and fellows during readouts and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical sub-specialties. The education of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. Clinical responsibilities may include providing clinical service in the usual clinical skill sets (PF, CT, MRI, arthrograms/joint aspirations). In addition, candidates are expected to be competent in diagnostic MSK US and image-guided tumor biopsies. The successful candidate will also participate in the Musculoskeletal Imaging off-hours on-call program, including evenings, nights, and weekend coverage. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center (PAVMC), as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176974": {
      "title": "Musculoskeletal Imaging - Academic Clinician - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision and teaching of residents and fellows during readouts and conferences and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical sub-specialties. The education of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. The successful candidate will be an accomplished educator and be expected to serve in an administrative, educational leadership role within the Musculoskeletal Imaging division. Clinical responsibilities may include providing clinical service in the usual clinical skill sets (PF, CT, MRI, arthrograms/joint aspirations). In addition, competence in diagnostic MSK US and image-guided tumor biopsies will be expected. The successful candidate will also participate in the Musculoskeletal Imaging off-hours on-call program, including evening, night, and weekend coverage. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center (PAVMC), as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184672": {
      "title": "Musculoskeletal Imaging - Clinician--Educator - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be certified by the American Board of Radiology, and completion of a musculoskeletal imaging fellowship is strongly recommended. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision and teaching of residents and fellows during readouts and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical sub-specialties. The education of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. The successful candidate will be an accomplished educator. Clinical responsibilities may include providing clinical service in the usual clinical skill sets (PF, CT, MRI, arthrograms/joint aspirations). In addition, competence in diagnostic MSK US and image-guided tumor biopsies will be expected. The successful candidate will also participate in the Musculoskeletal Imaging off-hours on-call program, including evening, night, and weekend coverage. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include leading the development of a focused body of research in a field within Musculoskeletal Imaging. The candidate will also be expected to serve as a mentor to junior faculty, providing strong guidance and support in the development of clinical or basic research careers. The ideal candidate will have a world-renowned reputation for innovative techniques, an established track record of scholarly activity and publications, and an impact within the field of Musculoskeletal Imaging. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP), Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), Pennsylvania Hospital (PAH), and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center (PAVMC), as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187610": {
      "title": "Neuroblastoma Developmental Therapeutics and Solid Tumor Program; Assistant Professor, Clinician Educator, Pediatric Oncology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics: Perelman School of Medicine - Pediatrics - Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Oncology in the Department of Pediatrics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of neuroblastoma and other pediatric solid malignancies. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree and be board-certified or board-eligible in pediatric hematology/oncology. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic and clinical instruction of medical students, residents, post-doctoral fellows, instructors, and/or clinical research assistants and educational liaison with advanced practice providers. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient and inpatient care focused on children, adolescents, and young adults with relapsed neuroblastoma and childhood solid tumors at CHOP and active involvement in fellowship training and mentoring. The ideal candidate will have experience in early phase clinical trials of precision medicine therapeutics including immunotherapies for children with relapsed/refractory or high-risk neuroblastoma and other solid malignancies. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include expanding translational and clinical research efforts in pediatric solid tumors with a focus on neuroblastoma.  Preferred applicants will have an established record of peer-reviewed scholarship and extramural grant funding.  The successful candidate is expected to be academically productive, collaborative, and able to expand our already robust research enterprise.  It is expected that > 50% independent research effort funding will be secured within three years of appointment."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195114": {
      "title": "Neuroradiology - Academic Clinician - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Neuroradiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be certified by the American Board of Radiology and be neuroradiology CAQ-eligible. Completion of a two-year neuroradiology fellowship is strongly recommended. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision, teaching residents and fellows during readouts and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical service to all referring clinicians, and expert clinical consultation to our partners in the departments of Emergency Medicine, Otorhinolaryngology: Head and Neck Surgery, Neurology, Neurosurgery, Psychiatry, and Ophthalmology. The successful candidate will also participate in the Neuroradiology off-hours on call program, including evening, night and weekend coverage. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195115": {
