and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195234": {
      "title": "Neuroradiology - Clinician--Educator - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of neuroradiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be certified by the American Board of Radiology and be CAQ-eligible in neuroradiology. Completion of a two-year neuroradiology fellowship is strongly recommended. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision, teaching residents and fellows during readouts and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical sub-specialties. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical service to all referring clinicians and expert clinical consultation to our partners in the departments of Emergency Medicine, Otorhinolaryngology: Head and Neck Surgery, Neurology, Neurosurgery, Psychiatry, and Ophthalmology. The successful candidate will also participate in the Neuroradiology off-hours on-call program, including evening, night, and weekend coverage. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing a focused body of research in a field within Neuroradiology. The successful candidate will have prior research experience, including evidence of training in research methodology and have demonstrated evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship. We will provide ample support and mentorship for research. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veteran Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195236": {
      "title": "Neuroradiology - Clinician-Educator - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of neuroradiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be certified by the American Board of Radiology and be CAQ-eligible in neuroradiology. Completion of a two-year neuroradiology fellowship is strongly recommended. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include daily clinical supervision, teaching residents and fellows during readouts and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. The successful candidate will be an accomplished educator and be expected to serve in an administrative, educational leadership role within the Neuroradiology division. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical service to all referring clinicians and expert clinical consultation to our partners in the departments of Emergency Medicine, Otorhinolaryngology: Head and Neck Surgery, Neurology, Neurosurgery, Psychiatry, and Ophthalmology. The successful candidate will also participate in the Neuroradiology off-hours on-call program, including evening, night, and weekend coverage. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include leading the development of a focused body of research in a field within Neuroradiology. The candidate will also be expected to mentor junior faculty, providing strong guidance and support as they develop clinical or basic research careers. The ideal candidate will have a world-renowned reputation for innovative techniques and have an impact within the field of Neuroradiology. The clinician-educator track requires evidence of scholarship. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, Philadelphia Veteran Affairs Medical Center, and affiliated outpatient imaging centers in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189350": {
      "title": "Non-Invasive/Consultative Cardiologist at Penn Presbyterian Medicine Center",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Cardiovascular Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Cardiovascular Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible in cardiovascular disease. Teaching responsibilities may include the education of medical students, residents, cardiovascular fellows and advanced practice providers. Selected candidates will be expected to contribute to the educational mission of the organization and contribute no less than 100 teaching credits annually. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient and inpatient cardiovascular care, as well as the interpretation and performance of non-invasive cardiac testing. The Division serves a large, well-established referral base across the Philadelphia region and Southern New Jersey, with multiple outpatient practice locations and a tertiary inpatient referral center at Penn Presbyterian Medicine Center (PPMC). The physician will primarily practice at one or two outpatient clinic locations, providing comprehensive consultative and longitudinal cardiovascular care while interpreting non-invasive cardiac studies, including echocardiography and stress testing. In addition, the position includes participation in the inpatient cardiology service on a rotating basis alongside other faculty members. The successful candidate will also serve as the Medical Director of the PPMC Outpatient (PHI3) Cardiology Clinic. In this leadership role, the physician will partner with clinical and administrative teams to optimize patient access, enhance quality and operational performance, support physician and staff engagement, and foster continued growth of the practice while maintaining Penn Medicine's commitment to exceptional patient-centered care. The selected candidate will join a robust well-established Division of Cardiology comprising more than 40 full-time cardiologists at Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC), providing comprehensive cardiovascular and vascular care within the Penn Medicine health system. Located in the heart of Philadelphia, Penn Medicine offers a uniquely dynamic environment that blends world-class academic medicine with the energy of a major metropolitan center. Its strategic position provides seamlee access to New jersey, New York, Maryland, and Washington D.C., placing faculty at the center of one of the most densely networked healthcare and research corridors in the country. The region supports robust collaboration, diverse populations, and extensive professional opportunites across clinical care, research, education, and leadership-making it an exceptionally attractive destination for those seeking both career advancement abd a vibrant, accessible place to live and work."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186037": {
      "title": "Nuclear Medicine Imaging and Therapy - Academic Clinician - Junior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be board-eligible or have specialty certification in nuclear medicine, either current American Board of Nuclear Medicine certification or a CAQ in nuclear radiology from the American Board of Radiology, and have completed a nuclear medicine or nuclear radiology ACGME-approved training program. Teaching responsibilities may include providing daily clinical nuclear medicine services, as well as supervising and teaching residents and fellows during procedures and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical sub-specialties. Candidates will be expected to lecture at assigned resident didactic conferences and nuclear radiology fellow lecture series. Attendance and teaching at case conferences as well as participation in journal club meetings is required. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. Clinical responsibilities may include performing and interpreting nuclear medicine stress tests, EKGs, evaluating and treating patients with therapeutic radio-pharmaceuticals and general nuclear medicine studies. Candidates must have extensive PET/CT experience. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers located in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186040": {
      "title": "Nuclear Medicine Imaging and Therapy - Academic Clinician - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must have specialty certification in nuclear medicine, either current American Board of Nuclear Medicine certification or a CAQ in nuclear radiology from the American Board of Radiology, and have completed a nuclear medicine or nuclear radiology ACGME-approved training program. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Position requires a minimum of 5 years of experience. Teaching responsibilities may include providing daily clinical nuclear medicine services, supervising and teaching residents and fellows during procedures and conferences, and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical sub-specialties. Candidates will be expected to lecture at assigned resident didactic conferences and nuclear radiology fellow lecture series. Attendance and teaching at case conferences, as well as participation in journal club meetings, is required. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. An ability to lead clinical excellence is an integral feature of the Academic Clinician track. Clinical responsibilities may include performing and interpreting nuclear medicine stress tests and EKGs, as well as evaluating and treating patients with therapeutic radiopharmaceuticals and general nuclear medicine studies. Candidates must have extensive PET/CT experience. The successful candidate will be expected to serve in a clinical administration leadership role within the Nuclear Medicine Imaging and Therapy Division. Penn Radiology provides clinical services for the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, Pennsylvania Hospital, and the Philadelphia Veterans Affairs Medical Center, as well as affiliated outpatient imaging centers located in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173262": {
      "title": "Obstetrical Anesthesiologist – Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology, the equivalent, or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Fellowship training in obstetric anesthesiology and/or extensive experience providing obstetric anesthesia care (ideally three years ) is strongly preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include the instruction of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the operating rooms of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and the Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC) as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of obstetrical anesthesia care at HUP as well as the provision of anesthesia care in the operating rooms and non-operating room anesthesia procedural areas at HUP, PPMC, Penn Medicine University City, and other locations staffed by the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care. Additional responsibilities may include serving on Department committees and serving in administrative leadership positions, as appropriate. The academic clinician track emphasizes clinical and teaching excellence. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE and individuals from all backgrounds are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173280": {
      "title": "Obstetrical Anesthesiologist – Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology, the equivalent, or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. Fellowship training in obstetric anesthesiology and/or extensive experience providing obstetric anesthesia care (ideally three years ) is strongly preferred. Applicants in mid-career are encouraged to apply. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include the instruction of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the operating rooms of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and the Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC) as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of obstetrical anesthesia care at HUP as well as the provision of anesthesia care in the operating rooms and non-operating room anesthesia procedural areas at HUP, PPMC, Penn Medicine University City, and other locations staffed by the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care. Additional responsibilities may include serving on Department committees and serving in administrative leadership positions, as appropriate. The academic clinician track emphasizes clinical and teaching excellence. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE and individuals from all backgrounds are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180519": {
      "title": "Orthopaedic Oncology Surgeon",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Orthopaedic Oncology, with additional sub specialization in Orthopaedic Surgery preferred. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Must be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Orthopaedic Surgery. Fellowship training in Orthopaedic Oncology is required. Teaching responsibilities may include resident and medical school teaching and education in Orthopaedic Oncology. Clinical responsibilities may include an Orthopaedic Oncology practice in the Health System Hospitals and on call responsibilities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/165576": {
      "title": "Orthopaedic Surgery - Adult Reconstruction Surgery - Assistant Professor AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Orthopaedic Adult Reconstruction. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Must be Board Certified or Board Eligible and Fellowship trained in Adult Reconstruction is required. Teaching responsibilities may include resident, medical school teaching and fellow education in Adult Reconstruction Surgery. Clinical responsibilities may include an Adult Reconstruction practice at PPMC and UPHS satellite locations and on call responsibilities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195345": {
      "title": "Orthopaedic Surgery - Orthoplastics Hand Surgery - Assistant Professor, AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Orthopaedic Hand and Reconstructive Microsurgery Surgery. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Must be board eligible/board certified in Orthopaedic Surgery or Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery. Fellowship trained in Reconstructive Microvascular Surgery is strongly preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include medical school teaching and resident and fellow education in Hand and reconstructive orthoplastics microsurgery. Clinical responsibilities may include Hand and Reconstructive Microvascular Surgery practice at Pennsylvania Hospital and affiliated Penn Medicine facilities on call responsibilities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193818": {
      "title": "Orthopaedic Surgery Adult Recon Surgeon @ PAH - AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Adult Reconstruction. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Orthopedic Surgery or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of medical students, fellows, and orthopedic surgery residents. Clinical responsibilities may include building a practice in adult reconstruction at Pennsylvania hospital, with additional duties in orthopedic surgery depending on candidate training and may include on call responsibilities. Applicants who have completed an accredited adult reconstruction fellowship are preferred. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Orthopedic Surgery."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193825": {
