    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193824": {
      "title": "Orthopaedic Surgery Sports Medicine @ PPMC - AC Track, Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Sports Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Orthopedic Surgery or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of medical students, fellows, and orthopedic surgery residents. Clinical responsibilities may include building a practice in sports medicine at Presbyterian Medical Center, with additional duties in orthopedic surgery depending on candidate training and may include on call responsibilities. Applicants who have completed an accredited sports medicine fellowship are preferred. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Orthopedic Surgery."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193819": {
      "title": "Orthopaedic Surgery Sports Medicine @ PPMC - AC Track, Assoc/Full Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Sports Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Orthopedic Surgery or eligible for such certification. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of medical students, fellows, and orthopedic surgery residents. Clinical responsibilities may include building a practice in sports medicine at Presbyterian Medical Center with additional duties in orthopedic surgery depending on candidate training and may include on call responsibilities. Applicants who have completed an accredited sports medicine fellowship are preferred. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Orthopedic Surgery."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/165584": {
      "title": "Orthopaedic Surgery-Adult Reconstruction Surgery - Associate/Full Professor-AC Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of of Adult Reconstruction/Joint Surgery. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. Must be Board Certified or Board Eligible and Fellowship trained in Adult Reconstruction is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include resident, medical school teaching and fellow education in Adult Reconstruction. Clinical responsibilities may include an adult reconstruction practice at Presbyterian Medical Center & UPHS satellite Hospitals and on call responsibilities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192109": {
      "title": "PAH Faculty Physician - Assistant Professor AC track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Family Medicine and Community Health Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Family Medicine and Community Health at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be Board Certified in Family Medicine. Fellowship training or a Certificate of Added Qualifications (CAQ) is not required. Applicant qualifications include having a commitment to comprehensive Family Medicine across the lifespan, enthusiasm for teaching residents and students, and commitment to equitable, patient-centered care. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and supervision of Family Medicine residents and medical students in the outpatient setting. Participation in residency and medical student education. Opportunities for curricular leadership as your career progresses. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient Family Medicine, providing care to a diverse patient population of all ages. The practice offers a broad scope of services, including gender-affirming care, office-based procedures, addiction medicine services, pediatric care and sports medicine. Additional clinical opportunities for interested candidates might include: Dedicated prenatal care sessions at an FQHC or within the Family Medicine practice. Inpatient adult medicine on the Family Medicine teaching service at Penn Presbyterian Medical Center. Teaching and supervision in ambulatory, maternity, and inpatient settings. Clinical care at community partner sites such as West Philadelphia High School and FQHCs. This full-time faculty position is based at the department’s center city practice on the campus of Pennsylvania Hospital. This practice provides comprehensive primary care to patients of all ages as well as gynecologic and other procedural care, care for individuals with opiate use disorder and LGBTQ+ oriented primary care services. This position involves medical student teaching and could include inpatient hospital medicine with our resident teaching service if desired by the candidate. Scholarship: Candidates on the Academic Clinician track are not required to engage in research or scholarship; however, scholarly activity is encouraged and supported."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189374": {
      "title": "Pediatric Foot & Ankle Surgeon - Senior Rank - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek a candidate for an Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of a clinical focus in foot and ankle pathology. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D/Ph.D or equivalent degree. Candidate must demonstrate excellent qualifications and clinical care and must be board certified/board eligible by the American Board of Orthopaedic Surgery. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services to patients. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or othopaedic basic science research and will be dependent on the candidate's interests and independent support. Evidence of scholarship is required for the Clinician Educator track. Mid-career applicants are encouraged. Rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189371": {
      "title": "Pediatric Foot & Ankle Surgeon-Assistant Professor - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek a candidate for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of foot and ankle pathology.  Applicants must have an M.D or M.D/Ph.D or equivalent degree. Candidate must demonstrate excellent qualifications and clinical care and must be board certified or eligible by the American Board of Orthopaedic Surgery. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of medical students, residents and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or orthopaedic basic science research and will be dependent on the candidate's interests and independent support."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187855": {
      "title": "Pediatric Gastrointestinal/Liver Pathologist – Assistant Professor - Clinician Educator Track - Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of gastrointestinal and liver pathology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. American Board of Pathology certification is required, AP-only or AP/CP. American Board of Pathology certification or eligibility in Pediatric Pathology is preferred. Eligibility for licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include participation in the GI/Liver pathology service. Coverage of additional pathology subspecialties and night/weekend call will also be considered. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include development of an independent or highly collaborative research program (as PI, Co-PI, or Co-I) in the area of GI/liver pathology. The position will be based within the Division of Anatomic Pathology at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187853": {
      "title": "Pediatric Gastrointestinal/Liver Pathologist – Associate Professor - Clinician Educator Track - Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of gastrointestinal and liver pathology. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. American Board of Pathology certification is required, AP-only or AP/CP. American Board of Pathology certification or eligibility in Pediatric Pathology is preferred. Eligibility for licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and mentoring of medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include participation in the GI/Liver pathology service. Coverage of additional pathology subspecialties and night/weekend call will also be considered. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include development of an independent or highly collaborative research program (as PI, Co-PI or Co-I) in the area of GI/liver pathology. Applicants who are mid-career are encouraged to apply. The position will be based within the Division of Anatomic Pathology at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Applicants may be involved in administrative and leadership responsibilities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189378": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neuromuscular Orthopaedic Surgeon - Assistant Professor - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of neuromuscular disorders.  Applicants must have an M.D, M.D/Ph.D, or equivalent degree. Candidate must demonstrate excellent qualifications and clinical care and must be board certified or eligible by the American Board of Orthopaedic Surgery. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. The candidate will be expected to participate in CHOP's new state of the art motion analysis center. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or basic science research and will be dependent on the candidate's interests and independent support."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189380": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neuromuscular Orthopaedic Surgeon - Senior Rank - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of neuromuscular disorders is preferred. Applicants must have an M.D, M.D/Ph.D, or equivalent degree. Candidate must demonstrate excellent qualifications and clinical care and must be board certified or eligible by the American Board of Orthopaedic Surgery. Teaching responsibilities may include participation in the clinical education of medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outpatient and inpatient consultative services. The candidate will be expected to participate in CHOP's new state of the art motion analysis center. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical or basic science research and will be dependent on the candidate's interests and independent support. Evidence of scholarship is required for the Clinician Educator track. Mid-career applicants are encouraged. Rank will be commensurate with experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171394": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neuroradiologist at CHOP - Clinician Educator - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of clinical pediatric neuroradiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. The applicant will be American Board of Radiology (ABR) eligible and have completed a formal fellowship in Pediatric Neuroradiology or equivalent training or experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching radiology residents and pediatric neuroradiology, neuroradiology, and pediatric radiology fellows during image interpretation sessions and departmental conferences. Successful candidates will also participate in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialists. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. In addition, the candidate will be expected to prepare learning materials and presentations for national and international meetings. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical coverage in the areas of Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), and MEG (optional). The candidate will also be assigned to coverage on evenings, nights, and weekends. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include leading the development of a focused body of research in the field of Pediatric Neuroradiology. The successful candidate will have prior research experience, including evidence of training in research methodology and have demonstrated evidence of peer reviewed scholarship. Ample support and mentorship for research will be provided. The Department of Radiology at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia consists of over 500 dedicated medical staff specializing in pediatric radiology. Our team provides clinical services across various divisions, including Interventional Radiology, Nuclear Medicine, Neuroradiology, and Body Imaging (with subspecialties in areas like musculoskeletal imaging, emergency radiology, and oncologic imaging). Annually, our Diagnostic Radiology Department handles more than 250,000 cases. We actively engage in cutting-edge research using technologies such as Contrast-Enhanced Ultrasound (CEUS), 3T MR imaging, PET/CT, and Magnetoencephalography. Additionally, our state-of-the-art translational research building supports research across radiology modalities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171396": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neuroradiologist at CHOP - Clinician Educator - Senior Ranks",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of clinical pediatric neuroradiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. The applicant will be American Board of Radiology (ABR) eligible and have completed a formal fellowship in Pediatric Neuroradiology or equivalent training or experience. Applicants in mid-career with established records and 5 or more years of experience are encouraged to apply. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching radiology residents and pediatric neuroradiology, neuroradiology, and pediatric radiology fellows during image interpretation sessions and departmental conferences, also participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialists. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. In addition, the candidate will be expected to prepare learning materials and presentations for national and international meetings. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical coverage in the areas of Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), and MEG (optional). The candidate will also be assigned to coverage on evenings, nights, and weekends. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include leading the development of a focused body of research in the field Pediatric Neuroradiology. The successful candidate will also be expected to mentor junior faculty, providing strong guidance and support in developing clinical or basic research careers. The ideal candidate will have a world-renowned reputation for innovative techniques and have an impact within the field of Pediatric Neuroradiology. Evidence of scholarship is required in the clinician-educator track. The Department of Radiology at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia consists of over 500 dedicated medical staff specializing in pediatric radiology. Our team provides clinical services across various divisions, including Interventional Radiology, Nuclear Medicine, Neuroradiology, and Body Imaging (with subspecialties in areas like musculoskeletal imaging, emergency radiology, and oncologic imaging). Annually, our Diagnostic Radiology Department handles more than 250,000 cases. We actively engage in cutting-edge research using technologies such as Contrast-Enhanced Ultrasound (CEUS), 3T MR imaging, PET/CT, and Magnetoencephalography. Additionally, our state-of-the-art translational research building supports research across radiology modalities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171091": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neuroradiologist at CHOP – Academic Clinician - Senior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of clinical pediatric neuroradiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Must be ABR board-certified or ABR eligible in Diagnostic Radiology. Completion of a formal fellowship in Pediatric Neuroradiology or demonstration of equivalent training or experience is required. Fellowship training in Pediatric Radiology or equivalent experience is considered a plus. Candidates should be Radiologists or Neuroradiologist with added qualifications in Pediatric Neuroradiology. Mid-career applicants with an established record and 5 or more years of experience are strongly encouraged to apply. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents and fellows during readouts and conferences and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. In addition, the candidate will prepare learning materials and lectures, teaching posters and presentations for national review. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical coverage in the areas of Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), MEG (optional), and coverage at the Specialty Centers when necessary. The candidate will also be assigned to in house coverage on evenings, nights and weekends."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171090": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neuroradiologist at CHOP – Academic Clinician – Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of clinical pediatric neuroradiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Must be ABR board-certified or ABR eligible in Diagnostic Radiology and have completed a formal fellowship in Pediatric Neuroradiology or equivalent training or experience. Fellowship training in Pediatric Radiology or demonstrated equivalent experience is considered a plus. Candidates should be Radiologists or Neuroradiologist with added qualifications in Pediatric Neuroradiology. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents and fellows during readouts and conferences and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. In addition, the candidate will prepare learning materials and lectures, teaching posters and presentations for national review. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical coverage in the areas of Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), MEG (optional), and coverage at the Specialty Centers when necessary. The candidate will also be assigned to in house coverage on evenings, nights and weekends."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183119": {
      "title": "Pediatric Ophthalmologist - Assistant Professor - Academic Clinician Track (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching pediatric ophthalmology fellows, ophthalmology and pediatric residents, and medical students. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical and surgical activity at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP) in outpatient and inpatient settings, and at affiliated hospitals. The clinical practice will focus on medical and surgical management of newborn, pediatric, and adolescent patients and will include on-call responsibilities. Clinical practice will also include outpatient clinics and outpatient surgery at CHOP Ambulatory Specialty Care Centers and Ambulatory Surgery Centers in the CHOP Primary and Secondary Region – specifically sites in and around New Jersey, as well as the Primary CHOP hospital site and possibly sites in Pennsylvania. Fellowship training in Pediatric Ophthalmology is required."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175487": {
      "title": "Pediatric Ophthalmologist - Associate Professor - Academic Clinician Track (CHOP)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Fellowship training in Pediatric Ophthalmology and Glaucoma and/or 5+ years of clinical experience treating complex pediatric glaucoma is preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching pediatric ophthalmology fellows, ophthalmology and pediatric residents, and medical students. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical and surgical activity at the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP) in outpatient and inpatient settings. The clinical practice will focus on medical and surgical management of newborn, pediatric, and adolescent patients and will include extended evening hours and/or weekend sessions and on-call responsibilities. Clinical practice will also include outpatient clinics and outpatient surgery at CHOP Ambulatory Specialty Centers and Ambulatory Surgery Centers in the CHOP Ambulatory Specialty Care Centers and Ambulatory Surgery Centers in the CHOP Primary and Secondary Region, as well as the primary CHOP hospital site. Responsibilities may include evening/weekend on call assignments."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189366": {
      "title": "Pediatric Orthopaedic Hand Surgeon - Assistant Professor - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of hand surgery, with a focus on microsurgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Orthopedic Surgery or eligible for such certification. Completion of an accredited hand fellowship is required. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of medical students, orthopedic surgery residents, and hand fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include building a practice in hand surgery, with additional duties in orthopedic surgery depending on candidate training. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical and/or basic science investigations in the field of orthopedic surgery and, specifically, hand surgery. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Orthopedic Surgery."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158460": {
      "title": "Pediatric Orthopaedic Hand Surgeon - Associate Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pediatric hand and upper extremity surgery.  Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Orthopedic Surgery or eligible for such certification. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of medical students, orthopaedic surgery residents, pediatric orthopaedic surgery fellows, and hand surgery fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include building a practice in pediatric hand surgery, with additional duties in orthopedic surgery depending on candidate training. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical and/or basic science investigations in the field of orthopaedic surgery and, specifically, hand surgery. Completion of an accredited hand surgery fellowship is required. Preference will be given to candidates that have additional fellowship training in pediatric hand surgery. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189367": {
      "title": "Pediatric Orthopaedic Hand Surgeon - Associate Professor - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of hand surgery, with a focus on microsurgery. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. They must also be certified by the American Board of Orthopedic Surgery or eligible for such certification. Completion of an accredited hand fellowship is required. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical and didactic instruction of medical students, orthopedic surgery residents, and hand fellows. Clinical responsibilities may include building a practice in hand surgery, with additional duties in orthopedic surgery depending on candidate training. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include clinical and/or basic science investigations in the field of orthopedic surgery and, specifically, hand surgery. The faculty appointment will be in the Department of Orthopedic Surgery. Applicants in mid-career are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171082": {
      "title": "Pediatric Radiologist at CHOP - Academic Clinician - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Body Imaging with a focus on Pediatric Diagnostic Radiology. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. American Board of Radiology (ABR) eligibility and completion of fellowship training in pediatric radiology or equivalent is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching of medical students and will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Clinical responsibilities may include coverage in the areas of Ultrasound (US), Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), Fluoroscopy, Inpatient Reading, Outpatient Reading, and coverage at the Specialty Centers when necessary. The candidate may also be assigned to in house coverage on evenings, nights and weekends. He/she will also teach residents and fellows during readouts and conferences and participate in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171449": {
      "title": "Pediatric Radiologist at CHOP - Clinician Educator - Junior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Body Imaging with a focus on Pediatric Diagnostic Radiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Completion of fellowship training in pediatric radiology or equivalent is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents and fellows during readouts and conferences and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. In addition, the candidate will prepare case-based and other learning materials and lectures, as well as teaching posters and presentations for national review. Clinical responsibilities may include coverage in the areas of Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), and other modalities such as Ultrasound (US), Fluoroscopy, and Inpatient/Outpatient Reading, as appropriate to the candidate’s experience. Optional coverage in Magnetoencephalography (MEG) and at Specialty Centers may also be required. The candidate will also participate in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties and teach residents and fellows during readouts and conferences. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing a focused body of clinical or basic research within the candidate’s area of expertise. This may involve clinical and translational studies, investigations into novel imaging approaches, or research into operational aspects of imaging and diagnosis within the health care system. The successful candidate will have prior research experience, with training at least equivalent to a clinical research certificate program or a mentored research experience during training and will have demonstrated evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship. Ample support and mentorship for research will be provided. The Department of Radiology at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia consists of over 500 dedicated medical staff specializing in pediatric radiology. Our team provides clinical services across various divisions, including Interventional Radiology, Nuclear Medicine, Neuroradiology, and Body Imaging (with subspecialties in areas like musculoskeletal imaging, emergency radiology, and oncologic imaging). Annually, our Diagnostic Radiology Department handles more than 250,000 cases. We actively engage in cutting-edge research using technologies such as Contrast-Enhanced Ultrasound (CEUS), 3T MR imaging, PET/CT, and Magnetoencephalography. Additionally, our state-of-the-art translational research building supports research across radiology modalities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171452": {
      "title": "Pediatric Radiologist at CHOP - Clinician Educator - Senior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure clinician educator track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Body Imaging with a focus on Pediatric Diagnostic Radiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Completion of fellowship training in pediatric radiology or equivalent is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching residents and fellows during readouts and conferences and participating in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties. Teaching of medical students will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. In addition, the candidate will prepare case-based and other learning materials and lectures, as well as teaching posters and presentations for national and international meetings. Clinical responsibilities may include coverage in the areas of Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), and other modalities such as Ultrasound (US), Fluoroscopy, and Inpatient/Outpatient Reading, as appropriate to the candidate’s experience. Optional coverage in Magnetoencephalography (MEG) and at Specialty Centers may also be required. The candidate will also participate in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties and teach residents and fellows during readouts and conferences. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include leading a focused body of research within the candidate’s area of expertise. This may include clinical and translational studies of novel imaging approaches in pediatric populations, evaluation of the impact of imaging on the diagnosis of diseases in children, or research into operational aspects of pediatric imaging and clinical diagnosis within the health care system. The successful candidate will have prior research experience and have demonstrated evidence of peer-reviewed scholarship. Ample support and mentorship for research will be provided. Applicants in mid-career with established records and 5 or more years of experience are encouraged to apply. The Department of Radiology at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia consists of over 500 dedicated medical staff specializing in pediatric radiology. Our team provides clinical services across various divisions, including Interventional Radiology, Nuclear Medicine, Neuroradiology, and Body Imaging (with subspecialties in areas like musculoskeletal imaging, emergency radiology, and oncologic imaging). Annually, our Diagnostic Radiology Department handles more than 250,000 cases. We actively engage in cutting-edge research using technologies such as Contrast-Enhanced Ultrasound (CEUS), 3T MR imaging, PET/CT, and Magnetoencephalography. Additionally, our state-of-the-art translational research building supports research across radiology modalities."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/171081": {
      "title": "Pediatric Radiologist at CHOP – Academic Clinician - Senior Rank",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Radiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Body Imaging with a focus on Pediatric Diagnostic Radiology. Applicants must have an M.D. degree. American Board of Radiology (ABR) eligibility and completion of fellowship training in pediatric radiology or equivalent is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching of medical students and will be limited to those rotating through the Department of Radiology at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical coverage in the areas of Ultrasound (US), Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), Fluoroscopy, Inpatient Reading, Outpatient Reading, and coverage at the Specialty Centers when necessary. The candidate may also be assigned to in house coverage on evenings, nights and weekends. He/she will also teach residents and fellows during readouts and conferences and participate in interdisciplinary conferences with clinical subspecialties."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192106": {
      "title": "Penn Medicine University City Faculty Physician - Assistant Professor AC track",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Family Medicine and Community Health Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Family Medicine and Community Health at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Family Medicine across the lifespan. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Applicants must be Board Certified in Family Medicine. Fellowship training or a Certificate of Added Qualifications (CAQ) is not required. Applicant qualifications include having a commitment to comprehensive Family Medicine across the lifespan, enthusiasm for teaching residents and students, and commitment to equitable, patient-centered care. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and supervision of Family Medicine residents and medical students in the outpatient setting, clinical precepting and mentorship of learners, participation in residency and medical student education, and contribution to curriculum development and educational initiatives. Participation in departmental educational activities. Clinical responsibilities may include outpatient Family Medicine, providing care to a diverse patient population of all ages. The practice offers a broad scope of services, including gender-affirming care, office-based procedures, addiction medicine services, and sports medicine. Additional clinical opportunities for interested candidates might include: Dedicated prenatal care sessions at an FQHC or within the Family Medicine practice. Inpatient adult medicine on the Family Medicine teaching service at Penn Presbyterian Medical Center. Teaching and supervision in ambulatory, maternity, and inpatient settings. Residency program leadership opportunities for candidates with experience in GME, particularly in supporting ILPs and/or creating inclusive learning environments. This full-time faculty position is based at the department’s primary residency practice site and offers the opportunity to provide comprehensive, relationship-centered care to patients across the lifespan within a thriving academic Family Medicine practice. The successful candidate will join a collaborative team dedicated to patient care, resident education, and community engagement. Scholarship: Candidates on the Academic Clinician track are not required to engage in research or scholarship; however, scholarly activity is encouraged and supported."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193393": {
      "title": "Physiatrist - General Rehabilitation - Academic Clinician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation with a focus on General Rehabilitation. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree.  Applicants must have demonstrated excellent qualifications in clinical care. Applicants must be Board Certified or Board Eligible by the American Board of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching and mentoring of Penn medical students and residents as well as allied professionals. Clinical responsibilities may include working closely with other surgical and non-surgical teams to provide the highest level of interdisciplinary care to a wide range of patients. This role will include attending physician for a comprehensive integrated inpatient service, consult service and outpatient programs. Applicants must possess broad clinical skills in managing outpatients with spine and musculoskeletal disorders. Selected candidates must have excellent, well refined interpersonal skills and leadership abilities to effectively lead our interdisciplinary rehabilitation teams. Candidates should have strong clinical training, enthusiasm, and a commitment to furthering our clinical services and advancing our academic missions. As an academic faculty member, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to provide outstanding teaching and mentoring for Penn medical students and residents as well as allied professionals."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179549": {
      "title": "Physician Co-Chief, Division of Community Care and Wellness, Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP), Academic Clinician track, Associate Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of strategic planning, program development and evaluation, leadership development, and mentoring. Applicants must have outstanding qualifications in clinical care and education. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Board certified or board eligible in Child and Adolescent Psychiatry. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, and fellows in psychiatry, psychology, social work, and nursing. Interprofessional training and educating the next generation of child mental health professionals and leaders is a priority for the Division. Clinical responsibilities may include assessment and treatment services to children and families, in inpatient and outpatient settings. Experience providing Mental Health services in community-based settings is strongly preferred. We are seeking candidates whose reputation for excellence is evidenced by meaningful impact within their area of expertise. The Division of Community Care and Wellness is a rapidly growing division dedicated to promoting equity in access to and delivery of evidence-based behavioral health services and advancing innovations in health care. The division supports numerous initiatives including integrated services in primary care and school-based services to improve access to behavioral health care. The successful candidate must demonstrate the ability to collaborate and partner effectively with psychiatry and psychology faculty and clinicians across multiple disciplines. The position requires the ability to forge strategic partnerships with community-based agencies, policy leaders at a local and state level, and faculty and administrators at CHOP and the University of Pennsylvania. The Physician Chief reports to the Chair of the Department of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences and works closely with the other Division Chiefs, the Vice Chair for Administration, and Associate Chairs. Division Chiefs are appointed faculty in the Department of Psychiatry in Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192388": {
      "title": "Professor (Tenure Track)-Department of Ophthalmology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Ophthalmology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Ophthalmology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a full-time Professor position in the Tenure Track. This position is intended for individuals with a strong commitment to independent research, with a particular focus on the mechanisms of ocular surface homeostasis and chronic inflammatory disease. Applicants must have an M.D and/or Ph.D or equivalent degree. Position Overview The successful candidate will have developed an innovative, NIH-funded research program on mechanisms of dry eye including inflammation. They will have both wet lab and clinical components to their research. Teaching responsibilities may include Mentor trainees, including fellows and graduate students. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include: • Establish and sustain an independent, high-impact research program in ophthalmology. • Secure extramural funding from federal agencies (e.g., NIH), foundations, and industry. • Collaborate with dry eye researchers in the Department and inflammation researchers at the University • Publish findings in high-impact peer-reviewed journals and present at national and international conferences. • Mentor trainees, including fellows and graduate students. Research Environment The Department of Ophthalmology provides a highly collaborative and interdisciplinary environment, with access to rich clinical data resources and collaborative eye research laboratories. The successful candidate will have opportunities to engage with leading programs in translational science and training of early career scientists. Faculty Track This is a tenure track position with a primary emphasis on research. Teaching responsibilities are limited, and no clinical duties are required. • Curriculum vitae • Cover letter describing research interests and career goals • Statement of research accomplishments and future plans • Names of three references"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191953": {
      "title": "Professor in Addiction Psychiatry",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position in the tenure track. Expertise is required in the specific area of mechanisms underpinning substance use and the treatment of substance use and misuse. Applicants with experience in novel therapeutics (e.g., psychedelics, incretin mimetics) in the treatment of substance use disorders are encouraged to apply. Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D degree. Board certification in Psychiatry is required. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching medical students, psychiatry residents, and postdoctoral fellows, as well as lecture opportunities within the department. Clinical responsibilities may include clinical evaluation and provision of treatment for adults with substance use disorders. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative and independent research programs related to the understanding and treatment of substance use disorders. Scholarship includes developing and maintaining a program of federally funded research."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/172628": {
      "title": "Professor of Clinical Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Emergency Medicine Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Emergency Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of Emergency Medicine. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. ABEM certified or board eligible is required. Teaching responsibilities may include bedside clinical teaching of emergency medicine residents and students. Additional teaching responsibilities include lectures, journal clubs, case conferences, simulation teaching, small group discussions, and others. Enthusiasm and dedication to educating our residents and students are highly valued in our department. Clinical responsibilities may include providing outstanding clinical care to emergency department patients in one or more of our three city hospitals: Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. Patients seen in our EDs include high acuity, complex patients, as well as patients with less acute illnesses and injuries. Penn Presbyterian Medical Center is a Level 1 Trauma Center. Mid-career faculty with local and/or national recognition in their area of interest/expertise are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193001": {
      "title": "Psychologist & Clinical Director, Perinatal Psychosocial, Center for Fetal Diagnosis & Treatment - Academic Clinician Track - CHOP",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for an Assistant or Associate Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. The selected candidate will also serve as the Clinical Director/Psychologist, Perinatal Psychosocial in the Center for Fetal Diagnoses and Treatment. Expertise is required in the specific area of the provision of maternal mental health, perinatal psychology and consultation-liaison psychology services, as well as evidence-based psychological assessment and intervention for families facing complex fetal diagnoses and high-risk pregnancies. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree and must be licensed or eligible for license, as a Psychologist in the State of Pennsylvania. Full Pennsylvania licensed is required prior to appointment. Academic rank will be commensurate with experience. Preference will be given to candidates who have experience leading multidisplinary psychosocial programs, providing supervision and mentorship to psychologists and trainees, collaborating with physicians, nurses, social workers, and advances practice providers, and developing innovative models of integrated behavioral healthcare. Experience with program development, quality improvement, and academic scholarship is preferred. Teaching responsibilities may include high-quality clinical education, supervision, and mentorship to psychology interns, postdoctoral fellows, psychiatry residents, medical students, fellows, and other interdisciplinary trainees from the Perelman School of Medicine. The successful candidate will contribute to the educational mission through didactic teaching, clinical supervision, and mentorship while fostering excellence in integrated behavioral health. Clinical responsibilities may include serving as the Clinical Director of Psychology and Psychosocial Program Manager for the Center for Fetal Diagnosis and Treatment. The successful candidate will provide comprehensive psychological assessment, consultation, and evidence-based interventions to expectant parents and families experiencing complex fetal diagnoses, fetal interventions, pregnancy loss, and neonatal transitions. Responsibilities include collaboration with a multidisciplinary team of maternal-fetal medicine specialists, pediatric surgeons, nurses, social workers, genetic counselors, and other behavioral health professionals to ensure integrated, family-centered care. The psychologist will oversee psychosocial services within the Center for Fetal Diagnosis and Treatment  (CFDT), supervise psychology staff and trainees, support program development, and participate in quality improvement initiatives to advance psychosocial care across the continuum of fetal therapy. The CFDT at Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP) is an internationally recognized leader in fetal diagnosis, fetal therapy, and multidisciplinary family-centered care. The Clinical Director of Psychology serves as the leader of the Center's psychosocial program, partnering closely with clinical and administrative leadership to ensure the delivery of exceptional behavioral health services for patients and families facing highly complex pregnancies. The psychologist will be a member of the Department of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences (DCAPBS) at CHOP. DCAPBS offers specialized care for individuals and families facing emotional, behavioral, and mental health challenges. The department emphasizes that mental health is health, and aims to provide appropriate diagnoses and personalized treatment. This position offers opportunities to develop innovative psychosocial care models, participate in multidisciplinary clinical and research initiatives, contribute to program growth, and engage in scholarly activities consistent with the Academic Clinician track. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to excellence in clinical care, education, leadership, and collaboration within a highly specialized, nationally recognized fetal therapy program. To learn more about the Academic Clinician track please visit Perelman School of Medicine's Faculty Career Development Page ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192105": {
      "title": "Pulmonary and Critical Care Division, Assistant Professor - Academic Clinician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of pulmonary and critical care. Selected candidates will attend on the inpatients medical critical care service as well as provide services in the outpatient ALD clinical. Additionally, nocturnal service coverage may be required. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Applicants should be board certified or board eligible in Pulmonary and Critical Care. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching pulmonary and critical care fellows, house staff and medical students. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include working with advanced practice providers and/or trainees, may include proficiency in consultation and diagnosis for ongoing treatment of critically ill patients in the ICU unit, rounding on in-patient services for advanced lung disease and participating in a busy out-patient clinical practice at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center and the Michael J. Crescenz VA Medical Center. Preferred candidates would have an interest and experience in education and systems improvement initiatives."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181329": {
      "title": "Pulmonary and Critical Care, Interventional Pulmonologist - Academic Clinician",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of medical care for a diverse patient population with a broad range of advanced thoracic oncology, airway and pleural diseases in outpatient clinics, inpatient consultation services, and medical intensive care unit. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Candidates should be board certified in Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care. Teaching responsibilities may include Teaching pulmonary and critical care fellows, house staff, medical students and advanced practitioners within the Health System. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include proficiency in treating patients with thoracic oncology, complex airways and pleural disorders and in performing advanced diagnostic and therapeutic bronchoscopy and pleural disease procedures. Rounding on inpatient and consultative services and participating in a busy outpatient clinical practice at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. There will be an expectation of the ability of selected candidates to provide management and/or leadership."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/177350": {
      "title": "Pulmonary and Critical Care, Interventional Pulmonologist, Academic Clinician - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Pulmonary, Allergy and Critical Care in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Applicants must have an M.D or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Teaching responsibilities may include teaching pulmonary and critical care fellows, house staff, medical students and advanced practitioners within the Health System. The academic clinician track requires 100 credits per year of active and high-quality teaching. Clinical responsibilities may include proficiency in treating patients with thoracic oncology, complex airways and pleural disorders and in performing advanced diagnostic and therapeutic bronchoscopy and pleural disease procedures. Rounding on inpatient and consultative services and participating in a busy outpatient clinical practice at the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Presbyterian Medical Center, and Pennsylvania Hospital. Preferred candidates will have an interest in thoracic oncology, complex benign airways and pleural disorders, lung cancer screening and biomarker assessment."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192619": {
      "title": "Radiation Oncology Assistant Professor, AC Track [Palliative Service]",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiation Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiation Oncology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of palliative care and strong palliative training. The candidate must have experience with palliative radiation, and it is preferable to have residency or fellowship in a palliative program. Applicants must have an M.D. or equivalent degree. Required certifications include eligibility for American Board of Radiology Certification. Teaching responsibilities may include the teaching, training, and mentoring of radiation oncology and medical physics residents, graduate students, and visiting trainees, etc. Informal and formal teachings include, but are not limited to, participating in resident didactic series, both as a lecturer and as an in-person discussant. Clinical responsibilities may include providing stereotactic body radiotherapy (SBRT), proton therapy, intensity modulated radiation therapy (IMRT), and high dose rate (HDR) brachytherapy as treatment modalities in the care of palliative cancer patients. Penn Radiation Oncology is dedicated to a three-part mission of excellence in patient care, basic and translational research, and the education of residents and students. We are committed to delivering excellence in every area and as such we steadfastly believe that \"Excellence is Standard.\" Penn Radiation Oncology is one of the most comprehensive radiation oncology programs in the world. The outstanding faculty and staff, combined with Penn’s extensive collection of advanced technology, gives patients access to nearly every treatment option available for their cancer. The broad range of radiation treatments available include External-Beam Radiation Therapy (Proton Therapy, Image-guided radiation therapy (IGRT), Intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT), Photodynamic therapy (PDT), Total body irradiation (TBI), Total skin electron beam therapy (TSEBT)), and Stereotactic Radiosurgery (CyberKnife, Edge, Gamma Knife, TrueBeam), as well as Internal Radiation Therapy (brachytherapy, MammoSite). The brachytherapy suite at the Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine is a state-of-the-art, dedicated outpatient facility specializing in high-dose rate (HDR) treatments for prostate, gynecologic, and head/neck cancers. It features advanced in-room imaging, including BK ultrasound and fluoroscopy, and is located next to MRI services for precise 3D treatment planning. With the Abramson Cancer Center of the University of Pennsylvania, Penn Radiation Oncology provides patient care at the Ruth and Raymond Perelman Center for Advanced Medicine and fourteen community-based sites."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168420": {
      "title": "Regional Anesthesiologist - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of regional anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. In addition, completion of fellowship training in regional anesthesiology and acute pain medicine or chronic pain medicine is required. Teaching responsibilities may include the instruction and/or supervision of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the operating rooms and wards of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and the Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC) as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of clinical anesthesia and ultrasound-guided regional anesthesia blocks (including single-shot peripheral nerve blocks, fascial plane blocks, indwelling continuous peripheral nerve and fascial plane catheters, and neuraxial blocks and catheters) at HUP and PPMC. The academic clinician track emphasizes clinical and teaching excellence. Are you interested in this position but are unsure about if it's the right fit? We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Faculty Career Development website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/faculty-career-development/"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/168421": {
      "title": "Regional Anesthesiologist - Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Anesthesiology and Critical Care Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Associate or Full Professor positions in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of regional anesthesiology. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. ABA certification in anesthesiology or status as a candidate in the examination system along with ability to obtain a Pennsylvania license are required. In addition, completion of fellowship training in regional anesthesiology and acute pain medicine or chronic pain medicine is required. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Teaching responsibilities may include the instruction and/or supervision of medical students, residents, and fellows rotating through the operating rooms and wards of the Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania (HUP) and the Penn Presbyterian Medical Center (PPMC) as well as participation in lectures, small groups, workshops, and/or simulation sessions. Clinical responsibilities may include the provision of clinical anesthesia and ultrasound-guided regional anesthesia blocks (including single-shot peripheral nerve blocks, fascial plane blocks, indwelling continuous peripheral nerve and fascial plane catheters, and neuraxial blocks and catheters) at HUP and PPMC. Applicants in mid-career are encouraged to apply. The academic clinician track emphasizes clinical and teaching excellence. Are you interested in this position but are unsure if it's the right fit? We welcome prospective candidates to visit the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania Office of Academic Affairs website to learn more about the different tracks: https://www.med.upenn.edu/oaa/faculty-career-development/"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/169719": {
      "title": "Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility, Assistant Professor of Clinical Ob/Gyn",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Obstetrics and Gynecology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track. Expertise is required in the specific area of reproductive endocrinology and infertility. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Candidates must be board certified or active candidates for certification by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology.  Successful Candidates will be subspecialty trained and board certified or active candidates for certification in REI. Teaching responsibilities may include clinical training and supervision of medical students, residents and fellows and participation in formal teaching curriculum. Clinical responsibilities may include caring for patients with reproductive endocrinology and infertility needs, in vitro fertilization, and reproductive surgery. Candidate would join established REI practice in Philadelphia and the surrounding counties."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193586": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor in Public Mental Health",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of psychiatric epidemiology, mental health services research, and substance use treatment. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include analysis of claims data and electronic health records to describe the experiences and outcomes of people with substance use disorders and/or psychiatric disorder; community-partnered research to improve quality of care and associate outcomes for these populations, using quantitative analytic skills to support other investigators in conducting similar research."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182061": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor of Biostatistics",
      "description": "Posted: Feb 27, 2026 Deadline: Feb 27, 2028 Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology and Informatics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biostatistics and Epidemiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of development and application of biostatistics methods and AI/ML models (particularly, generative AI and agentic AI) for clinical trials and real-world data in oncology. Candidates with postdoctoral training are encouraged to apply. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include conducting research with a standing faculty member involving collaborative research studies, and the development, evaluation, or application of biostatistics methods and AI/ML models for clinical trials and real-world data (e.g., EHR/EMR and registry data). Candidates with experience in these areas are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will be expected to attract and maintain extramural funding. The successful candidate will become a member of the Abramson Cancer Center (ACC)’s Biostatistics and Bioinformatics Core and the Center for Cancer Data Science and is expected to collaborate with ACC members. As such, prior experiences in collaboration in cancer research and analyses of cancer data are strongly preferred. Additional qualifications include: 1) Expertise in statistical and ML programming (R, Python); 2) Demonstrated ability to lead peer-reviewed publications and support multi-site collaborative research projects; 3) Experience in collaborating with biomedical researchers, particularly physician-scientists; 4) Demonstrated aptitude working with state-of-the-art computing infrastructure, Overleaf/LaTeX, GitHub, and supporting reproducible research pipelines; and 5) Strong communication skills. The University of Pennsylvania is a vibrant team-science-oriented environment with elite biomedical research collaborators that is ideal for biostatistical collaboration and application-driven methodological research. The Division of Biostatistics includes over 30 full-time faculty with diverse expertise spanning numerous methodological and biomedical areas, and we have strong, highly ranked, and growing MS and PhD programs in which we train the next generation of innovative quantitative leaders. The placement of Biostatistics in the Perelman School of Medicine with world-class medical, biological, and population scientists, as part of an integrated campus including the Wharton School of Business, School of Arts and Sciences, and the School of Engineering and Applied Science and other premier biomedical research institutions including the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia provides the ideal setting for cross-disciplinary collaboration and impactful quantitative research."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193761": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor of Epidemiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology and Informatics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology, and Informatics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of causal inference and machine learning methods. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include expertise in statistical programming (R, Python, SAS) and proficiency in analyzing and interpreting health outcomes, along with a demonstrated aptitude for working with state-of-the-art computing infrastructure, Overleaf/LaTeX, GitHub, and reproducible research pipelines. The successful candidate will bring a demonstrated record of first- or senior-authored peer-reviewed publications in statistical methodology, causal inference, biostatistics, epidemiology, or related fields, as well as experience developing and evaluating novel statistical methods for observational and experimental data. The candidate should demonstrate the ability to lead peer-reviewed publications in causal inference methodology applied to perinatal health and support multi-site collaborative research projects, while effectively communicating complex quantitative methods to interdisciplinary scientific audiences. Additionally, experience in collaborating with clinician-scientists, mentoring graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, or junior investigators, and contributing to federal and foundation grant submissions (e.g., NIH, PCORI, foundations) is highly valued. The Center for Causal Inference (CCI) and the Center for Health Innovations in Reproductive and Perinatal Population Research (CHIRP) in the Division of Epidemiology, Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology, and Informatics seeks candidates with a PhD in Biostatistics, Statistics, Epidemiologic Methods, or a closely related quantitative field, with 1+ years of postdoctoral experience. The ideal candidates will be outstanding early-career researchers who will advance innovative causal inference methodologies and lead cutting-edge research in the development of novel causal inference and machine learning methods. This faculty member will be expected to lead and publish high-impact research in top-tier biostatistics, epidemiology, and clinical research journals; support, prepare, and submit grant applications; and support ongoing research studies with Penn faculty and external partners. We will begin reviewing applications on November 15th, 2026, and the position start date is flexible."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194585": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor of Informatics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology and Informatics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology and Informatics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of biomedical informatics methods development and applications. Candidates with postdoctoral training are encouraged to apply. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include conducting research with a standing faculty member involving collaborative research studies, and the development, evaluation, or application of biomedical informatics methods. Candidates with experience in NLP, AI and Machine Learning, bioinformatics, translational bioinformatics, clinical informatics, clinical research informatics, consumer health informatics, and/or public health informatics are encouraged to apply. Research track faculty typically work on extramurally-funded research within a research group led by a standing faculty member. The successful candidate will be expected to attract and maintain extramural funding. They should have experience conducting research and publishing peer reviewed manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/159786": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor of Medicine Faculty Position, Division of Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Endocrinology, Diabetes and Metabolism in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of transcriptional regulation, including genomic architecture, and circadian biology, specifically in the fields of chromatin and transcription with emphasis on genome-wide approaches in diabetes and obesity models, preferably in circadian models. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include generating and characterizing novel reagents for gene expression, mouse models of regulators of circadian physiology, and analyzing large next generation sequencing datasets. Applicants will have demonstrated excellent qualifications in research including a track record of publication in the areas of transcriptional regulation, including genomic architecture, and circadian biology. The successful candidate must have the ability to obtain and maintain extramural funding. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania is an EOE. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176419": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor of Neuroscience",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neuroscience Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neuroscience at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of state-of-the-art recording and manipulation techniques, including high-density electrophysiology, optogenetics, and computational analysis of neural data and proficiency with behavioral learning paradigms. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include the development of an independent research program focused on the circuit-level mechanisms underlying sleep regulation in the mammalian brain. Candidates should have a distinguished record of scholarship, evidenced by publications on in vivo electrophysiology and on the neural control and function of sleep. The successful candidate will be expected to attract and maintain extramural funding. Teaching responsibilities may include training of graduate students and post-doctoral investigators."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161096": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor, CHOP Neurology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA Children's Hospital of Philadelphia and the Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seek candidates for several Assistant Professor positions in the non-tenure research track. Expertise is required in the specific area of oligodendrocyte biology and myelination with knowledge of lysosomal and cytoskeletal functions. The successful candidate will have experience in methods including primary cell culture of oligodendrocytes, imaging and analysis of oligodendrocyte in vitro and in vivo using fluorescence, confocal, live cell microscopy, knowledge of cellular organellar structure, function, and interactions to study the generation of the myelin sheath and regeneration in the context of developmental and neurodegenerative diseases and injury. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Research or scholarship responsibilities may include developing collaborative and independent research programs related to myelination and the relationship between glial cells in the nervous system. The candidate may supervise postdoctoral fellows, students, and research staff coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators. The candidate may participate in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts. Consistently ranked a world leader in patient care, education, and research, the Division of Neurology at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia boasts robust research programs investigating a variety of genetic and acquired neurologic conditions. Our research is diverse but centered on identifying and understanding the mechanisms of neurological diseases that affect children and adolescents to design appropriate treatments. Integrated research programs partner with the Division of Child Neurology with basic neuroscientists, developmental pediatrics, metabolic medicine, psychiatry, cardiology, critical pediatric and neonatal medicine, and adult neurology across Children’s Hospital and the University of Pennsylvania. We seek candidates who embrace and reflect diversity in the broadest sense. The University of Pennsylvania and Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia are EOEs. Minorities/women/individuals with disabilities/protected veterans are encouraged to apply."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192452": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Psychiatry Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Psychiatry at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of Drosophila neurogenetics and behavioral neuroscience, with demonstrated experience in quantitative sleep and behavioral analysis, genetic manipulation of defined neuronal populations, and experimental investigation of sensory and neural function. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Responsibilities may include conducting research investigating the neural and molecular mechanisms underlying interactions between sensory processing and sleep using Drosophila models of neurodevelopmental disorders. Responsibilities will include experimental design and execution, Drosophila genetics and behavioral studies, analysis and interpretation of data, preparation of manuscripts and presentations, and supervision and mentoring of junior laboratory members. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to lead ongoing and new studies examining how sensory processing, neural function, and internal state interact to regulate sleep, develop and apply genetic and imaging approaches to investigate underlying mechanisms, contribute to manuscripts and grant applications, and mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers. Applicants should have a Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree in neuroscience, biology, or a related field and substantial research experience using Drosophila to investigate neural mechanisms of behavior. Experience with sleep and/or sensory neuroscience, fluorescence imaging, molecular approaches, quantitative data analysis, scientific writing, and mentoring is preferred."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184434": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Biochemistry and Biophysics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biochemistry and Biophysics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of protein structure-function relationships with a focus on metalloenzyme mechanisms. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Responsibilities may include independently designing and carrying out research by performing biochemical activity and kinetic measurements, and analyzing enzyme structure using commonly used laboratory and spectroscopic methods. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to collaborate with other colleagues and participate in challenging research projects in the lab, attend research conferences, publish his/her work on scientific journals."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/166684": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Biochemistry and Biophysics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biochemistry and Biophysics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of Mass Spectrometry. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include developing collaborative and independent research programs related to the intersection of chromatin biology and proteomics. Learn, apply, and contribute to the development of cutting-edge mass spectrometry-based methods for the quantitative analysis of nuclear proteins and histone post-translational modifications, along with a variety of biochemical, cellular, and molecular biology approaches. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to Co-supervision of postdoctoral fellows, students, and research staff, coordinating NIH-funded grant efforts with local, national, and international collaborators, and participation in writing grants, reports, and manuscripts."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185717": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Biochemistry and Biophysics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biochemistry and Biophysics at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include conducting research in the molecular functions and biological roles of the novel chimeric fusion product of TOMM40 and APOE, the two highest risk genes for Alzheimer’s disease, aging-related cognitive decline and life expectancy in humans. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to collaborate with other colleagues and participate in challenging research projects in the lab, attend research conferences, publish his/her work on scientific journals."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185624": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Radiation Oncology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Radiation Oncology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of Tumor biology, preferably in radiation biology/oncology is required. Work with rodents is also required. Experience with growing of tissue organoids, and performing complex immunohistochemical and immunofluorescence analyses on fixed/embedded tissue is strongly recommended. Experience inscRNAseq analysis is a plus. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Small animal training certification is required. Responsibilities may include engagement in research investigating the role of Ultra-High-Dose Rate (\"FLASH\") radiotherapy in normal and tumor response in head and neck cancer models. Specifically, the role will be engaged in injecting HNSCC cells (both HPV+ and HPV-) in the oral cavity of syngeneic mice, and irradiating them with Proton FLASH or Standard radiation. The impact of these treatments on tumor growth as well as normal tissue toxicity (fibrosis, hyposalivation, atrophy of salivary glands etc) will be assayed. Furthermore, normal tissue and tumor organoids will be developed from mouse models as well as patients with HNSCC-these organoids will be used to determine the impact of FLASH RT +/- DNA damage repair inhibitors on the therapeutic window. The successful candidate is also expected to perform analyses such as scRNAseq and bioinformatics and perform mechanistic studies pertaining to the role of Ferroptosis in normal and tumor tissue response to these treatments. Finally, the RA will be expected to write first drafts of manuscripts and apply for funding form several Institutions and foundations, including the NIH, ACS and AACR. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to be trained in cutitng edge research on FLASH and HNSCC biology, publish in high-impact journals and receive mentoring in career transition toindependence through grant writing workshops, attending and presenting their research findings at national and international meetings."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183374": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Neurology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Neurology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Research Associate positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include developing and implementing signal processing pipelines, visualization strategies for complex data, statistical analyses, and writing scientific papers. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to help supervise laboratory technicians, postdoctoral fellows, and graduate students in an academic setting."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191203": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Berger Lab)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Cell and Developmental Biology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Cell and Developmental Biology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of neuronal and iPSC cell culture, molecular biology, chromatin biology, genomics, and imaging studies. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include investigation of the regulation and functions of nuclear speckles and chromatin organization during neuronal stimulation, using a wide range of approaches including molecular biology, cell biology, genomics approaches, and imaging studies. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to further develop and prepare manuscripts and grants, present research findings in a national meeting, mentor junior scientists, and participate in career trainings offered by the University. Candidate should have a minimum of 3-5 years postdoctoral experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/180877": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Wan Lab)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Cancer Biology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Cancer Biology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of protein biochemistry, cell culture techniques, molecular biology, imaging, epigenetics and chromatin biology, and animal models of development and cancer. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include investigation of epigenetic mechanisms in development and cancer, using a wide range of approaches including molecular biology, biochemistry, cell biology, epigenomic analysis, and animal models. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to further develop critical thinking skills, get familiarized with related literatures and experimental techniques, participate in manuscript and grant preparation, present research findings in national and international meetings, mentor junior scientists, and participate in career trainings offered by the University. Candidate should have a minimum of 3-5 years postdoctoral experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181514": {
      "title": "Research Associate - CBIO (Witze)",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Cancer Biology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Cancer Biology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of protein biochemistry, cell culture techniques, molecular biology and animal models of cancer. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include investigation of the role of protein palmitoylation in the regulation of autophagy in cancer. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to further develop critical skills in studying cellular processes in cancer using biochemical and cell biological approaches."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183210": {
      "title": "Research Associate - Informatics",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Biostatistics, Epidemiology and Informatics Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Biostatistics and Epidemiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Responsibilities may include : (1) development and application of informatics and machine learning methods for analyzing genomics, imaging, biomarker and other biomedical and healthcare data; and (2) collaboration on cutting-edge biomedical data science research with researchers in Perelman School of Medicine and other Schools at Penn. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to work under the supervision of an Informatics PI, with a focus on methodological developments and biomedical applications. The candidate is expected to establish a clear trajectory towards an independent researcher in preparation for the next stage of their career."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195598": {
      "title": "Research Associate - Kidney and Cardiovascular - Metabolic Disease Research",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Department of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Medicine - Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension Location: Philadelphia, PA The Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of molecular and cellular biology, kidney disease research, cardiovascular-metabolic disease research, human genetics, genomics, or a closely related biomedical research field. Candidates should have demonstrated experience in experimental design, advanced molecular biology techniques, genetically modified animal models, and computational analysis and interpretation of complex biomedical datasets. Experience with single-cell or single-nucleus RNA sequencing, spatial transcriptomics, multi-omics data integration, gene expression analysis, primary cell culture, and functional validation studies is highly desirable. Research experience involving diabetic kidney disease, kidney injury and fibrosis, cardiovascular disease mechanisms, or metabolic disorders is preferred. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. or equivalent degree. Responsibilities may include designing and conducting biomedical research focused on the molecular and cellular mechanisms underlying kidney and cardiovascular-metabolic diseases, with an emphasis on diabetic kidney disease and therapeutic responses to SGLT2 inhibitors. Responsibilities will include designing and performing molecular and cellular experiments; utilizing genetically modified mouse models to investigate disease mechanisms; performing advanced molecular biology techniques, including gene expression analysis, plasmid construction, and primary cell isolation and culture; conducting computational analyses of human genetic, single-cell, single-nucleus RNA sequencing, and high-resolution spatial transcriptomic datasets; integrating multi-omics data to identify disease-associated cellular states, molecular pathways, and therapeutic responses; conducting functional validation studies; interpreting experimental findings; and collaborating with multidisciplinary research teams and external research facilities. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to advance their expertise in kidney and cardiovascular-metabolic disease research within a highly collaborative academic research environment at the University of Pennsylvania. The successful applicant will have opportunities to independently design and lead multidisciplinary biomedical research projects investigating diabetic kidney disease and therapeutic responses to SGLT2 inhibitors; integrate human genetics, single-cell and spatial transcriptomics, and spatial metabolomics with experimental disease models; conduct advanced molecular and cellular studies; collaborate with investigators and specialized research facilities; and contribute to scientific discoveries that improve our understanding of kidney injury, disease progression, and therapeutic mechanisms. The successful candidate will join the Division of Renal-Electrolyte and Hypertension in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania and participate in a collaborative biomedical research program focused on understanding the molecular and cellular mechanisms underlying kidney and cardiovascular-metabolic diseases. The research program integrates human genetics, genomics, advanced molecular and cellular biology, genetically modified animal models, and computational approaches to investigate disease mechanisms and therapeutic responses. Current research initiatives include investigations of diabetic kidney disease and the therapeutic effects of SGLT2 inhibitors, incorporating single-cell and spatial transcriptomics, multi-omics analysis, and spatial metabolomics. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with investigators and multidisciplinary research teams to advance ongoing research initiatives within the Division."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176683": {
      "title": "Research Associate - Microbiology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Microbiology Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Microbiology at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for a Research Associate position in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Expertise is required in the specific area of mRNA biochemistry, mRNA production, immunology (evaluate vaccine-induced cellular and humarol immune responses) and work with mice. Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include investigation of novel adjuvants for mRNA vaccines in various mouse models. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to further develop critical research skills, literature and experimental techniques, prepare manuscripts, present findings at national and international meetings. Candidate should have a minimum of 3-5 years of postdoctoral experience."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183796": {
      "title": "Research Associate - Otorhinolaryngology",
      "description": "Department: University of Pennsylvania: Perelman School of Medicine: Perelman School of Medicine - Otorhinolaryngology - Head and Neck Surgery Location: Philadelphia, PA The Department of Otorhinolaryngology: Head and Neck Surgery at the Perelman School of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania seeks candidates for several Research Associate positions in the Academic Support Staff. This appointment will be initially for one (1) year and continuation during that time period and renewal are based on satisfactory performance and availability of funding (limited to three (3) years). Applicants must have an M.D. or Ph.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree. Responsibilities may include scientific research in the field of Otorhinolaryngology with a focus on aiding in the preparation of scientific papers, grants writing and grants proposals. The successful applicant will have an opportunity to develop independence in research through writing grants and peer-reviewed publications."
